        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Renovation and addition  of statues"@en ;
    dcterms:description "In 2005 CE (NS 1125), the temple underwent major renovation under the Lalitpur Sub-Metropolitan City. During this process, replicas of Lakṣmī and Sarasvatī were installed to replace the stolen originals, a task initiated in the 1970s by local residents Hirabahadur Bajrācārya and Candralakṣmī Pradhāna (local resident, Maharjana, male, age 64)."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/008d3c7c-7cde-4a0b-b917-9124111b7552> ;
