<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/00ebce6c-2bba-44ee-aed0-4e1e40fa9b42_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Construction of the temple"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Ratnarāma Bhāro and his wife Caṃpāvatī Mayī, residents of Sikochẽ, Cāpāgāũ, established the Lakṣmīnārāyaṇa statue and constructed this temple in front of their home in 1681 CE (NS 801). They also installed statues of Hariśaṅkara to the right of Lakṣmīnārāyaṇa and Bhavānīśaṅkara to the left, following a day-and-night fire oblation. The donor couple donated 12ropanis of land to sustain the temple's operations. They specified that donations should be made during the annual Vajrabārāhī procession in Caitra and theYẽnyāḥ(IndraJātrā) festival. Lamps were to be lit during these events, as well as throughout the month of Kārtika. Additionally, lamps were to be lit on the first day of the bright fortnight of Bhādra at the temple of Buṅgadyaḥ and during the second annual Vajrabārāhī procession in Kārtika. A ritual offering (dakṣiṇā) of onepaisāwas required on the first day of each solar month. Fruits were also to be displayed at the temple during theYẽnyāḥfestival."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/00ebce6c-2bba-44ee-aed0-4e1e40fa9b42> ;
    rdfs:comment "Ratnarāma Bhāro and his wife Caṃpāvatī Mayī, residents of Sikochẽ, Cāpāgāũ, established the Lakṣmīnārāyaṇa statue and constructed this temple in front of their home in 1681 CE (NS 801). They also installed statues of Hariśaṅkara to the right of Lakṣmīnārāyaṇa and Bhavānīśaṅkara to the left, following a day-and-night fire oblation. The donor couple donated 12ropanis of land to sustain the temple's operations. They specified that donations should be made during the annual Vajrabārāhī procession in Caitra and theYẽnyāḥ(IndraJātrā) festival. Lamps were to be lit during these events, as well as throughout the month of Kārtika. Additionally, lamps were to be lit on the first day of the bright fortnight of Bhādra at the temple of Buṅgadyaḥ and during the second annual Vajrabārāhī procession in Kārtika. A ritual offering (dakṣiṇā) of onepaisāwas required on the first day of each solar month. Fruits were also to be displayed at the temple during theYẽnyāḥfestival."@en ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/agent/antigravity_agent> ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/activity/heritagegraph_kg_construction> ;
