<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/0228287b-e064-4332-9f1e-cd0042f3542f_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:TransferOfCustody ;
    rdfs:label "Initial construction of the Temple and land endowment for its operation and maintenances"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The inscription recording the construction of this Temple is posted on the rear wall of the adjoiningphalcā. It states that Cuku (?) Bhāju Pradhānāṅga, Yajñanārāyaṇa, along with other donors had constructed the Temple during the reign of King Raṇajita Malla in 1734 CE (NS 854). They had formed aguthiby donating fiveropanīs of land to carry out the daily rituals and timely renovations."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/0228287b-e064-4332-9f1e-cd0042f3542f> ;
    rdfs:comment "The inscription recording the construction of this Temple is posted on the rear wall of the adjoiningphalcā. It states that Cuku (?) Bhāju Pradhānāṅga, Yajñanārāyaṇa, along with other donors had constructed the Temple during the reign of King Raṇajita Malla in 1734 CE (NS 854). They had formed aguthiby donating fiveropanīs of land to carry out the daily rituals and timely renovations."@en ;
