<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/0232aa9c-821a-4872-ad21-af13cac95b0b_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Construction of defensive walls, etc."@en ;
    dcterms:description "Yakṣa Malla fortified the city of Bhaktapur with defensive walls, gatehouse bastions, and protective moats. Following their construction, the annual repair and maintenance of these structures was delegated to local residents and fortress officials in each respective area. Historical accounts emphasize that members of all four castes contributed significantly to this collective endeavor. This inscription holds particular historical significance as it documents both the Malla kingdom's defensive strategies and the active participation of local communities in safeguarding their city. It stands as an important record of civic-military cooperation during this period."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/0232aa9c-821a-4872-ad21-af13cac95b0b> ;
    rdfs:comment "Yakṣa Malla fortified the city of Bhaktapur with defensive walls, gatehouse bastions, and protective moats. Following their construction, the annual repair and maintenance of these structures was delegated to local residents and fortress officials in each respective area. Historical accounts emphasize that members of all four castes contributed significantly to this collective endeavor. This inscription holds particular historical significance as it documents both the Malla kingdom's defensive strategies and the active participation of local communities in safeguarding their city. It stands as an important record of civic-military cooperation during this period."@en ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/agent/antigravity_agent> ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/activity/heritagegraph_kg_construction> ;
    hg:eventIndex 0 ;
    hg:extractionMethod "source_table" ;
    hg:isEventOf <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/0232aa9c-821a-4872-ad21-af13cac95b0b> .

<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/0232aa9c-821a-4872-ad21-af13cac95b0b_1> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Beatification of Golden Gate"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Raṇajita Malla and his wife Jayalakṣmī conducted a grand fire ritual of 10 million oblations (koṭyāhuti yajña) for their tutelary deity, culminating in the donation of a goldentoraṇa, decorative panels, finials, and roof elements to the Golden Gate. The specific mention of gilded additions rather than full construction suggests this project likely involved the renovation and embellishment of an existing gate rather than building an entirely new structure. The gate features dual inscriptions - one in Sanskrit and another in Newar - flanking its entrance. The present inscription under discussion is the Sanskrit version."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/0232aa9c-821a-4872-ad21-af13cac95b0b> ;
    rdfs:comment "Raṇajita Malla and his wife Jayalakṣmī conducted a grand fire ritual of 10 million oblations (koṭyāhuti yajña) for their tutelary deity, culminating in the donation of a goldentoraṇa, decorative panels, finials, and roof elements to the Golden Gate. The specific mention of gilded additions rather than full construction suggests this project likely involved the renovation and embellishment of an existing gate rather than building an entirely new structure. The gate features dual inscriptions - one in Sanskrit and another in Newar - flanking its entrance. The present inscription under discussion is the Sanskrit version."@en ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/agent/antigravity_agent> ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/activity/heritagegraph_kg_construction> ;
