<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/0232aa9c-821a-4872-ad21-af13cac95b0b_2> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Beatification of Golden Gate"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Raṇajita Malla and his wife Jayalakṣmī conducted a grand fire ritual of 10 million oblations (koṭyāhuti yajña) for their tutelary deity, culminating in the donation of a goldentoraṇa, decorative panels, finials, and roof elements to the Golden Gate. The specific mention of gilded additions rather than full construction suggests this project likely involved the renovation and embellishment of an existing gate rather than building an entirely new structure. The gate features dual inscriptions - one in Sanskrit and another in Newar - flanking its entrance. The present inscription under discussion is the Newar version."@en ;
