<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/0232aa9c-821a-4872-ad21-af13cac95b0b_3> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Offering of jewelry"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The principal artisans involved in the construction of the Golden Gate were Sabhākara, Karaṇākara, and Ratikara, who performed monthly worship of Mañjuśrī throughout the construction period. Upon completion, they presented ahelepho(a type of metal ornament) to Mañjuśrī as an offering to mark the project's successful conclusion. Interestingly, King Raṇajita Malla also gifted an ornament of identical name and form to Mañjuśrī. Both offerings bear the same inscription date: the 10th of the bright fortnight of Kārtika, NS 875 (1754 CE)."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/0232aa9c-821a-4872-ad21-af13cac95b0b> ;
    rdfs:comment "The principal artisans involved in the construction of the Golden Gate were Sabhākara, Karaṇākara, and Ratikara, who performed monthly worship of Mañjuśrī throughout the construction period. Upon completion, they presented ahelepho(a type of metal ornament) to Mañjuśrī as an offering to mark the project's successful conclusion. Interestingly, King Raṇajita Malla also gifted an ornament of identical name and form to Mañjuśrī. Both offerings bear the same inscription date: the 10th of the bright fortnight of Kārtika, NS 875 (1754 CE)."@en ;
