<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/0274d17a-ceb6-4480-bcbd-8d893d078724_4> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Unclear event"@en ;
    dcterms:description "On either side of the western entrance of the temple are four stone slabs bearing inscriptions. One of these is carved on the same pale-yellow stone used in the temple’s construction, suggesting that it dates back to the temple’s original building phase. However, due to lime plastering and erosion, the text is difficult to read, and the date is no longer visible. The inscription lists ritual duties to be performed at the temple and names the responsible individuals. Some Nevārī and Sanskrit words can be read."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/0274d17a-ceb6-4480-bcbd-8d893d078724> ;
    rdfs:comment "On either side of the western entrance of the temple are four stone slabs bearing inscriptions. One of these is carved on the same pale-yellow stone used in the temple’s construction, suggesting that it dates back to the temple’s original building phase. However, due to lime plastering and erosion, the text is difficult to read, and the date is no longer visible. The inscription lists ritual duties to be performed at the temple and names the responsible individuals. Some Nevārī and Sanskrit words can be read."@en ;
