<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/02da1b3e-8f31-4000-ad9f-d5b5f6b4c2e3_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Addition of an aniconic stone (?)"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The inscription dated to 1710 CE (NS 831) carved on the aniconic stone identified with Indrāyaṇī indicates that the stone was established in that very year. It remains uncertain, however, whether the stone was installed at an already venerated site of Indrāyaṇī or whether thepīṭhaoriginated at this time. Although the date is legible, other portions of the short inscription are fragmentary, rendering the context unclear."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/02da1b3e-8f31-4000-ad9f-d5b5f6b4c2e3> ;
    rdfs:comment "The inscription dated to 1710 CE (NS 831) carved on the aniconic stone identified with Indrāyaṇī indicates that the stone was established in that very year. It remains uncertain, however, whether the stone was installed at an already venerated site of Indrāyaṇī or whether thepīṭhaoriginated at this time. Although the date is legible, other portions of the short inscription are fragmentary, rendering the context unclear."@en ;
