<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/02da1b3e-8f31-4000-ad9f-d5b5f6b4c2e3_1> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Reconstruction of a phalcā"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The historicalphalcā(public rest platform) located to the south of thepīṭha—previously renovated by thrice venerable great queen Kṛṣṇakumārī—had deteriorated and was therefore reconstructed as a cement structure under local supervision. At that time, ritual observances were also formally prescribed for the occasions of Śivarātri, Navarātri, Maṅgal Cauthī, and Bālācaturdaśī."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/02da1b3e-8f31-4000-ad9f-d5b5f6b4c2e3> ;
    rdfs:comment "The historicalphalcā(public rest platform) located to the south of thepīṭha—previously renovated by thrice venerable great queen Kṛṣṇakumārī—had deteriorated and was therefore reconstructed as a cement structure under local supervision. At that time, ritual observances were also formally prescribed for the occasions of Śivarātri, Navarātri, Maṅgal Cauthī, and Bālācaturdaśī."@en ;
