<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/0316e917-5197-44e7-b865-37ba1be3397b_2> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Consecration ;
    rdfs:label "Initial construction"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Previously, only the abstract stone known as Hāsadyaḥ existed at this site. The then ward chairman of Ward No. 2 of Tokha Municipality took a vow to construct a temple over the stone and built the new temple in 2024 CE (VS 2080). On the ninth day of Caitra of that year, consecration ceremony was performed in the newly constructed temple."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/0316e917-5197-44e7-b865-37ba1be3397b> ;
    rdfs:comment "Previously, only the abstract stone known as Hāsadyaḥ existed at this site. The then ward chairman of Ward No. 2 of Tokha Municipality took a vow to construct a temple over the stone and built the new temple in 2024 CE (VS 2080). On the ninth day of Caitra of that year, consecration ceremony was performed in the newly constructed temple."@en ;
