<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/03774891-215f-450c-b5b6-b72271507e2d_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Issue of royal decree"@en ;
    dcterms:description "King Lakṣmīnarasiṃha Malla himself, issuing a royal decree, installed the inscription, warns that killing is prohibited within the land west of the Svayambhū Caitya, north of the Agnihotra brahmin, east of the wide road, and south of the “old area,” and anyone who does so will incur the sin equivalent to killing Mahādeva. Brahmins, Pradhānas, Khasa, Magaras, andpañcas (local council of five or more members) are kept as witnesses in the royal decree. This inscription is considered the earliest inscription in the Nepali language found in the Kathmandu valley."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/03774891-215f-450c-b5b6-b72271507e2d> ;
    rdfs:comment "King Lakṣmīnarasiṃha Malla himself, issuing a royal decree, installed the inscription, warns that killing is prohibited within the land west of the Svayambhū Caitya, north of the Agnihotra brahmin, east of the wide road, and south of the “old area,” and anyone who does so will incur the sin equivalent to killing Mahādeva. Brahmins, Pradhānas, Khasa, Magaras, andpañcas (local council of five or more members) are kept as witnesses in the royal decree. This inscription is considered the earliest inscription in the Nepali language found in the Kathmandu valley."@en ;
