<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/04e62546-0b04-41d7-9651-12189c45e5c6_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Renovation of the Digi (A)"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The Saṅkaṭā Ilānani was renovated with financial support (totalling 13,000 rupees) offered by thesaṅghamembers, some Brahmins, the Ṭhakurī Kings, Daivajñas and Dhaṃgūs. These funds also allowed a large metal statue of Saṅkatā to be established on the Ilānani's ground floor. The statue is a replica of the smaller one kept in a secret space dedicated to Cakrasamvara. It was designed by Bahādura Vajrācārya of Aki Bāhāḥ. Local women donated the metals which were used for its construction."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/04e62546-0b04-41d7-9651-12189c45e5c6> ;
    rdfs:comment "The Saṅkaṭā Ilānani was renovated with financial support (totalling 13,000 rupees) offered by thesaṅghamembers, some Brahmins, the Ṭhakurī Kings, Daivajñas and Dhaṃgūs. These funds also allowed a large metal statue of Saṅkatā to be established on the Ilānani's ground floor. The statue is a replica of the smaller one kept in a secret space dedicated to Cakrasamvara. It was designed by Bahādura Vajrācārya of Aki Bāhāḥ. Local women donated the metals which were used for its construction."@en ;
