<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/051a3dc8-3787-4227-b269-4014a16805fe_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Construction of wall, offering toraṇa and a pinnacle"@en ;
    dcterms:description "During the reign of King Pārthivendra Malla, two brothers Śivakalyāṇa (text: Śivakaryāna) and Nvamisiṃha built walls and installed a door at thedyaḥchẽwhile also offering an ornamented arch (toraṇa). They also offered a stone throne and a finial in the name of the Ajimā. Moreover, they established their statues at thedyaḥchẽ."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/051a3dc8-3787-4227-b269-4014a16805fe> ;
