<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/06151b6a-47c6-46a3-bf29-518691623cb5_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:TransferOfCustody ;
    rdfs:label "Initial construction of the monument"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Rāṇā Prime Minister Jaṅga Bahādura's queen from Gorakhpur built this temple and donated a vast tract of land as a religious endowment. A detailed account of the land allocated by the Gorakhpur queen for daily worship, annual rituals, cleaning, regular music, and temple maintenance is inscribed on the large stone slab installed in the south wing of thesataḥ. The temple was built six years after Jaṅga Bahādura's death. The queen had made arrangements for daily, periodic, and anniversary rituals, and even provided for the musicians and workers by allocating specific crops."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/06151b6a-47c6-46a3-bf29-518691623cb5> ;
    rdfs:comment "Rāṇā Prime Minister Jaṅga Bahādura's queen from Gorakhpur built this temple and donated a vast tract of land as a religious endowment. A detailed account of the land allocated by the Gorakhpur queen for daily worship, annual rituals, cleaning, regular music, and temple maintenance is inscribed on the large stone slab installed in the south wing of thesataḥ. The temple was built six years after Jaṅga Bahādura's death. The queen had made arrangements for daily, periodic, and anniversary rituals, and even provided for the musicians and workers by allocating specific crops."@en ;
