<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/0687a32c-e7e8-11e9-8bc4-0242ac130002_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Fixing of doors"@en ;
    dcterms:description "All bays of the phalcā were closed. The Ṭola Sudhārā Samiti installed doors on the eastern and northern sides, allegedly to prevent the monument being used by homeless persons. In a photo published inPruscha(1975, vol. 2, p. 181, P-186), the Phalcā can be seen in the rightr corner without doors and closed bays."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/0687a32c-e7e8-11e9-8bc4-0242ac130002> ;
    rdfs:comment "All bays of the phalcā were closed. The Ṭola Sudhārā Samiti installed doors on the eastern and northern sides, allegedly to prevent the monument being used by homeless persons. In a photo published inPruscha(1975, vol. 2, p. 181, P-186), the Phalcā can be seen in the rightr corner without doors and closed bays."@en ;
