<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/06d2c415-2c7e-4d6f-9617-2b1eb6ab8c4a_1> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Consecration ;
    rdfs:label "Construction of the Taleju Temple"@en ;
    dcterms:description "This event is not related to the Bhīmasena Temple. On the bottom part of the copperplate inscription, which records the consecration of the Bhīmasena Statue, it is mentioned that King Mahendra Malla constructed theTao Devala(the Taleju Mandira) in 1564 CE (NS 660).The copperplate inscription only mentions NS 684 Mārgaśīrṣa. The date mentioned on a record that details themandira’s construction, also mentions tenth day of the dark fortnight in Mārgaśīrṣa on NS 684 (Vajrācārya G.2033, 116)."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/06d2c415-2c7e-4d6f-9617-2b1eb6ab8c4a> ;
    rdfs:comment "This event is not related to the Bhīmasena Temple. On the bottom part of the copperplate inscription, which records the consecration of the Bhīmasena Statue, it is mentioned that King Mahendra Malla constructed theTao Devala(the Taleju Mandira) in 1564 CE (NS 660).The copperplate inscription only mentions NS 684 Mārgaśīrṣa. The date mentioned on a record that details themandira’s construction, also mentions tenth day of the dark fortnight in Mārgaśīrṣa on NS 684 (Vajrācārya G.2033, 116)."@en ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/agent/antigravity_agent> ;
