    dcterms:description "During the reign of King Rājendra Vikrama Śāha, Tulādhara Rāvata and Mānandhara Jaganārāyaṇa (Jagannārāyaṇa), residents of Maru Ṭola, offered the lion pillar including a gold-plated lion statue resting atop of it. They also offered thepatāḥto the deity."@en ;
