        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Erecting a pillar (dharmastabha)"@en ;
    dcterms:description "During the reign of Prime Minister Mohana Śamśera, a person named Komala Prasāda Gautama got a stone pillar erected south of the Ādinārāyaṇa Temple. Devotional songs were performed throughout the night on that occasion, along with offering food to Brahmins and grains to the poor."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/0826415c-dd5f-4666-aa9e-7ecbb32bfd60> ;
