<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/083ed396-3cc8-41ae-af0f-c4df103305ed_4> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Rebuilt of the monument"@en ;
    dcterms:description "A photo taken soon after the 1934 earthquake shows Dharaharā’s lower four stories intact. However, the inscription installed by Juddha Śamśera after the renovation of Dharaharā in 1936 CE (VS 1992) states that ‘only two stories had remained intact after the earthquake and the upper floors were raised during the renovation’ (Tevārī and others VS 2019, p.8-9). Probably, the upper two of the four floors that remained intact were not in good condition and were dismantled before the renovation."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/083ed396-3cc8-41ae-af0f-c4df103305ed> ;
    rdfs:comment "A photo taken soon after the 1934 earthquake shows Dharaharā’s lower four stories intact. However, the inscription installed by Juddha Śamśera after the renovation of Dharaharā in 1936 CE (VS 1992) states that ‘only two stories had remained intact after the earthquake and the upper floors were raised during the renovation’ (Tevārī and others VS 2019, p.8-9). Probably, the upper two of the four floors that remained intact were not in good condition and were dismantled before the renovation."@en ;
