<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/08cdc69e-3e61-4192-8757-255b7b931fdd_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Instructions for maintaining the pond, Nāgapokharī"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The inscription is not related to the temple itself but is associated with the adjacent Nāgapokharī. This inscription outlines the annual obligation to clean the Nāgapokharī on the 1st day of dark fortnight of Śrāvaṇa. Oversight of this task is assigned to the localpramāṇa(official), and households situated along the northern water channel are responsible for its upkeep. Failure to comply results in a fine of twodamma, imposed as royal penalty by thepramāṇa. Furthermore, buffaloes are explicitly prohibited from entering or bathing in the pond."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/08cdc69e-3e61-4192-8757-255b7b931fdd> ;
    rdfs:comment "The inscription is not related to the temple itself but is associated with the adjacent Nāgapokharī. This inscription outlines the annual obligation to clean the Nāgapokharī on the 1st day of dark fortnight of Śrāvaṇa. Oversight of this task is assigned to the localpramāṇa(official), and households situated along the northern water channel are responsible for its upkeep. Failure to comply results in a fine of twodamma, imposed as royal penalty by thepramāṇa. Furthermore, buffaloes are explicitly prohibited from entering or bathing in the pond."@en ;
