<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/0a006229-7e08-4cb2-9883-1527f615bbfb_12> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Completion of roofing on topmost tier and performance of propitiatory rituals"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The topmost roof tier was completely tiled with traditional materials. Supplies for raising the ceremonial banner (betālipatāḥ) atop the finial were sent from the Nhaygāṃ (literally, \"seven villages\") cluster east of Bhaktapur. Following the completion of the top tier's roofing, special propitiatory rituals (śānti-svasti) were performed, and the necessary ritual paintings were commissioned."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/0a006229-7e08-4cb2-9883-1527f615bbfb> ;
    rdfs:comment "The topmost roof tier was completely tiled with traditional materials. Supplies for raising the ceremonial banner (betālipatāḥ) atop the finial were sent from the Nhaygāṃ (literally, \"seven villages\") cluster east of Bhaktapur. Following the completion of the top tier's roofing, special propitiatory rituals (śānti-svasti) were performed, and the necessary ritual paintings were commissioned."@en ;
