<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/0b0e8dd4-b9a3-4348-b53b-e2d8cd54f9f4_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Construction"@en ;
    dcterms:description "King Mahendra Malla built the grand temple for his tutelary deity, Taleju Bhavānī on the 10th of the dark fortnight of Māgha in 1564 CE (NS 684). TheDevamālāVaṃśāvalī, a 19th century chronicle, records the temple's completion as the 5th of the bright fortnight of Māgha in 1549 CE (NS 669). The chronicle's account appears inaccurate, as historical evidence places Mahendra Malla's reign between 1562 and 1574 CE (NS 682-694). Both Gutschow (2011, p. 428) and Slusser (1982, p. 191) also concur with the 1564 CE date, which is now considered the most accurate."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/0b0e8dd4-b9a3-4348-b53b-e2d8cd54f9f4> ;
    rdfs:comment "King Mahendra Malla built the grand temple for his tutelary deity, Taleju Bhavānī on the 10th of the dark fortnight of Māgha in 1564 CE (NS 684). TheDevamālāVaṃśāvalī, a 19th century chronicle, records the temple's completion as the 5th of the bright fortnight of Māgha in 1549 CE (NS 669). The chronicle's account appears inaccurate, as historical evidence places Mahendra Malla's reign between 1562 and 1574 CE (NS 682-694). Both Gutschow (2011, p. 428) and Slusser (1982, p. 191) also concur with the 1564 CE date, which is now considered the most accurate."@en ;
