<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/0cb251ee-3005-42d3-bc37-fe6cfbb30747_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Consecration ;
    rdfs:label "Initial construction of Caitya and phalcā"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Rāmahari Bhāro, his wife Rudrāyani (Rudrāyaṇī) and their nephew Viśveśvara Bhāro (together with 23 other members of the community) jointly constructed aphalcāand consecrated a statue of Triratnan inside it, and built this Caitya in front of thephalcā. The founders had also made arrangements for a regular income to maintain those monuments. The inscription records a group of four Bhāros (Cikuti Bhāro, Viśvarāma Bhāro, Śaśideva Bhāro and Rāmarāja Bhāro) who were made responsible for taking care of the monuments. The inscription also lists the entireguṭhīmembers, position of the planets and persons to be invited for annual rituals."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/0cb251ee-3005-42d3-bc37-fe6cfbb30747> ;
    rdfs:comment "Rāmahari Bhāro, his wife Rudrāyani (Rudrāyaṇī) and their nephew Viśveśvara Bhāro (together with 23 other members of the community) jointly constructed aphalcāand consecrated a statue of Triratnan inside it, and built this Caitya in front of thephalcā. The founders had also made arrangements for a regular income to maintain those monuments. The inscription records a group of four Bhāros (Cikuti Bhāro, Viśvarāma Bhāro, Śaśideva Bhāro and Rāmarāja Bhāro) who were made responsible for taking care of the monuments. The inscription also lists the entireguṭhīmembers, position of the planets and persons to be invited for annual rituals."@en ;
