<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/0f14007d-53ac-4148-8478-6a2f8b447e82_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Initial construction"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Bhavānīśaṅkara, son of Bhavānīdāsa Bhāro, from Kirtipur built the temple together with other individuals from local groups named Duvāra and Deśa. Bhavānīdāsa Bhāro, on the other hand, installed the sculptures of the deities and donated land parcels to set religious trusts to oversee daily and periodic rituals at the temple."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/0f14007d-53ac-4148-8478-6a2f8b447e82> ;
    rdfs:comment "Bhavānīśaṅkara, son of Bhavānīdāsa Bhāro, from Kirtipur built the temple together with other individuals from local groups named Duvāra and Deśa. Bhavānīdāsa Bhāro, on the other hand, installed the sculptures of the deities and donated land parcels to set religious trusts to oversee daily and periodic rituals at the temple."@en ;
