<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/1165bb2e-eb1e-11e9-8bc4-0242ac130002_1> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Opening of a shop"@en ;
    dcterms:description "In the 1970s the Lagankhel area was reconstructed and a public bus station was built. At that time homeless people from the area started using thephalcāas their shelter. To prevent this, the residents of Lagankhel, Thati and Taṃgaḥ decided to rent thephalcāout to shops. According to an elderly man living in Thati Ṭola, the rent collected from thephalcāwas used to install street lights in the area."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/1165bb2e-eb1e-11e9-8bc4-0242ac130002> ;
    rdfs:comment "In the 1970s the Lagankhel area was reconstructed and a public bus station was built. At that time homeless people from the area started using thephalcāas their shelter. To prevent this, the residents of Lagankhel, Thati and Taṃgaḥ decided to rent thephalcāout to shops. According to an elderly man living in Thati Ṭola, the rent collected from thephalcāwas used to install street lights in the area."@en ;
