<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/12e25456-4bce-11ea-91df-0242ac130006_1> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Occupation by Āditya Malla"@en ;
    dcterms:description "In 1328 CE (NS 448) the Khaśīyā king Āditya Malla invaded the Kathmandu Valley. He occupied the Pulavahīrī in Patan and laid seige on the town for 22 days. Mentioned Pulavahīrī most possibly is this Bahī. He set fire to all the three cities."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/12e25456-4bce-11ea-91df-0242ac130006> ;
