<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/1347d2d6-66e1-4884-bc56-a2286a68d4e8_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Enshrinement ;
    rdfs:label "Initial construction"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Two large inscriptions in Sanskrit and Newari record the construction of Kavīndrapura by King Pratāpa Malla. The inscriptions state that Narasiṃha, the fourth incarnation of Lord Viṣṇu, got infuriated when the king danced in the guise of the deity. To appease Narasiṃha, Pratāpa Malla built Kavīndrapura and enshrined a statue of Narasiṃha along with various other deities."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/1347d2d6-66e1-4884-bc56-a2286a68d4e8> ;
    rdfs:comment "Two large inscriptions in Sanskrit and Newari record the construction of Kavīndrapura by King Pratāpa Malla. The inscriptions state that Narasiṃha, the fourth incarnation of Lord Viṣṇu, got infuriated when the king danced in the guise of the deity. To appease Narasiṃha, Pratāpa Malla built Kavīndrapura and enshrined a statue of Narasiṃha along with various other deities."@en ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/agent/antigravity_agent> ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/activity/heritagegraph_kg_construction> ;
    hg:eventIndex 0 ;
    hg:extractionMethod "source_table" ;
    hg:isEventOf <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/1347d2d6-66e1-4884-bc56-a2286a68d4e8> .

<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/1347d2d6-66e1-4884-bc56-a2286a68d4e8_1> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Enshrinement ;
    rdfs:label "Land endowment"@en ;
    dcterms:description "King Pratapa Malla recorded the endowment of many plots of land in the name of the deities enshrined in Kavīndrapura in this inscription. He also outlined various rituals and traditions to be carried out from the income of the lands."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/1347d2d6-66e1-4884-bc56-a2286a68d4e8> ;
    rdfs:comment "King Pratapa Malla recorded the endowment of many plots of land in the name of the deities enshrined in Kavīndrapura in this inscription. He also outlined various rituals and traditions to be carried out from the income of the lands."@en ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/agent/antigravity_agent> ;
