<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/1347d2d6-66e1-4884-bc56-a2286a68d4e8_6> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Reinstallation of a damaged inscription"@en ;
    dcterms:description "After a person named Abhimānasiṃha Khatrī intentionally destroyed the inscription installed by Vīradhvaja Kārkī in 1827 CE (VS 1883), his youngest wife Mahāmāyā petitioned Jagat Śamśera and Raṇa Uddīpa Siṃha in the Rāṇā administration and got the content of the broken inscription reinstalled on this inscription. However, the year of the installation of this inscription is erroneously given as VS 190. Therefore, the year is unclear."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/1347d2d6-66e1-4884-bc56-a2286a68d4e8> ;
    rdfs:comment "After a person named Abhimānasiṃha Khatrī intentionally destroyed the inscription installed by Vīradhvaja Kārkī in 1827 CE (VS 1883), his youngest wife Mahāmāyā petitioned Jagat Śamśera and Raṇa Uddīpa Siṃha in the Rāṇā administration and got the content of the broken inscription reinstalled on this inscription. However, the year of the installation of this inscription is erroneously given as VS 190. Therefore, the year is unclear."@en ;
