<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/138e0452-8e6c-4b68-8410-b5263da353a8_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Consecration ;
    rdfs:label "Construction of temple"@en ;
    dcterms:description "A four line inscription indevanāgarīscript is inserted above the temple's door. It is inscribed on stone. Yogi Naraharinath first mentioned it in 1956 (Naraharinath 1956 (VS 2013), 168-169, cited inShrestha 2009, 80).The inscription records the construction of the temple under the auspices of Pratāpa Śāhī and his nephew Māna Śāhī, in ŚS 1504 (1582 CE). It was consecrated by Ātmanātha and Laṁgarnātha, two Nātha yogis. Interestingly, the inscription was written by a certain Rāma Kṛṣṇa from Benares (Shrestha 2009, 280)."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/138e0452-8e6c-4b68-8410-b5263da353a8> ;
    rdfs:comment "A four line inscription indevanāgarīscript is inserted above the temple's door. It is inscribed on stone. Yogi Naraharinath first mentioned it in 1956 (Naraharinath 1956 (VS 2013), 168-169, cited inShrestha 2009, 80).The inscription records the construction of the temple under the auspices of Pratāpa Śāhī and his nephew Māna Śāhī, in ŚS 1504 (1582 CE). It was consecrated by Ātmanātha and Laṁgarnātha, two Nātha yogis. Interestingly, the inscription was written by a certain Rāma Kṛṣṇa from Benares (Shrestha 2009, 280)."@en ;
