<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/13b0e238-70ba-11ea-b99f-0242ac130006_5> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Sacrificial worship at Mahālakṣmī temple"@en ;
    dcterms:description "In Nepal, many people believe that when there is a big problem in the country, tears leak from the eyes of gods or sweat comes out of their bodies. When tears flowed from the eyes of Rāto Matsyendranātha in Taḥ Bāhāḥ (LAL0050), thePañcarakṣātext was recited for eight days and a special worship followed by sacrifices was performed in this temple, the Vaiṣṇavī temple of Yappā and the Bālakumārī temple of Kvāṭhachẽ. This event took place before the Mahālakṣmī temple was reconstructed in its current style."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/13b0e238-70ba-11ea-b99f-0242ac130006> ;
    rdfs:comment "In Nepal, many people believe that when there is a big problem in the country, tears leak from the eyes of gods or sweat comes out of their bodies. When tears flowed from the eyes of Rāto Matsyendranātha in Taḥ Bāhāḥ (LAL0050), thePañcarakṣātext was recited for eight days and a special worship followed by sacrifices was performed in this temple, the Vaiṣṇavī temple of Yappā and the Bālakumārī temple of Kvāṭhachẽ. This event took place before the Mahālakṣmī temple was reconstructed in its current style."@en ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/agent/antigravity_agent> ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/activity/heritagegraph_kg_construction> ;
