<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/147f9da8-5a54-438d-b51e-1d473f23b374_8> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Regulation about Kumārī"@en ;
    dcterms:description "During the reign of King Raṇajita Malla, Kumārīs were sought from outside the Śākya-Vajrācārya family and appointed as Kumārī. In doing so, the virgins died unlucky. After that, a rule was made that a Kumārī should be appointed only from the Śākya-Vajrācārya family and the Kumārī was also given special rights. The king framed the following regulations: anyone including the king and the gods who observed the Ihi, Cuḍākarma and piercing of the ears without a permission of Kumārī would be fined of Rs. 100."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/147f9da8-5a54-438d-b51e-1d473f23b374> ;
    rdfs:comment "During the reign of King Raṇajita Malla, Kumārīs were sought from outside the Śākya-Vajrācārya family and appointed as Kumārī. In doing so, the virgins died unlucky. After that, a rule was made that a Kumārī should be appointed only from the Śākya-Vajrācārya family and the Kumārī was also given special rights. The king framed the following regulations: anyone including the king and the gods who observed the Ihi, Cuḍākarma and piercing of the ears without a permission of Kumārī would be fined of Rs. 100."@en ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/agent/antigravity_agent> ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/activity/heritagegraph_kg_construction> ;
