<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/166b876b-49b3-480a-b7c4-73694e95b056_4> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Reconstruction of the temple"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The Department of Archaeology, deciding that the temple needed to be rebuilt after the 2015 earthquakes, carried out its reconstruction in 2022 CE at a contractual amount of NRs. 23.7 million (P. MālīVS 2074). Prior to the 2015 earthquakes, the temple's first-floor roof connected to the adjacentsataḥ(THC0060), enabling access between thesataḥand the temple's sanctum. This unique architectural element was not preserved during this reconstruction. The traditional tiles on the roofs were also replaced with copper sheets."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/166b876b-49b3-480a-b7c4-73694e95b056> ;
    rdfs:comment "The Department of Archaeology, deciding that the temple needed to be rebuilt after the 2015 earthquakes, carried out its reconstruction in 2022 CE at a contractual amount of NRs. 23.7 million (P. MālīVS 2074). Prior to the 2015 earthquakes, the temple's first-floor roof connected to the adjacentsataḥ(THC0060), enabling access between thesataḥand the temple's sanctum. This unique architectural element was not preserved during this reconstruction. The traditional tiles on the roofs were also replaced with copper sheets."@en ;
