<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/16f8b0dc-e9b1-11e9-8bc4-0242ac130002_1> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Destruction by earthquake"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The temple was levelled during the earthquake of 1934 (Rāṇā1992, 115). TheDevmalavaṃśāvalīstates that all the three stories of the temple collapsed and the image of the main deity was covered in rubble (Yogī2013, 55)."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/16f8b0dc-e9b1-11e9-8bc4-0242ac130002> ;
    rdfs:comment "The temple was levelled during the earthquake of 1934 (Rāṇā1992, 115). TheDevmalavaṃśāvalīstates that all the three stories of the temple collapsed and the image of the main deity was covered in rubble (Yogī2013, 55)."@en ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/agent/antigravity_agent> ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/activity/heritagegraph_kg_construction> ;
    hg:eventIndex 1 ;
    hg:extractionMethod "source_table" ;
    hg:isEventOf <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/16f8b0dc-e9b1-11e9-8bc4-0242ac130002> .

<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/16f8b0dc-e9b1-11e9-8bc4-0242ac130002_2> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Consecration ;
    rdfs:label "Rebuilding the temple"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Prime minister Juddha Śamśera reconstructed the temple and consecrated the deity in 1938 (VS 1995 Jestha 11). He was honoured withsindurajātrāand welcomed with many decorated gates in Patan. Gambling was also allowed from 9.00 pm on that day."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/16f8b0dc-e9b1-11e9-8bc4-0242ac130002> ;
    rdfs:comment "Prime minister Juddha Śamśera reconstructed the temple and consecrated the deity in 1938 (VS 1995 Jestha 11). He was honoured withsindurajātrāand welcomed with many decorated gates in Patan. Gambling was also allowed from 9.00 pm on that day."@en ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/agent/antigravity_agent> ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/activity/heritagegraph_kg_construction> ;
    hg:eventIndex 2 ;
    hg:extractionMethod "source_table" ;
    hg:isEventOf <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/16f8b0dc-e9b1-11e9-8bc4-0242ac130002> .

<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/16f8b0dc-e9b1-11e9-8bc4-0242ac130002_3> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Construction of five storied temple for Degutale"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Śivasiṃha Malla established the temple. However, we do not know whether he only installed the deity or if he really constructed the temple. King Siddhinarasiṃha Malla is credited for changing the structure of the Degutale; he turned it into a five-storey temple and made an offering of a golden pinnacle and a flag. Various historical records disagree on the dates that these events took place. TheDevmalāvaṃśāvalīmentions that this occured on NS 787 Jestha 2 (see inYogī2013, 55), whileBhaṣāvaṃśāvalīstates that it was NS 767, on the second of the dark half of Jestha (see inLamsāl2023, 62). The inscription, however, provides NS 761 as the date when this event happened. The inscription appears to be the most authentic source."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/16f8b0dc-e9b1-11e9-8bc4-0242ac130002> ;
    rdfs:comment "Śivasiṃha Malla established the temple. However, we do not know whether he only installed the deity or if he really constructed the temple. King Siddhinarasiṃha Malla is credited for changing the structure of the Degutale; he turned it into a five-storey temple and made an offering of a golden pinnacle and a flag. Various historical records disagree on the dates that these events took place. TheDevmalāvaṃśāvalīmentions that this occured on NS 787 Jestha 2 (see inYogī2013, 55), whileBhaṣāvaṃśāvalīstates that it was NS 767, on the second of the dark half of Jestha (see inLamsāl2023, 62). The inscription, however, provides NS 761 as the date when this event happened. The inscription appears to be the most authentic source."@en ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/agent/antigravity_agent> ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/activity/heritagegraph_kg_construction> ;
    hg:eventIndex 3 ;
    hg:extractionMethod "source_table" ;
    hg:isEventOf <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/16f8b0dc-e9b1-11e9-8bc4-0242ac130002> .

<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/16f8b0dc-e9b1-11e9-8bc4-0242ac130002_4> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Destruction by blaze"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Nepālikabhūpavaṃśāvalī(19.3.152) states that King Śrīnivāsa Malla rebuilt the three-tiered Degutale temple in NS 783. Aṭhyāsaphūrecording the historical events mentions that there was a huge fire on the sixth day of the bright half of Vaiśākha NS 783 (Regmi1966, part 3, page 100, Thyasaphu). A colophon ofKubjikāpaddhatimanuscript notes that Degutale was completely destroyed by the fire of NS 783 (Regmi1966, part 2, 76). Although the event year is similar, only one document provides the full date."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/16f8b0dc-e9b1-11e9-8bc4-0242ac130002> ;
    rdfs:comment "Nepālikabhūpavaṃśāvalī(19.3.152) states that King Śrīnivāsa Malla rebuilt the three-tiered Degutale temple in NS 783. Aṭhyāsaphūrecording the historical events mentions that there was a huge fire on the sixth day of the bright half of Vaiśākha NS 783 (Regmi1966, part 3, page 100, Thyasaphu). A colophon ofKubjikāpaddhatimanuscript notes that Degutale was completely destroyed by the fire of NS 783 (Regmi1966, part 2, 76). Although the event year is similar, only one document provides the full date."@en ;
