<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/170a68d0-e68d-11e9-b125-0242ac130002_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Consecration ;
    rdfs:label "Reconstruction of the temple"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Paramāna Viśvaṁbhara Bhāro reconstructed the old three-storey temple. He consecrated a new statue of Umāmaheśvara, and golden vessels and banners were added to the temple in the presence of King Śrīnivasa Malla and Prince Yoganaredra Malla. Aguṭhīwas also established with the land-grants to facilitate daily ritual worship and other functions of the temple."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/170a68d0-e68d-11e9-b125-0242ac130002> ;
