<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/1798db32-ecce-11e9-8bc4-0242ac130002_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Construction of Jothā Bāhāḥ"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Construction of the Jothā Bāhāḥ. On the right side of the main shrine, a copper plate inscription informs visitors of the establishment of the monastery. The inscription states that this Bāhāḥ, named Jayaśrī Vihāra, was established on Wednesday 3rd of the bright moon of Vaiśākha in NS 773. Moreover, it states that it was established by Yodhā, together with his wife Jayantī and their their daughter Śirī, as well as their sons Ratna, Amu, Ratnasiṃha, and Cintāmaṇi."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/1798db32-ecce-11e9-8bc4-0242ac130002> ;
    rdfs:comment "Construction of the Jothā Bāhāḥ. On the right side of the main shrine, a copper plate inscription informs visitors of the establishment of the monastery. The inscription states that this Bāhāḥ, named Jayaśrī Vihāra, was established on Wednesday 3rd of the bright moon of Vaiśākha in NS 773. Moreover, it states that it was established by Yodhā, together with his wife Jayantī and their their daughter Śirī, as well as their sons Ratna, Amu, Ratnasiṃha, and Cintāmaṇi."@en ;
