<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/1798db32-ecce-11e9-8bc4-0242ac130002_1> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Samyak Mahādāna ritual"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Vajrācārya(1999,151) states that on Thursday, 8th of the bright half of Śrāvaṇa, NS 787, Jothāju sent an invitation to King Śrīnivāsa Malla and performed asamyak mahādāna. The king was seated in a throne made of gold, which can now be found in the Patan Museum. Every year on the full moon day of Jyeṣṭha (Jyā Punhi) this throne is placed in the Kṛṣṇa temple of Mangalbazar for exhibition."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/1798db32-ecce-11e9-8bc4-0242ac130002> ;
    rdfs:comment "Vajrācārya(1999,151) states that on Thursday, 8th of the bright half of Śrāvaṇa, NS 787, Jothāju sent an invitation to King Śrīnivāsa Malla and performed asamyak mahādāna. The king was seated in a throne made of gold, which can now be found in the Patan Museum. Every year on the full moon day of Jyeṣṭha (Jyā Punhi) this throne is placed in the Kṛṣṇa temple of Mangalbazar for exhibition."@en ;
