<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/1809008c-3ba0-449b-afe6-1e8f47b66816_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Construction of Mandaḥ Phalcā (KIR4056)"@en ;
    dcterms:description "This inscription is placed in the inside of a wall of the Sāḥgaḥ Gaṇeśa Phalcā, but does not belong, or directly refer, to it. Instead, it relates to the nearby Mandaḥ Phalcā (KIR4056). This inscription was probably relocated for security reasons after the Mandaḥ Phalcā collapsed. It clearly mentions the initial construction of the Phalcā with ajaḥdhuṃand formation of aguṭhīby Bhāgīsiṃha Bhāro (Amātya) and his younger brother Siddhisiṃha from the Dathu Ṭola (text: Dathu Tvāra) in the memory of their father Manoharasiṃha. The inscription also records the installation of statues of Trivikrama and Lakṣmīnārāyaṇa. While the statue of Lakṣmīnārāyaṇa is still placed in the Sāḥgaḥ Gaṇeśa Phalcā, the Trivikrama statue is no longer available at the site."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/1809008c-3ba0-449b-afe6-1e8f47b66816> ;
    rdfs:comment "This inscription is placed in the inside of a wall of the Sāḥgaḥ Gaṇeśa Phalcā, but does not belong, or directly refer, to it. Instead, it relates to the nearby Mandaḥ Phalcā (KIR4056). This inscription was probably relocated for security reasons after the Mandaḥ Phalcā collapsed. It clearly mentions the initial construction of the Phalcā with ajaḥdhuṃand formation of aguṭhīby Bhāgīsiṃha Bhāro (Amātya) and his younger brother Siddhisiṃha from the Dathu Ṭola (text: Dathu Tvāra) in the memory of their father Manoharasiṃha. The inscription also records the installation of statues of Trivikrama and Lakṣmīnārāyaṇa. While the statue of Lakṣmīnārāyaṇa is still placed in the Sāḥgaḥ Gaṇeśa Phalcā, the Trivikrama statue is no longer available at the site."@en ;
