<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/1b0a5033-a1ca-4049-8d6f-d1c7b243eabe_1> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Initial construction"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Lāykū Phalcā was established at the time of King Jitāmitramalla by his younger brother Ugra Malla and son Bhūpatindra along with his chief minister Dukhi Bhāgirāma (Gutschow2011, 645). The inscription also records rules and regulations about distributing water to farmers by an irrigation system. This inscription is a very important source of information with respect to the traditional irrigation system of the valley and the state's role in it."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/1b0a5033-a1ca-4049-8d6f-d1c7b243eabe> ;
    rdfs:comment "Lāykū Phalcā was established at the time of King Jitāmitramalla by his younger brother Ugra Malla and son Bhūpatindra along with his chief minister Dukhi Bhāgirāma (Gutschow2011, 645). The inscription also records rules and regulations about distributing water to farmers by an irrigation system. This inscription is a very important source of information with respect to the traditional irrigation system of the valley and the state's role in it."@en ;
