<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/1ea23294-c955-4058-b587-66d1041cb161_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Installation of pillar"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The eastern side of the pillar is inscribed with 7 lines written in a Nāgarī script. The date of 1231 can be read. If referring to the Śāka era, this date would correspond to 1339 CE.It is possible that the inscription was executed years after the installation, as it goes past the square space usually used for it and ends below it."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/1ea23294-c955-4058-b587-66d1041cb161> ;
    rdfs:comment "The eastern side of the pillar is inscribed with 7 lines written in a Nāgarī script. The date of 1231 can be read. If referring to the Śāka era, this date would correspond to 1339 CE.It is possible that the inscription was executed years after the installation, as it goes past the square space usually used for it and ends below it."@en ;
