<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/1ef0f80f-bf24-4b92-9fc2-e913881c5a44_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Initial construction"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The inscription reveals that the Aṣṭamī Sevā Samiti, a group of devotees from the Svayambhū area in Kathmandu, built the Phalcā that lies on the way to the Cobhāra hillock where the temple of Ānandādi Lokeśvara is situated. The inscription also instructs the concerned persons to perform the Phalcā’s anniversary ritual."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/1ef0f80f-bf24-4b92-9fc2-e913881c5a44> ;
    rdfs:comment "The inscription reveals that the Aṣṭamī Sevā Samiti, a group of devotees from the Svayambhū area in Kathmandu, built the Phalcā that lies on the way to the Cobhāra hillock where the temple of Ānandādi Lokeśvara is situated. The inscription also instructs the concerned persons to perform the Phalcā’s anniversary ritual."@en ;
