<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/20c7052d-2611-47b2-836d-b7f92638a1ee_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Consecration ;
    rdfs:label "Consecration of Amoghasiddhi statue and beautifying it by offering various decorative ritual objects"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Two local groups named ‘Bhagavāna Buddha Palisthā Samiti’ and ‘Sāymi Dabū’ installed a statue of Amoghasiddhi to the southwest of the Temple. Meanwhile, Jñānaratna Sāymi offered anilāṃover the statue in memory of his father Jñānabahādura Sāymi. Likewise, Hari Sāymi and Buddhalakṣmī Sāymi got a balustrade of 108dalūlamps installed here in memory of their parents Pūrṇabahādura and Jñānamāyā. Buddhalakṣmī also offered a bell."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/20c7052d-2611-47b2-836d-b7f92638a1ee> ;
    rdfs:comment "Two local groups named ‘Bhagavāna Buddha Palisthā Samiti’ and ‘Sāymi Dabū’ installed a statue of Amoghasiddhi to the southwest of the Temple. Meanwhile, Jñānaratna Sāymi offered anilāṃover the statue in memory of his father Jñānabahādura Sāymi. Likewise, Hari Sāymi and Buddhalakṣmī Sāymi got a balustrade of 108dalūlamps installed here in memory of their parents Pūrṇabahādura and Jñānamāyā. Buddhalakṣmī also offered a bell."@en ;
