<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/21b56e2d-d3ff-4ce6-94cc-d5b85fb8a31e_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Licchavi period inscription"@en ;
    dcterms:description "This inscription is attached to the eastern wall of the Nāsaḥ Chẽ. Unfortunately, it cannot be deciphered because it is badly eroded. It might be the same inscription that is mentioned by D. Śākya (VS 2030, p. 582). He writes that almost all letters (akṣaras) of the inscription, except the part where its date is mentioned, have deteriorated. The date reads as follows: ‘saṃbat 454 jyeśṭhakṛiṣṇadivā 6’. Thus, it could be said that the inscription was issued during the reign of King Vasantadeva (r. 506 - 532 CE)."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/21b56e2d-d3ff-4ce6-94cc-d5b85fb8a31e> ;
    rdfs:comment "This inscription is attached to the eastern wall of the Nāsaḥ Chẽ. Unfortunately, it cannot be deciphered because it is badly eroded. It might be the same inscription that is mentioned by D. Śākya (VS 2030, p. 582). He writes that almost all letters (akṣaras) of the inscription, except the part where its date is mentioned, have deteriorated. The date reads as follows: ‘saṃbat 454 jyeśṭhakṛiṣṇadivā 6’. Thus, it could be said that the inscription was issued during the reign of King Vasantadeva (r. 506 - 532 CE)."@en ;
