    rdfs:label "Installation of lion statues"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Pruscha (1975, p. 241) suggests the lion statues at the Siddhivināyaka temple were established in 1603 CE. He probably referred to the lion statues that flank the Gaṇeśa statue, as the lion statues by the main entrance appear to be considerably later addition."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/21d0cb3c-a698-496c-8807-26338c5d30c8> ;
