<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/224ae916-e8e2-11e9-8bc4-0242ac130002_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Unknown"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The inscription is on the base of the Pañca Buddha statues, beneath theesoteric deity(kvāḥpāḥdyaḥ). It is fragmented, and so the date and event is not clearly readable. The inscription mentions that Viso Siṃ was a caretaker. It also mentions that everyone must respect the wishes of the donors. It states that any act contrary to their wishes would be sinful and equivalent to killing a Brāhmaṇa."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/224ae916-e8e2-11e9-8bc4-0242ac130002> ;
    rdfs:comment "The inscription is on the base of the Pañca Buddha statues, beneath theesoteric deity(kvāḥpāḥdyaḥ). It is fragmented, and so the date and event is not clearly readable. The inscription mentions that Viso Siṃ was a caretaker. It also mentions that everyone must respect the wishes of the donors. It states that any act contrary to their wishes would be sinful and equivalent to killing a Brāhmaṇa."@en ;
