<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/23d6e0b6-7f2d-44db-a22e-913a500a756a_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Addition of suvarṇamukha (gilt face)"@en ;
    dcterms:description "According to this inscription, asuvarṇamukha(gilded face) was fixed to the previously existing statue of Gaṇeśa. Fifteen people from the Bhāvo or Bhāro (Jyāpu) and Śākya communities were involved in this task. The chief of the group was an individual named Devarāja. The group also formedpunhī sevā,performing certain activities to honour Gaṇeśa. The inscription also records the offering of a gilt \"mudaya\"to the temple. The exact meaning \"mudaya\"is not clear."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/23d6e0b6-7f2d-44db-a22e-913a500a756a> ;
    rdfs:comment "According to this inscription, asuvarṇamukha(gilded face) was fixed to the previously existing statue of Gaṇeśa. Fifteen people from the Bhāvo or Bhāro (Jyāpu) and Śākya communities were involved in this task. The chief of the group was an individual named Devarāja. The group also formedpunhī sevā,performing certain activities to honour Gaṇeśa. The inscription also records the offering of a gilt \"mudaya\"to the temple. The exact meaning \"mudaya\"is not clear."@en ;
