<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/24001b17-8be8-4a56-82b4-e4191db787ec_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Initial construction"@en ;
    dcterms:description "In 1851 CE (VS 1907), Bamabahādura Kũvara built the Tina Devala temple along the Vāgamatī riverbanks, showcasing a distinctive architectural style.The historical record of the temple, preserved in atāmrapatra, offers evidence of the simultaneous construction ofsataḥs, particularly highlighting the Tīna Devala Sataḥ."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/24001b17-8be8-4a56-82b4-e4191db787ec> ;
    rdfs:comment "In 1851 CE (VS 1907), Bamabahādura Kũvara built the Tina Devala temple along the Vāgamatī riverbanks, showcasing a distinctive architectural style.The historical record of the temple, preserved in atāmrapatra, offers evidence of the simultaneous construction ofsataḥs, particularly highlighting the Tīna Devala Sataḥ."@en ;
