<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/24afe176-f66a-11e9-a3c8-0242ac130002_14> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:RitualEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Establishment of a guṭhī for organising hāthuhāyukegu (see below)"@en ;
    dcterms:description "King Jayanarasiṃha established aguṭhīto organisehāthuhāyukeguduring the chariot procession of Karuṇāmaya.Hāthuhāyekeguis a tradition of placing a mud vessel filled with local liquor (chyāṅ) behind the mask of Bhairava and connecting a pipe to his mouth from which the liquor comes. People drink the liquor during the chariot procession."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/24afe176-f66a-11e9-a3c8-0242ac130002> ;
