        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Donation of gold by a king of Sikkim"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Paṇḍita Jīvarāja and Jayamuni from Gāḥ Bāhāḥ (LAL0510) went to Sikkim and offered a full plateprasāda(gift) to the King of Sikkim. In gratitude, the King filled the plate with gold. When Jayamuni returned with the gold, he called a meeting of the members of thesaṅghato decide what to do with it. They decided to make fixtures (side panels for the four sides, thetoraṇas, and the decorations above thetoraṇasfor the chariot) for the Red Matsyendranātha. The fixtures were placed on the chariot for the first time in NS 774 after the chariot arrived at Gāḥ Bāhāḥ. Aguṭhīknown as theLusa Guṭhīwas then set up to ensure the safekeeping and maintenance of the fixtures."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/24afe176-f66a-11e9-a3c8-0242ac130002> ;
    rdfs:comment "Paṇḍita Jīvarāja and Jayamuni from Gāḥ Bāhāḥ (LAL0510) went to Sikkim and offered a full plateprasāda(gift) to the King of Sikkim. In gratitude, the King filled the plate with gold. When Jayamuni returned with the gold, he called a meeting of the members of thesaṅghato decide what to do with it. They decided to make fixtures (side panels for the four sides, thetoraṇas, and the decorations above thetoraṇasfor the chariot) for the Red Matsyendranātha. The fixtures were placed on the chariot for the first time in NS 774 after the chariot arrived at Gāḥ Bāhāḥ. Aguṭhīknown as theLusa Guṭhīwas then set up to ensure the safekeeping and maintenance of the fixtures."@en ;
