<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/24afe176-f66a-11e9-a3c8-0242ac130002_20> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "References to Bugmalokeśvara (Buṅgadyaḥ) in the palm-leaf manuscripts"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Slusser(1982, vol. 2, plate no. 594 and 595) gives photos of two Nepalese manuscripts with depictions of Bugmalokeśvara. She dates the first manuscript to 1071 CE and the second to 1679 CE. However, she does not provide any further details regarding the manuscripts and does not mention anything about how she dated them. Paleographically, the first manuscript cannot be from such an early date. It is more likely that it comes from the 17th-18th century.Locke(1980, 300) also mentions one such manuscript containing a miniture painting of Bugama Lokeśvara preserved in Paris and vaguely dates it to 120-220 NS."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/24afe176-f66a-11e9-a3c8-0242ac130002> ;
    rdfs:comment "Slusser(1982, vol. 2, plate no. 594 and 595) gives photos of two Nepalese manuscripts with depictions of Bugmalokeśvara. She dates the first manuscript to 1071 CE and the second to 1679 CE. However, she does not provide any further details regarding the manuscripts and does not mention anything about how she dated them. Paleographically, the first manuscript cannot be from such an early date. It is more likely that it comes from the 17th-18th century.Locke(1980, 300) also mentions one such manuscript containing a miniture painting of Bugama Lokeśvara preserved in Paris and vaguely dates it to 120-220 NS."@en ;
