<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/24afe176-f66a-11e9-a3c8-0242ac130002_5> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:TransferOfCustody ;
    rdfs:label "Installation of an inscription regulating the Kārttika fesitval"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Śrīnivāsa Malla installed an inscription at the temple to regulate the Kārttika festival. The inscription states that women of the Dhobi (washermen), Jogī (Kusle) and Kasāi (butcher) caste are not allowed to take the vow (vrata) to participate in the festival. Only those who come on the full moon day (24 hours) of Āśvina are allowed to take thevrata. The king had also endowed land to feed the devotees at the end of the festival."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/24afe176-f66a-11e9-a3c8-0242ac130002> ;
    rdfs:comment "Śrīnivāsa Malla installed an inscription at the temple to regulate the Kārttika festival. The inscription states that women of the Dhobi (washermen), Jogī (Kusle) and Kasāi (butcher) caste are not allowed to take the vow (vrata) to participate in the festival. Only those who come on the full moon day (24 hours) of Āśvina are allowed to take thevrata. The king had also endowed land to feed the devotees at the end of the festival."@en ;
