        hg:Consecration ;
    rdfs:label "Consecration of the Śikharakūṭa Caitya"@en ;
    dcterms:description "During the reign of King Raṇabahādura Śāha, aśikharakūṭa caityawas established to the west of the monastic building. On this occasion, a golden necklace (hṛdayaphola) and a silverpiṇḍapātra(a bowl forpiṇḍa) decorated with lotus petals were also offered to thekvāḥpāḥdyaḥ."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/26404afc-cb0a-11e9-b993-0242ac140002> ;
