<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/26be7902-a8b4-403e-a593-00cde09fc614_1> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:TransferOfCustody ;
    rdfs:label "Expansion of the temple"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Thirty-seven years after the establishment of the Bhīmasena statue, Dhanasiṃ and his wife Māneśvarī of Tekhāco, Bhaktapur, expanded the temple. They enclosed the sanctum by building a temple on it and added aphalcādirectly in front, dedicated to Bhīmasena. To ensure the temple's continued maintenance, they endowed a four-ropanīplot of land in Banepa."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/26be7902-a8b4-403e-a593-00cde09fc614> ;
    rdfs:comment "Thirty-seven years after the establishment of the Bhīmasena statue, Dhanasiṃ and his wife Māneśvarī of Tekhāco, Bhaktapur, expanded the temple. They enclosed the sanctum by building a temple on it and added aphalcādirectly in front, dedicated to Bhīmasena. To ensure the temple's continued maintenance, they endowed a four-ropanīplot of land in Banepa."@en ;
