    hg:isEventOf <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/26d29a66-b9bb-4787-9175-479e3cb2c5e9> .

<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/26d29a66-b9bb-4787-9175-479e3cb2c5e9_1> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Installation of bell"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The inscription on a bell installed south of the temple states that Princess Amarakānteśvarī offered the bell through Captain Juddhamānasiṃha Rājabhaṇḍārī. Michaels and Tandon (2017, p.70), however, mention that she offered the bell through Siddhimānasiṃha Rājbhaṇḍārī. The bell is no longer at the site. Therefore, it could not be ascertained if it was Juddhamānasiṃha or Siddhimānasiṃha, who assisted Amarakānteśvarī in offering the bell. Usually, the donor of the bell is also the person to commission the construction of the temple the bell was donated to."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/26d29a66-b9bb-4787-9175-479e3cb2c5e9> ;
    rdfs:comment "The inscription on a bell installed south of the temple states that Princess Amarakānteśvarī offered the bell through Captain Juddhamānasiṃha Rājabhaṇḍārī. Michaels and Tandon (2017, p.70), however, mention that she offered the bell through Siddhimānasiṃha Rājbhaṇḍārī. The bell is no longer at the site. Therefore, it could not be ascertained if it was Juddhamānasiṃha or Siddhimānasiṃha, who assisted Amarakānteśvarī in offering the bell. Usually, the donor of the bell is also the person to commission the construction of the temple the bell was donated to."@en ;
