    rdfs:label "Construction of a caitya"@en ;
    dcterms:description "During the reign of King Jayajaga (Jagajjaya Malla), acaityawas established. Dvāre Dhanasiṃha, a resident of Dhugāma Ṭola in Gokarṇa, together with his wife Rachamani and their children Kṛsnanasiha (Kṛṣṇanarasiṃha), Sumati, and Dhanakṛṣṇa, constructed the caitya. Thiscaityais located along the route from the Kāntibhairava Dyaḥchẽ to the Pakanāvatī Gaṇeśa temple."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/27291618-45b0-4bc5-b9ca-3e3ea8c4b8b5> ;
