    rdfs:label "Establishment of Śivapūjeśvara (PPK0610-012)"@en ;
    dcterms:description "This inscription predates the temple by many centuries. It is said to belong to the Mānadeva period back in the 5th century. As most of the text of the inscription has been damaged, its content is unclear. The inscription was installed after aśivaliṅgawas established in the name of a person’s son who died in his childhood."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/27fefdad-0e5e-407b-95af-fb8a2401dcc9> ;
