<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/27fefdad-0e5e-407b-95af-fb8a2401dcc9_4> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Offering the bell (PPK0610-008)"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Prince Trailokya, King Surendra’s son, established the Trailokyeśvara Mahādeva (PPK0610-007) in the name of his mother Trailokyarājyalakṣmī and also offered a bell to the temple. Born in 1847 CE, Prince Trailokya died in 1878 CE while his father was still the king."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/27fefdad-0e5e-407b-95af-fb8a2401dcc9> ;
