<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/27fefdad-0e5e-407b-95af-fb8a2401dcc9_5> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Offering the bell (PPK0610-010)"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Surendra’s father King Rājendra Vikrama offered a bell (PPK0610-010) to the Rājendreśvara Mandira (PPK0610-009) that produced a ‘beautiful sound’. He was in prison when he made the offering. With the intent to retake the throne, the dethroned King Rājendra and his army moved to the capital in 1847 CE but were defeated by Prime Minister Jaṅga Bahādura’s army in the Battle of Alau. He was imprisoned in Bhaktapur since then and passed away in incarceration in 1881 CE."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/27fefdad-0e5e-407b-95af-fb8a2401dcc9> ;
    rdfs:comment "Surendra’s father King Rājendra Vikrama offered a bell (PPK0610-010) to the Rājendreśvara Mandira (PPK0610-009) that produced a ‘beautiful sound’. He was in prison when he made the offering. With the intent to retake the throne, the dethroned King Rājendra and his army moved to the capital in 1847 CE but were defeated by Prime Minister Jaṅga Bahādura’s army in the Battle of Alau. He was imprisoned in Bhaktapur since then and passed away in incarceration in 1881 CE."@en ;
