<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/28cc6491-dcc2-4cdd-9ee3-4aac928db2d8_1> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Damage caused by the 1934 CE earthquake and rebuilding"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Following the devastating earthquakes of 1934 CE, the Vaṃśeśvara Mahādeva temple suffered a collapse. Prior to this unfortunate event, the temple stood as a grand three-tiered structure. However, in the process of reconstruction that ensued after the earthquakes, the temple was restored with its upper tiers replaced by a domed top (see 'description' and 'historical photos' above)."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/28cc6491-dcc2-4cdd-9ee3-4aac928db2d8> ;
    rdfs:comment "Following the devastating earthquakes of 1934 CE, the Vaṃśeśvara Mahādeva temple suffered a collapse. Prior to this unfortunate event, the temple stood as a grand three-tiered structure. However, in the process of reconstruction that ensued after the earthquakes, the temple was restored with its upper tiers replaced by a domed top (see 'description' and 'historical photos' above)."@en ;
