<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/28e34398-8dda-11ea-8e56-0242ac130005_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Renovation and land donation"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Thākusiṅ and Toyuṣvā Thakunī a couple from nearby Valā Ṭola financed the restoration of the Phalcā. Oneropanīland of Jhurabu was donated to theguṭhī. The inscription directs theguṭhīto light three oil lamps on the day when the chariot of the deity stops in Gāḥbāhāḥ. It also encourages them to save some money every year to fund its potential reconstruction."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/28e34398-8dda-11ea-8e56-0242ac130005> ;
