<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/293c1896-a3bb-454a-8fe9-b56ebfadc51c_13> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:TransferOfCustody ;
    rdfs:label "Endowment of land"@en ;
    dcterms:description "This inscription is also located on the wall at the north-eastern corner of the temple. Due to the lack of clarity in the letters, it is difficult to fully comprehend the inscription's details. The date mentioned on it is also erased and cannot be ascertained. Upon a careful reading of the inscription, it can be understood that there are mentions of offering pañcāmṛta to Mahādeva on the new moon day of Śrāvaṇa, that Kāśīrāma established endowments in various locations in the temple's name, and that various worship methods are described."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/293c1896-a3bb-454a-8fe9-b56ebfadc51c> ;
    rdfs:comment "This inscription is also located on the wall at the north-eastern corner of the temple. Due to the lack of clarity in the letters, it is difficult to fully comprehend the inscription's details. The date mentioned on it is also erased and cannot be ascertained. Upon a careful reading of the inscription, it can be understood that there are mentions of offering pañcāmṛta to Mahādeva on the new moon day of Śrāvaṇa, that Kāśīrāma established endowments in various locations in the temple's name, and that various worship methods are described."@en ;
