        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Unknown event"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Numerous inscriptions are affixed to the wall at the north-eastern corner of the temple. Among these, one inscription is dated 1804 CE (SS 1725). On the upper part of the inscription, figures of the Trident, the Moon, and the Sun can be seen, while the lower part features the carved image of a donor couple. As the inscription has faded, the details contained within it are not clear."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/293c1896-a3bb-454a-8fe9-b56ebfadc51c> ;
