        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Renovation of upper floor"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The topmost roof of the temple consists of gold-gilded brass plates and a cast metal pinnacle. This roof was installed during the reign of Raṇabahādura Śāha in 1830 CE (SS 1751). This detail is found in the inscription located on the roof."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/293c1896-a3bb-454a-8fe9-b56ebfadc51c> ;
