<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/2a0b1750-ee3e-11e9-8649-0242ac130002_1> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Reconstruction of the Pāṭī"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Kumārī Pāṭī was reconstructed with the help of the Rotary Club Lalitpur and the local residents, who together donated a sum of 550,000 NRS. The inauguration day was the 31st of Jyeṣṭha 2060 VS. Before the reconstruction, the building was severely dilapidated and had collapsed in places. A concrete structure which imitates traditional carving forms was selected as the replacement. 16 years later, some of the local residents have expressed a wish that the building included more traditional elements (such as wood carvings) so as to give it more traditional look."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/2a0b1750-ee3e-11e9-8649-0242ac130002> ;
    rdfs:comment "Kumārī Pāṭī was reconstructed with the help of the Rotary Club Lalitpur and the local residents, who together donated a sum of 550,000 NRS. The inauguration day was the 31st of Jyeṣṭha 2060 VS. Before the reconstruction, the building was severely dilapidated and had collapsed in places. A concrete structure which imitates traditional carving forms was selected as the replacement. 16 years later, some of the local residents have expressed a wish that the building included more traditional elements (such as wood carvings) so as to give it more traditional look."@en ;
