    rdfs:label "Offering of a Moharamālā"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Amoharamālā(jewellery made with coins) was offered to Bāghabhairava by a family living in Kirtipur. The family members, whose names can be deciphered from the readable part of the inscription, are: Tiyogī, Lumayi, Helamayi, Yogā, Mālasiṃha and Harṣavī."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/2a1ca80c-8b69-43a0-ab19-ac6b126986ee> ;
