    rdfs:label "Theft of metal cover of Jyotirliṅgeśvara"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Thepañcamukhīśivaliṅga, a ceremonial hollow cover made of gilt copper in the shape of aśivaliṅgawith five figures of Lord Śiva’s face embossed on it, was stolen from the priest’s own house. The cover that is taken around the town on a palanquin has not been recovered so far. A replacement has been made for the procession now."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/2a5fe4da-69eb-426c-af0d-99672f6885f9> ;
