    rdfs:label "Repair of golden pinnacle and offering struts"@en ;
    dcterms:description "During the reign of King Jagajjaya Malla, Devarāma Bhāro, a resident of  the Yapāta Ṭola in Sankhu, along with his three sons Latneśvara Bhāro, Dhaneśvara Bhāro and Vireśvara Bhāro, repaired the golden finial of the Temple. On the same occasion, they also offered struts to the Temple."@en ;
