<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/2a8e92e4-ffb7-11e9-8f3c-0242ac130002_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Construction of Sataḥ"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Cakrasiṃha Bābu (a son of Bhīmālakṣmī who married the daughter of King Siddhinarasiṃha Malla) and his four sons Pratāpasiṃha Bābu, Narasiṃha Bābu, Jayabhadrasiṃha Bābu and Ānandasiṃha Bābu commissioned this Sataḥ and established the statue of Lakṣmīnārāyaṇa. They also performed a fire ritual, established aguṭhi,and had a golden pinnacle fixed upon the Sataḥ. King Yoganarendra Malla was present at the inaugural ceremony."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/2a8e92e4-ffb7-11e9-8f3c-0242ac130002> ;
    rdfs:comment "Cakrasiṃha Bābu (a son of Bhīmālakṣmī who married the daughter of King Siddhinarasiṃha Malla) and his four sons Pratāpasiṃha Bābu, Narasiṃha Bābu, Jayabhadrasiṃha Bābu and Ānandasiṃha Bābu commissioned this Sataḥ and established the statue of Lakṣmīnārāyaṇa. They also performed a fire ritual, established aguṭhi,and had a golden pinnacle fixed upon the Sataḥ. King Yoganarendra Malla was present at the inaugural ceremony."@en ;
