<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/2b614d26-2bde-455e-97bc-35eba55d7faf_4> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Reconstruction of the temple"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The temple was reconstructed under the supervision of the Department of Archaeology following the damages sustained by the temple in the 2015 earthquakes. In the course of dismantling the temple for reconstruction, bricks with the inscription ‘Śrī3 Candra’ were recovered from the temple’s foundation. This suggests that the temple was built during the reign of Prime Minister Candra Śamśera (1901-1929 CE)."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/2b614d26-2bde-455e-97bc-35eba55d7faf> ;
    rdfs:comment "The temple was reconstructed under the supervision of the Department of Archaeology following the damages sustained by the temple in the 2015 earthquakes. In the course of dismantling the temple for reconstruction, bricks with the inscription ‘Śrī3 Candra’ were recovered from the temple’s foundation. This suggests that the temple was built during the reign of Prime Minister Candra Śamśera (1901-1929 CE)."@en ;
