<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/2c4ce775-72ec-4621-809f-77c137e58dfc_7> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Construction of a dabū (elevated public platform)"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Lohokāra …, his wife Malakṣmī, daughters Bhimalakṣmī and Daśalaksṃī, and other family members constructed thedabūin memory of the main donor’s deceased father Lakṣmīdhara (text: Lachimidhara) and mother. The name of the donor is illegible due to surface chipping. He was, however, clearly a stone sculptor (lohokāra). He also established a fund of 101 mohararupaīyā̃ from which to perform the anniversary ritual of thedabū."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/2c4ce775-72ec-4621-809f-77c137e58dfc> ;
    rdfs:comment "Lohokāra …, his wife Malakṣmī, daughters Bhimalakṣmī and Daśalaksṃī, and other family members constructed thedabūin memory of the main donor’s deceased father Lakṣmīdhara (text: Lachimidhara) and mother. The name of the donor is illegible due to surface chipping. He was, however, clearly a stone sculptor (lohokāra). He also established a fund of 101 mohararupaīyā̃ from which to perform the anniversary ritual of thedabū."@en ;
