        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Installation of a stone pillar (object number KAT0830-011)"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The stone pillar (dharmastambha) in front of the Temple was inaugurated by Guru Kaviprasāda and Komalaprasāda Gautama as part of their larger campaign of flourishing Krisnaism in Nepal and beyond. Inscriptions can be found on the pillar's eastern, western, and southern faces."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/2c4ce775-72ec-4621-809f-77c137e58dfc> ;
