<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/2c57e6c8-e8cb-11e9-b125-0242ac130002_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Construction of the phalcā"@en ;
    dcterms:description "A stone inscription is attached to the eastern wall of the Bhailaḥ Phalcā which provides information about its construction in 1871 CE (NS 991). According to the inscription, thephalcāwas built by Rāma Prajāpati Thakura and his family in the name of his late parents. Aguṭhīwas established at the same time, and land was donated to fund the organisation of annual rituals. As of 2018, theguṭhīno longer exists. Some of the rituals have therefore also come to an end.One can find images of the donors at the bottom of the inscription and a Bhairava flanked by two deities above it. Bhairava is shown standing in theālīḍhaposture with four arms; holding akhaḍgaand akhaṭvāṁka in his upper two hands."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/2c57e6c8-e8cb-11e9-b125-0242ac130002> ;
    rdfs:comment "A stone inscription is attached to the eastern wall of the Bhailaḥ Phalcā which provides information about its construction in 1871 CE (NS 991). According to the inscription, thephalcāwas built by Rāma Prajāpati Thakura and his family in the name of his late parents. Aguṭhīwas established at the same time, and land was donated to fund the organisation of annual rituals. As of 2018, theguṭhīno longer exists. Some of the rituals have therefore also come to an end.One can find images of the donors at the bottom of the inscription and a Bhairava flanked by two deities above it. Bhairava is shown standing in theālīḍhaposture with four arms; holding akhaḍgaand akhaṭvāṁka in his upper two hands."@en ;
