<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/2da0a89a-f458-4203-99cf-d119819a48bd_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Installation of stone lions flanking the main entrance of the Pīṭha"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The earliest inscription from the Pīṭha premises records the installation of two guardian stone lions by theguthis of Bhāro and Bhābos of Balambu. Due to the poor condition of the inscription, the date cannot be ascertained although the first digit can be read as '8'. As the inscription mentions the name of the king as Mahīndra Malla, it is certain that the event took place in between his reigning years NS 829 (1709 CE) and NS 835 (1715 CE) (Burleigh 1976, 56)."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/2da0a89a-f458-4203-99cf-d119819a48bd> ;
    rdfs:comment "The earliest inscription from the Pīṭha premises records the installation of two guardian stone lions by theguthis of Bhāro and Bhābos of Balambu. Due to the poor condition of the inscription, the date cannot be ascertained although the first digit can be read as '8'. As the inscription mentions the name of the king as Mahīndra Malla, it is certain that the event took place in between his reigning years NS 829 (1709 CE) and NS 835 (1715 CE) (Burleigh 1976, 56)."@en ;
