<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/2db1bbc0-f156-42ec-965c-e5cc9adc8981_1> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Renovation"@en ;
    dcterms:description "According to local residents, the Phalcā had been renovated by the Pradhāna Pañca, Māndāsa Śreṣṭha in 1973. At that time, the Phalcā had not been in its \"traditional\" form. The floor and the wall were built using cement and bricks. This way, the Phalcā could not retain its previous appearance."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/2db1bbc0-f156-42ec-965c-e5cc9adc8981> ;
    rdfs:comment "According to local residents, the Phalcā had been renovated by the Pradhāna Pañca, Māndāsa Śreṣṭha in 1973. At that time, the Phalcā had not been in its \"traditional\" form. The floor and the wall were built using cement and bricks. This way, the Phalcā could not retain its previous appearance."@en ;
