<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/2dc687d3-753b-421c-802c-e9f74a427496_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:TransferOfCustody ;
    rdfs:label "Initial construction"@en ;
    dcterms:description "King Pratapa Malla initiated the erection of the Hanumān statue upon the pillar. An accompanying inscription commemorated the occasion, emphasizing the statue's role in granting victory in battles and protecting homes. This inscription is edited in G. Vajrācārya (VS 2033, pp. 224-225). Vajrācārya noted that the inscription was engraved on the statue's pedestal during his site documentation. As of February 2023, the pedestal has been painted over, obscuring all traces of the inscription."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/2dc687d3-753b-421c-802c-e9f74a427496> ;
    rdfs:comment "King Pratapa Malla initiated the erection of the Hanumān statue upon the pillar. An accompanying inscription commemorated the occasion, emphasizing the statue's role in granting victory in battles and protecting homes. This inscription is edited in G. Vajrācārya (VS 2033, pp. 224-225). Vajrācārya noted that the inscription was engraved on the statue's pedestal during his site documentation. As of February 2023, the pedestal has been painted over, obscuring all traces of the inscription."@en ;
