<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/2e39f1d1-81c3-4ead-838b-b3da76f95dc8_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Construction of the temple"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Jītajaṅga Rāṇā built the temple by establishing Jītajaṅgaprakāśeśvara, aśivaliṅganamed after himself, in the sanctum. He also established two additionalśivaliṅgas with the name Suprakāśeśvara. These twośivaliṅgas are probably the ones established as Suprakāśeśvarathat flank Jītajaṅgaprakāśeśvara from the north and south. Besides the main threeśivaliṅgas, there are 12 otherśivaliṅgas inside the temple. He also donated 306ropanīs of land to set up a trust for the management of daily and periodic worship at the temple. Jītajaṅga also built a rest house (sataḥ) west of the temple. In the inscription that records these events, Jītajaṅga eulogizes his ancestors while also inscribing their names starting from Abhirāma Kũvara to his father Jaṅga Bahādura Rāṇā."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/2e39f1d1-81c3-4ead-838b-b3da76f95dc8> ;
    rdfs:comment "Jītajaṅga Rāṇā built the temple by establishing Jītajaṅgaprakāśeśvara, aśivaliṅganamed after himself, in the sanctum. He also established two additionalśivaliṅgas with the name Suprakāśeśvara. These twośivaliṅgas are probably the ones established as Suprakāśeśvarathat flank Jītajaṅgaprakāśeśvara from the north and south. Besides the main threeśivaliṅgas, there are 12 otherśivaliṅgas inside the temple. He also donated 306ropanīs of land to set up a trust for the management of daily and periodic worship at the temple. Jītajaṅga also built a rest house (sataḥ) west of the temple. In the inscription that records these events, Jītajaṅga eulogizes his ancestors while also inscribing their names starting from Abhirāma Kũvara to his father Jaṅga Bahādura Rāṇā."@en ;
