        hg:RitualEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Renovation of the Nyāgaḥmaṇi caityas"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The surviving threecaityas of Nyāgaḥmaṇi were renovated with donations collected from the devotees. A statue of Amoghasiddhi was also established south of thecaityas. The statue was jointly inaugurated by Ven. Bhaddiya Mahāsthavira, Sri Lankan Ambassador W. M. Senevirathna, and Puṇya Śākya (President of Jñānamālā Bhajana Khalaḥ, Svayambhū)."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/2fa81a11-e4b0-4c7b-bedd-ed1573e4e4f0> ;
    rdfs:comment "The surviving threecaityas of Nyāgaḥmaṇi were renovated with donations collected from the devotees. A statue of Amoghasiddhi was also established south of thecaityas. The statue was jointly inaugurated by Ven. Bhaddiya Mahāsthavira, Sri Lankan Ambassador W. M. Senevirathna, and Puṇya Śākya (President of Jñānamālā Bhajana Khalaḥ, Svayambhū)."@en ;
