<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/2fea6eaa-1b5f-43ca-96fd-9baad7fce137_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Renovation of Hiti and pond next to it and prohibition of soap at Hiti"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Lack of care and renovations for a long period had left both the Hiti and pond next to it shrouded in bushes. In 2021 CE, the Kirtipur Municipality reconstructed both monuments. At the same time, Icchā Maharjana, a local resident, sponsored the statue of Viṣṇu to fill up the empty niche in memory of his deceased mother. As there are fishes farmed in the water pond, the use of soap for doing laundry or bathing at the Hiti is now prohibited."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/2fea6eaa-1b5f-43ca-96fd-9baad7fce137> ;
    rdfs:comment "Lack of care and renovations for a long period had left both the Hiti and pond next to it shrouded in bushes. In 2021 CE, the Kirtipur Municipality reconstructed both monuments. At the same time, Icchā Maharjana, a local resident, sponsored the statue of Viṣṇu to fill up the empty niche in memory of his deceased mother. As there are fishes farmed in the water pond, the use of soap for doing laundry or bathing at the Hiti is now prohibited."@en ;
