<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/307d6756-386b-4d59-bf7a-5f76a6bf7c79_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Renovation of the pond"@en ;
    dcterms:description "As the pond constructed for Sarveśvara Mahādeva had fallen into disrepair, during the reign of King Gīrvāṇayuddhavikrama Śāha, four brothers Amatya Hanumanta Siṁha Bhāro, Bhājudhana Siṁha, Sadāśiva Siṁha, and Lakṣmīnarasiṁha, residing in Dhaugala Ṭola, Lalitpur, jointly undertook its restoration. The responsibility of overseeing this work was entrusted to Daivajña Sadāśiva and other residents of Calakhu Ṭola. They also installed a goldenhitiand a golden statue of Umāmaheśvara. It is likely that they adorned thehiti’sspout and the Umāmaheśvara statue with sheets of gilded copper."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/307d6756-386b-4d59-bf7a-5f76a6bf7c79> ;
    rdfs:comment "As the pond constructed for Sarveśvara Mahādeva had fallen into disrepair, during the reign of King Gīrvāṇayuddhavikrama Śāha, four brothers Amatya Hanumanta Siṁha Bhāro, Bhājudhana Siṁha, Sadāśiva Siṁha, and Lakṣmīnarasiṁha, residing in Dhaugala Ṭola, Lalitpur, jointly undertook its restoration. The responsibility of overseeing this work was entrusted to Daivajña Sadāśiva and other residents of Calakhu Ṭola. They also installed a goldenhitiand a golden statue of Umāmaheśvara. It is likely that they adorned thehiti’sspout and the Umāmaheśvara statue with sheets of gilded copper."@en ;
