<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/3129a121-de9f-4067-912a-e8f44549dd05_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Unclear"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The inscription dating back to 1613 CE (NS 733), located to the northeast of the temple, is unrelated to the temple itself. It precedes the temple's construction by a minimum of two centuries, likely originating from another structure but later placed at this site. Due to significant erosion, the complete understanding of its content remains elusive. The inscription makes reference to the establishment of an oil-related trust, indicating that a benefactor likely erected a statue or temple and instituted a trust for the purpose of illuminating oil lamps at the site."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/3129a121-de9f-4067-912a-e8f44549dd05> ;
    rdfs:comment "The inscription dating back to 1613 CE (NS 733), located to the northeast of the temple, is unrelated to the temple itself. It precedes the temple's construction by a minimum of two centuries, likely originating from another structure but later placed at this site. Due to significant erosion, the complete understanding of its content remains elusive. The inscription makes reference to the establishment of an oil-related trust, indicating that a benefactor likely erected a statue or temple and instituted a trust for the purpose of illuminating oil lamps at the site."@en ;
