<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/313ebade-3b32-4491-845d-fe5520f8622c_2> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Blood seen on the statue"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Special rituals for auspiciousness were performed by sacrificing two he-goats after blood was seen on the Jayavāgīśvarī statue. The sacrifices were probably made at the Navadurgā shrine, as Jayavāgīśvarī does not accept animal sacrifices. A few days later, blood was seen on the statue again on the 2nd of the dark fortnight of Pauṣa. A fire oblation was performed to remove the defilement caused by the blood this time."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/313ebade-3b32-4491-845d-fe5520f8622c> ;
    rdfs:comment "Special rituals for auspiciousness were performed by sacrificing two he-goats after blood was seen on the Jayavāgīśvarī statue. The sacrifices were probably made at the Navadurgā shrine, as Jayavāgīśvarī does not accept animal sacrifices. A few days later, blood was seen on the statue again on the 2nd of the dark fortnight of Pauṣa. A fire oblation was performed to remove the defilement caused by the blood this time."@en ;
