<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/32b21dd4-78f4-49a4-89ef-cec4b28c0f6b_1> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Endowment of lands"@en ;
    dcterms:description "An extensive area of over 45ropanīs of land was endowed to set up a trust (guthi) responsible for conducting various rituals at the temple. The trust included Mānandhara (text: Manaṃdhra) Puna, Kṛṣṇa, Hṛdayasiṃha, Viṣṇusiṃha, and Harisiṃ as members. The income from the land was to be used for sacrificing a buffalo a day ahead ofPiśācaCaturdaśī, the 14th of the dark fortnight of Caitra, and lighting five sets of lamps at the Kvāthachẽ Āgaṃ. Additionally, the funds were utilized for the worship of Vatsalā on the new moon day of Caitra. Likewise, the trust was also responsible for sending the set of five nectars (pañcāmṛta) to Buṅgadyaḥ on the day of the deity’s ritual bathing (nhavaṃ), the 1st of the dark fortnight of Vaiśākha. The original donation deed was damaged in a fire and was copied into a new donation deed."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/32b21dd4-78f4-49a4-89ef-cec4b28c0f6b> ;
    rdfs:comment "An extensive area of over 45ropanīs of land was endowed to set up a trust (guthi) responsible for conducting various rituals at the temple. The trust included Mānandhara (text: Manaṃdhra) Puna, Kṛṣṇa, Hṛdayasiṃha, Viṣṇusiṃha, and Harisiṃ as members. The income from the land was to be used for sacrificing a buffalo a day ahead ofPiśācaCaturdaśī, the 14th of the dark fortnight of Caitra, and lighting five sets of lamps at the Kvāthachẽ Āgaṃ. Additionally, the funds were utilized for the worship of Vatsalā on the new moon day of Caitra. Likewise, the trust was also responsible for sending the set of five nectars (pañcāmṛta) to Buṅgadyaḥ on the day of the deity’s ritual bathing (nhavaṃ), the 1st of the dark fortnight of Vaiśākha. The original donation deed was damaged in a fire and was copied into a new donation deed."@en ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/agent/antigravity_agent> ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/activity/heritagegraph_kg_construction> ;
    hg:eventIndex 1 ;
    hg:extractionMethod "source_table" ;
    hg:isEventOf <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/32b21dd4-78f4-49a4-89ef-cec4b28c0f6b> .

<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/32b21dd4-78f4-49a4-89ef-cec4b28c0f6b_2> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Offering horn of wild water buffalo"@en ;
    dcterms:description "King Raṇabahādura Śāha offered three horns of wildarnābuffaloes for fermented beer (thvã) to be poured from it on to the stoneyantrarevered as Goddess Vatsalā on the new moon day of Caitra. Gold sheets were wrapped around the horns back then."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/32b21dd4-78f4-49a4-89ef-cec4b28c0f6b> ;
    rdfs:comment "King Raṇabahādura Śāha offered three horns of wildarnābuffaloes for fermented beer (thvã) to be poured from it on to the stoneyantrarevered as Goddess Vatsalā on the new moon day of Caitra. Gold sheets were wrapped around the horns back then."@en ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/agent/antigravity_agent> ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/activity/heritagegraph_kg_construction> ;
    hg:eventIndex 2 ;
    hg:extractionMethod "source_table" ;
    hg:isEventOf <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/32b21dd4-78f4-49a4-89ef-cec4b28c0f6b> .

<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/32b21dd4-78f4-49a4-89ef-cec4b28c0f6b_3> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:TransferOfCustody ;
    rdfs:label "Lālamohara by Raṇabahādura Śāha for Sindūra Guṭhī"@en ;
    dcterms:description "King Raṇabahādura Śāha, through a royal decree with a red seal (lālamohara), granted authorization to a trust named the Sindūra Guthi, allowing it to operate in accordance with the established tradition. King Jayaprakāśa Malla had endowed 120ropanīs of land for the trust of Goddess Vatsalā. Thelālamoharainstructed the trust members to perform thepañcopacāraworship, which involved offering a buffalo sacrifice to Vatsalā onPiśācaCaturdaśī, the 14th of the dark fortnight of Caitra. Additionally, during the same occasion, the horns of the wildarnābuffaloes were to be blown. Furthermore, the royal decree made the trust responsible for organizing thesindūrajātrāof Vatsalā on the new moon day of Caitra. Sixdhārnīs (1dhārnī= 2.39 kgs) of vermillion powder (sindūra) were required for the procession. Devotees participated the procession by throwing thesindūrapowder in the air and at each other, creating a vibrant atmosphere."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/32b21dd4-78f4-49a4-89ef-cec4b28c0f6b> ;
    rdfs:comment "King Raṇabahādura Śāha, through a royal decree with a red seal (lālamohara), granted authorization to a trust named the Sindūra Guthi, allowing it to operate in accordance with the established tradition. King Jayaprakāśa Malla had endowed 120ropanīs of land for the trust of Goddess Vatsalā. Thelālamoharainstructed the trust members to perform thepañcopacāraworship, which involved offering a buffalo sacrifice to Vatsalā onPiśācaCaturdaśī, the 14th of the dark fortnight of Caitra. Additionally, during the same occasion, the horns of the wildarnābuffaloes were to be blown. Furthermore, the royal decree made the trust responsible for organizing thesindūrajātrāof Vatsalā on the new moon day of Caitra. Sixdhārnīs (1dhārnī= 2.39 kgs) of vermillion powder (sindūra) were required for the procession. Devotees participated the procession by throwing thesindūrapowder in the air and at each other, creating a vibrant atmosphere."@en ;
