<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/32b21dd4-78f4-49a4-89ef-cec4b28c0f6b_7> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Replacing the roof with brass plates?"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The content of the inscription embossed on the temple's eaves board poses some challenges. It involves the names of Jaṅga Bahādura Rāṇā and his wife Siddhigajendralakṣmī, who happened to be the younger sister of his first wife. Following the passing of his first wife, Jaṅga Bahādura proposed marriage to Siddhigajendralakṣmī, but her father declined the proposal and instead married her to another man. After Jaṅga Bahādura took the office of the prime minister, he took Siddhigajendralakṣmī as his wife forcibly but paid her husband the compensation (P. Rāja VS 2073, p.57)."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/32b21dd4-78f4-49a4-89ef-cec4b28c0f6b> ;
    rdfs:comment "The content of the inscription embossed on the temple's eaves board poses some challenges. It involves the names of Jaṅga Bahādura Rāṇā and his wife Siddhigajendralakṣmī, who happened to be the younger sister of his first wife. Following the passing of his first wife, Jaṅga Bahādura proposed marriage to Siddhigajendralakṣmī, but her father declined the proposal and instead married her to another man. After Jaṅga Bahādura took the office of the prime minister, he took Siddhigajendralakṣmī as his wife forcibly but paid her husband the compensation (P. Rāja VS 2073, p.57)."@en ;
