<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/34697056-9775-466d-b46d-c83f874b93d3_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:ConditionAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Unknown event"@en ;
    dcterms:description "This inscription is heavily eroded, making it undecipherable. Thus, its contents remain obscure. However, with the carvings of a jagged-edged knife (kartṛ) and a skull cup (kapālapātra), the implements of Bhairava, on its topmost part, the inscription appears to belong to the late-medieval period. The inscription was already in an unreadable shape in 1975 CE when D. Vajrācārya and Ṭ. Śreṣṭha documented the inscriptions from Nuwakot (VS 2032, first part, p. 7)."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/34697056-9775-466d-b46d-c83f874b93d3> ;
    rdfs:comment "This inscription is heavily eroded, making it undecipherable. Thus, its contents remain obscure. However, with the carvings of a jagged-edged knife (kartṛ) and a skull cup (kapālapātra), the implements of Bhairava, on its topmost part, the inscription appears to belong to the late-medieval period. The inscription was already in an unreadable shape in 1975 CE when D. Vajrācārya and Ṭ. Śreṣṭha documented the inscriptions from Nuwakot (VS 2032, first part, p. 7)."@en ;
