<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/34d3a0bc-bf6d-489e-b2a4-9bf09d771740_4> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Excavation in front of the dyaḥchẽ"@en ;
    dcterms:description "To investigate the antiquity of the Manamāneśvarī site, the Department of Archaeology, led by S.B. Deo, conducted excavations in the vacant area north of thedyaḥchẽin 1965 CE. The excavations yielded artifacts such as Paśupati coins, stone seals with the imprint of a cow and calf from the Aṃśuvarmā period, and earthenware from the pre-Lichhavi period. These findings confirm that the Manamāneśvarī site existed as early as the Lichhavi period."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/34d3a0bc-bf6d-489e-b2a4-9bf09d771740> ;
    rdfs:comment "To investigate the antiquity of the Manamāneśvarī site, the Department of Archaeology, led by S.B. Deo, conducted excavations in the vacant area north of thedyaḥchẽin 1965 CE. The excavations yielded artifacts such as Paśupati coins, stone seals with the imprint of a cow and calf from the Aṃśuvarmā period, and earthenware from the pre-Lichhavi period. These findings confirm that the Manamāneśvarī site existed as early as the Lichhavi period."@en ;
