<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/3527c75f-8262-4a09-802b-b3188ee27d40_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:TransferOfCustody ;
    rdfs:label "Initial construction of the Temple and land endowment"@en ;
    dcterms:description "As stated in the 'description' above, Ḍiṭṭhā Dharma Siṃha and his younger brother Premanārāyaṇa Siṃha from the Jaisīdevala Ṭola constructed the Temple, along with rest houses (caugharā sataḥ) on all four sides (surrounding the Temple in the centre), a garden, and a pond. Over 121ropanīsof land were endowed for Temple's annual and periodic rituals, as well as other cultural activities."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/3527c75f-8262-4a09-802b-b3188ee27d40> ;
    rdfs:comment "As stated in the 'description' above, Ḍiṭṭhā Dharma Siṃha and his younger brother Premanārāyaṇa Siṃha from the Jaisīdevala Ṭola constructed the Temple, along with rest houses (caugharā sataḥ) on all four sides (surrounding the Temple in the centre), a garden, and a pond. Over 121ropanīsof land were endowed for Temple's annual and periodic rituals, as well as other cultural activities."@en ;
