<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/359211db-32de-4942-9808-1023db60054c_1> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Installation of pillar 003"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The west and north sides of the pillar are inscribed. The inscription to the west contains 6 lines in Nāgarī script. It mentions the date Śake 1256 (1334 CE). The inscription to the north contains 5 lines, no date but bears the name Thāpā and the mention of a son (putra)."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/359211db-32de-4942-9808-1023db60054c> ;
    rdfs:comment "The west and north sides of the pillar are inscribed. The inscription to the west contains 6 lines in Nāgarī script. It mentions the date Śake 1256 (1334 CE). The inscription to the north contains 5 lines, no date but bears the name Thāpā and the mention of a son (putra)."@en ;
