<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/359211db-32de-4942-9808-1023db60054c_2> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Installation of pillar 004"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The west and north sides of the pillar are inscribed. The inscription to the west contains 5 lines in Nāgarī script. It mentions the date Śake 1256 (1334 CE). The inscription to the north contains 5 lines and no date.D. R.Sharma(2012: p. 101) reads the inscription as follow:Oṁ swosti śri sāke 1256 ghi a putra Bāmu Khadgā ko bira khaṃtranslated as:Hail, saka 1256 (1334 A.D.) this is the memorial pillar of Bāmu Khadgā"@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/359211db-32de-4942-9808-1023db60054c> ;
    rdfs:comment "The west and north sides of the pillar are inscribed. The inscription to the west contains 5 lines in Nāgarī script. It mentions the date Śake 1256 (1334 CE). The inscription to the north contains 5 lines and no date.D. R.Sharma(2012: p. 101) reads the inscription as follow:Oṁ swosti śri sāke 1256 ghi a putra Bāmu Khadgā ko bira khaṃtranslated as:Hail, saka 1256 (1334 A.D.) this is the memorial pillar of Bāmu Khadgā"@en ;
