<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/3668d45a-f899-11e9-8649-0242ac130002_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Yaḥsi kā vanegu"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The presentyaḥsipole was brought from Nālā in 1979 on March 27th. One member from each family of Sunāguthi went to collect theyaḥsi. The event took place because the formeryaḥsibroke. It was said to be have been installed in the year 1946 CE. The pole was carried for three days in 1979, from Sunday March 25th to Tuesday March 27th.Informant: Mr. Ram Sundar Maharjan (participant of the event Yaḥsi kā vanegu in 1979)"@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/3668d45a-f899-11e9-8649-0242ac130002> ;
    rdfs:comment "The presentyaḥsipole was brought from Nālā in 1979 on March 27th. One member from each family of Sunāguthi went to collect theyaḥsi. The event took place because the formeryaḥsibroke. It was said to be have been installed in the year 1946 CE. The pole was carried for three days in 1979, from Sunday March 25th to Tuesday March 27th.Informant: Mr. Ram Sundar Maharjan (participant of the event Yaḥsi kā vanegu in 1979)"@en ;
