<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/3753ac0e-dc29-4c1f-b326-edb307e831d8_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Enshrinement ;
    rdfs:label "Establishment of the bāhāḥ"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Harṣaratna Vajrācārya established thebāhāḥin 1876 CE (VS 1933) together with his son, Tejaratna Vajrācārya, and with contributions from his wife, Harṣalakṣmī, and other family members. It was constructed on two adjacent plots of land. One plot had been used by Harṣaratna's ancestor, Samaju Āḥju. The other, granted to Bhājuvīra Prajāpatī of Jyāthā Ṭola, Khyāḥ Bāhāḥ in Kathmandu bylālamohara(royal decree), was purchased by Harṣaratna. Combining these two plots, Harṣaratna built thebāhāḥ. Following its construction, he installed thetriratna(Akṣobhya, Prajñāpāramitā, and Lokeśvara), acaitya, and images of Meṣasamvara, Vajrapāṇi, Mahāmañjuśrī, and Bhīmasena. Harṣaratna and Harṣalakṣmī also celebrated theirbhīmarathārohaṇa(jaṃko), an old-age ritual, at this time. Land was endowed to thebāhāḥas a religious trust to support its annual rituals."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/3753ac0e-dc29-4c1f-b326-edb307e831d8> ;
    rdfs:comment "Harṣaratna Vajrācārya established thebāhāḥin 1876 CE (VS 1933) together with his son, Tejaratna Vajrācārya, and with contributions from his wife, Harṣalakṣmī, and other family members. It was constructed on two adjacent plots of land. One plot had been used by Harṣaratna's ancestor, Samaju Āḥju. The other, granted to Bhājuvīra Prajāpatī of Jyāthā Ṭola, Khyāḥ Bāhāḥ in Kathmandu bylālamohara(royal decree), was purchased by Harṣaratna. Combining these two plots, Harṣaratna built thebāhāḥ. Following its construction, he installed thetriratna(Akṣobhya, Prajñāpāramitā, and Lokeśvara), acaitya, and images of Meṣasamvara, Vajrapāṇi, Mahāmañjuśrī, and Bhīmasena. Harṣaratna and Harṣalakṣmī also celebrated theirbhīmarathārohaṇa(jaṃko), an old-age ritual, at this time. Land was endowed to thebāhāḥas a religious trust to support its annual rituals."@en ;
