<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/3753ac0e-dc29-4c1f-b326-edb307e831d8_1> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Installation of a stone inscription"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Jyotiratna Vajrācārya reinstated daily worship and other religious practices after thebāhāḥ,built by his grandfather Harṣaratna and father Tejaratna Vajrācārya, as the rituals at the monastery were not regularly performed. He also installed a commemorative stone inscription. Because of his systematic organization and management, thebāhāḥbecame known as Jyotiyā Bāhāḥ (Jyoti'sbāhāḥ), after him."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/3753ac0e-dc29-4c1f-b326-edb307e831d8> ;
    rdfs:comment "Jyotiratna Vajrācārya reinstated daily worship and other religious practices after thebāhāḥ,built by his grandfather Harṣaratna and father Tejaratna Vajrācārya, as the rituals at the monastery were not regularly performed. He also installed a commemorative stone inscription. Because of his systematic organization and management, thebāhāḥbecame known as Jyotiyā Bāhāḥ (Jyoti'sbāhāḥ), after him."@en ;
