<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/37d714e8-29e1-44ec-a474-ab9eb80403c1_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Construction of Jaḥdhuṃhiti"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The Jaḥdhuṃ near the Sataḥ was constructed by Mahāpātra Purandarasiṃhadeva, a powerful local functionary of Patan during the late Malla period. He also formed a community-based trust with the responsibility of filling water in the Jaḥdhuṃ. The members of the trust were required to keep the Jaḥdhuṃ full as long as the statue of Buṅgadyaḥ remained in the temple at Taḥ Bāhāḥ. Every year on the 1stsolar day of Māgha, the Jaḥdhuṃ was worshipped and whitewashed. The trust distributed puffed rice (syāḥbaji), fermented rice beer (thvã), meat, etc. to the locals on the occasion."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/37d714e8-29e1-44ec-a474-ab9eb80403c1> ;
    rdfs:comment "The Jaḥdhuṃ near the Sataḥ was constructed by Mahāpātra Purandarasiṃhadeva, a powerful local functionary of Patan during the late Malla period. He also formed a community-based trust with the responsibility of filling water in the Jaḥdhuṃ. The members of the trust were required to keep the Jaḥdhuṃ full as long as the statue of Buṅgadyaḥ remained in the temple at Taḥ Bāhāḥ. Every year on the 1stsolar day of Māgha, the Jaḥdhuṃ was worshipped and whitewashed. The trust distributed puffed rice (syāḥbaji), fermented rice beer (thvã), meat, etc. to the locals on the occasion."@en ;
