<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/38cbbdf2-a42b-4901-9784-8ef09a9ce2b7_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:TransferOfCustody ;
    rdfs:label "Initial construction"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Jāiphala Adhikārī, a government officer (subbā), commissioned the temple's construction in 1815 CE (VS 1871). In the accompanying inscription, he traces his genealogy back to his ancestor Bhāradvāja. The inscription also documents the construction of the Gaurīghāṭa bridge, the establishment of a path near the cremation site, the construction of a rest house, and other infrastructure projects, along with the provision of food for a thousand brahmins. Additionally, he endowed 48ropanīs of land to establish a trust responsible for temple rituals and maintenance."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/38cbbdf2-a42b-4901-9784-8ef09a9ce2b7> ;
    rdfs:comment "Jāiphala Adhikārī, a government officer (subbā), commissioned the temple's construction in 1815 CE (VS 1871). In the accompanying inscription, he traces his genealogy back to his ancestor Bhāradvāja. The inscription also documents the construction of the Gaurīghāṭa bridge, the establishment of a path near the cremation site, the construction of a rest house, and other infrastructure projects, along with the provision of food for a thousand brahmins. Additionally, he endowed 48ropanīs of land to establish a trust responsible for temple rituals and maintenance."@en ;
