<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/39ae7f90-422a-4c1b-af7e-766ae97dac4b_1> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Renovation of Mañjuśrī Vihāra (Viśvakarmā Bāhāḥ KAT2190)"@en ;
    dcterms:description "This inscription is affixed to the wall of the house situated on the western side of thisbāhāḥ. According to the details mentioned within, it does not pertain to thisbāhāḥbut rather concerns the renovation of the nearby Viśvakarmā Bāhāḥ, located to its west. Motikāji, the son of Caitavarasiṃ of Kathmandu, carried out the renovation of Viśvakarmā Bāhāḥ."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/39ae7f90-422a-4c1b-af7e-766ae97dac4b> ;
    rdfs:comment "This inscription is affixed to the wall of the house situated on the western side of thisbāhāḥ. According to the details mentioned within, it does not pertain to thisbāhāḥbut rather concerns the renovation of the nearby Viśvakarmā Bāhāḥ, located to its west. Motikāji, the son of Caitavarasiṃ of Kathmandu, carried out the renovation of Viśvakarmā Bāhāḥ."@en ;
