<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/39ae7f90-422a-4c1b-af7e-766ae97dac4b_2> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Offering of the toraṇa"@en ;
    dcterms:description "From the inscription located at the base of the main door, it is known that Caityavara Siṃha, the son of Harṣamāna and grandson of Rudramāna Śākya, along with his family, offered the woodentoraṇa. Locke (1985, p. 358) has mentioned the date of this inscription as NS 1024, whereas it is actually inscribed as 1905 CE (NS 1026)"@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/39ae7f90-422a-4c1b-af7e-766ae97dac4b> ;
    rdfs:comment "From the inscription located at the base of the main door, it is known that Caityavara Siṃha, the son of Harṣamāna and grandson of Rudramāna Śākya, along with his family, offered the woodentoraṇa. Locke (1985, p. 358) has mentioned the date of this inscription as NS 1024, whereas it is actually inscribed as 1905 CE (NS 1026)"@en ;
