<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/39fd71a8-5548-4c14-8ea8-c3d299e9391b_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Initial construction (?)"@en ;
    dcterms:description "As previously mentioned, the inscription dated 1583 CE (NS 703) found on the pedestal of the Garuḍa statue (refer to the 'description' section above) documents a land donation by Uddhava Bābu from Maṃgalā̃chẽ, Bhaktapur. This act took place during the joint reign of King Śivasiṃha and Raṇajitasiṃha. While the inscription signifies the dedication of the land, it remains unclear whether the construction of the temple corresponded with the establishment of the Garuḍa statue positioned in front of it."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/39fd71a8-5548-4c14-8ea8-c3d299e9391b> ;
    rdfs:comment "As previously mentioned, the inscription dated 1583 CE (NS 703) found on the pedestal of the Garuḍa statue (refer to the 'description' section above) documents a land donation by Uddhava Bābu from Maṃgalā̃chẽ, Bhaktapur. This act took place during the joint reign of King Śivasiṃha and Raṇajitasiṃha. While the inscription signifies the dedication of the land, it remains unclear whether the construction of the temple corresponded with the establishment of the Garuḍa statue positioned in front of it."@en ;
