<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/3a781560-86b0-11ea-86ac-0242ac130005_1> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Reconstruction"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Although the Phalcā was not in a very bad condition, it was dismantled and rebuilt in a style seen as 'more traditional'. The reconstruction work began in September 2019. Lalitpur Metropolitan, Ward no. 16 provided Rs. 1.4 million rupees for its reconstruction. The inauguration of the Phalcā was held on the 10thday of the dark fortnight of Phālguna. This was also the day that the spirits of the serpents were returned to their vessels during Itilhane Samyak."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/3a781560-86b0-11ea-86ac-0242ac130005> ;
    rdfs:comment "Although the Phalcā was not in a very bad condition, it was dismantled and rebuilt in a style seen as 'more traditional'. The reconstruction work began in September 2019. Lalitpur Metropolitan, Ward no. 16 provided Rs. 1.4 million rupees for its reconstruction. The inauguration of the Phalcā was held on the 10thday of the dark fortnight of Phālguna. This was also the day that the spirits of the serpents were returned to their vessels during Itilhane Samyak."@en ;
