        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Construction of separate shrine for various deities"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Jānu Gautama built a separate shrine north of the temple and installed the statues of various deities, including Gaṇeśa (KAT3081-003) and Hanumān (KAT3081-007). These statues were recovered from different parts of Hā̃ḍīgāũ and were initially placed in the sanctum of the Sarasvatī temple."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/3d43778b-bbe9-40fb-8a5c-5d7141d937c6> ;
