<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/3d6d075f-5820-48d7-9fb2-b2b4157f1439_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Reconstruction of the Sīdhvākhā"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The Sīdhvākhā was one of the two other gates that had retained its original structure Unfortunately, this medieval gate lost its original shape and structure during its reconstruction in VS 2055 (1998 CE) (Ś. ŚreṣṭhaVS 2057, p. 35). The ancient gate was converted into a modern structure arguing that the old gate was not wide enough to allow vehicles like taxis, ambulances, fire brigade, etc. to pass into the city at times of emergency (local knowledge, local resident, Maharjana, male, age 69)."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/3d6d075f-5820-48d7-9fb2-b2b4157f1439> ;
    rdfs:comment "The Sīdhvākhā was one of the two other gates that had retained its original structure Unfortunately, this medieval gate lost its original shape and structure during its reconstruction in VS 2055 (1998 CE) (Ś. ŚreṣṭhaVS 2057, p. 35). The ancient gate was converted into a modern structure arguing that the old gate was not wide enough to allow vehicles like taxis, ambulances, fire brigade, etc. to pass into the city at times of emergency (local knowledge, local resident, Maharjana, male, age 69)."@en ;
