<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/3eed6ff1-e60f-4425-b7dc-052f8094f611_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Addition of toraṇa"@en ;
    dcterms:description "An inscription is embedded into the eastern wall of the Phalcā, which mentions the locality's name as 'Custhurī' and the installation date. However, the exact purpose or significance of the event on that day is unknown. Notably, the color and texture of the stone inscription match those of the stone toraṇa nearby. This suggests that the inscription might have been created around the same time when the toraṇa was constructed. Shokoohys and Śreṣṭha (2014, p. 282) also associate this inscription with the toraṇa, further supporting the idea that they are contemporaneous."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/3eed6ff1-e60f-4425-b7dc-052f8094f611> ;
    rdfs:comment "An inscription is embedded into the eastern wall of the Phalcā, which mentions the locality's name as 'Custhurī' and the installation date. However, the exact purpose or significance of the event on that day is unknown. Notably, the color and texture of the stone inscription match those of the stone toraṇa nearby. This suggests that the inscription might have been created around the same time when the toraṇa was constructed. Shokoohys and Śreṣṭha (2014, p. 282) also associate this inscription with the toraṇa, further supporting the idea that they are contemporaneous."@en ;
