<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/3eed6ff1-e60f-4425-b7dc-052f8094f611_1> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Addition of a  bell"@en ;
    dcterms:description "During the reconstruction project in 2019, a significant discovery was made when a worker uncovered a stone fragment of a metha. Upon examination, it was found that the surface of the metha bore an inscription dating back to the Malla period. This metha is believed to be a part of a hanging bell, suggesting that a hanging bell was once present here, suspended from a stone beam. The inscription on the metha records the installation of this bell, shedding light on the historical significance of this site."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/3eed6ff1-e60f-4425-b7dc-052f8094f611> ;
    rdfs:comment "During the reconstruction project in 2019, a significant discovery was made when a worker uncovered a stone fragment of a metha. Upon examination, it was found that the surface of the metha bore an inscription dating back to the Malla period. This metha is believed to be a part of a hanging bell, suggesting that a hanging bell was once present here, suspended from a stone beam. The inscription on the metha records the installation of this bell, shedding light on the historical significance of this site."@en ;
