<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/3eed6ff1-e60f-4425-b7dc-052f8094f611_2> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Paving of stone"@en ;
    dcterms:description "During the rule of King Pṛthvī Śāha, a jyāmadāra named Suravīra's sons, namely Kṛṣṇavīra, Kulamāna, and Budhimāna, were responsible for the installation of stone slabs on a specific section of the main lane within the city of Kirtipur. The approximate length of this paving project is described as extending \"from the east of Gaḥchẽ Dhvākhā to the west of Chīthū Dhvākhā.\" This historical record provides insight into the civic development and infrastructure projects undertaken during that period."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/3eed6ff1-e60f-4425-b7dc-052f8094f611> ;
    rdfs:comment "During the rule of King Pṛthvī Śāha, a jyāmadāra named Suravīra's sons, namely Kṛṣṇavīra, Kulamāna, and Budhimāna, were responsible for the installation of stone slabs on a specific section of the main lane within the city of Kirtipur. The approximate length of this paving project is described as extending \"from the east of Gaḥchẽ Dhvākhā to the west of Chīthū Dhvākhā.\" This historical record provides insight into the civic development and infrastructure projects undertaken during that period."@en ;
