<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/3eed6ff1-e60f-4425-b7dc-052f8094f611_9> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Enshrinement ;
    rdfs:label "Dyaḥsīkaḥ vanegu procession"@en ;
    dcterms:description "In keeping with the Newar tradition of visiting other major shrines in the city following the installation of a new statue, a grand procession of devotees was organized to pay homage to other significant Bhairava shrines in the Kathmandu Valley. This procession saw the participation of approximately 1,000 devotees. The procession visited a total of 9 major Bhairava shrines, including Pacalī Bhairava, Kāla Bhairava, Ākāśa Bhairava, Ānanda Bhairava, Vaṭuka Bhairava, Tyāṅgā Bhairava, Hayagrīva Bhairava, along with Kirtipur's own Bāgha Bhairava, Aṣṭasiddhi Bhairava, and the newly installed Bhairava mask at the Phalcā. This pilgrimage allowed devotees to offer their reverence and prayers at these sacred sites."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/3eed6ff1-e60f-4425-b7dc-052f8094f611> ;
    rdfs:comment "In keeping with the Newar tradition of visiting other major shrines in the city following the installation of a new statue, a grand procession of devotees was organized to pay homage to other significant Bhairava shrines in the Kathmandu Valley. This procession saw the participation of approximately 1,000 devotees. The procession visited a total of 9 major Bhairava shrines, including Pacalī Bhairava, Kāla Bhairava, Ākāśa Bhairava, Ānanda Bhairava, Vaṭuka Bhairava, Tyāṅgā Bhairava, Hayagrīva Bhairava, along with Kirtipur's own Bāgha Bhairava, Aṣṭasiddhi Bhairava, and the newly installed Bhairava mask at the Phalcā. This pilgrimage allowed devotees to offer their reverence and prayers at these sacred sites."@en ;
