<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/3f0790b1-f7ca-4261-89df-ea1e85658ced_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Construction of a guesthouse"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The details of the Caitya’s initial construction are unclear. The inscription on the Caitya’s plinth, which is inscribed in Tibetan and Newari scripts is not related to the Caitya. It records the construction of a guesthouse in the village by a certain Dorje Lāmā, themukhiyāof the village, along with his wife Karmāvatī, son Śerbā Dorje and other relatives, during the reign of King Raṇa Bahādura Śāha. Nothing is known about the guesthouse at present, as no one in the village recalls its existence here."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/3f0790b1-f7ca-4261-89df-ea1e85658ced> ;
    rdfs:comment "The details of the Caitya’s initial construction are unclear. The inscription on the Caitya’s plinth, which is inscribed in Tibetan and Newari scripts is not related to the Caitya. It records the construction of a guesthouse in the village by a certain Dorje Lāmā, themukhiyāof the village, along with his wife Karmāvatī, son Śerbā Dorje and other relatives, during the reign of King Raṇa Bahādura Śāha. Nothing is known about the guesthouse at present, as no one in the village recalls its existence here."@en ;
