<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/3f87ad30-e5d0-11e9-8bc4-0242ac130002_1> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:RitualEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Construction of the western Phalcā"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The inscription in the western wing states that a group of Prajāpatis/Avāles led by Kṛṣṇamuni Bare (śākya) initiated the construction of a six-bayedPhalcā devoted to Bhīmarāṇeśvara and established a statue of Padmapāṇi Lokeśvara (inside the Phalcā). From here, Rām Prajāpati and his family were appointed as the caretakers of thePhalcā. The inscription also mentions the offering of wick lamps, rice and meat on the festivals of Buṃgama Lokeśvara and Indrajātra."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/3f87ad30-e5d0-11e9-8bc4-0242ac130002> ;
    rdfs:comment "The inscription in the western wing states that a group of Prajāpatis/Avāles led by Kṛṣṇamuni Bare (śākya) initiated the construction of a six-bayedPhalcā devoted to Bhīmarāṇeśvara and established a statue of Padmapāṇi Lokeśvara (inside the Phalcā). From here, Rām Prajāpati and his family were appointed as the caretakers of thePhalcā. The inscription also mentions the offering of wick lamps, rice and meat on the festivals of Buṃgama Lokeśvara and Indrajātra."@en ;
