<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/425bbdb8-54b5-474e-839a-7da85f116aa3_10> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:RitualEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Offering of silver toraṇa, serpent noose, and parasol"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Kālu Siṃ offered Vajravārāhī a silvertoraṇa(decorative arch), anāgapāśa(serpent noose), and a parasol, with a combined weight of 221tolās of silver. He also presented a 15-tolāsilver garland to the buffalo figure (CHG0110-024), Vajravārāhī's animal mount. These offerings were to be displayed during festivals and on Saturdays. The donor further stipulated that Vajravārāhī be worshipped with an animal sacrifice on the 3rd of the dark fortnight of Jyeṣṭha, the day his father, Harṣanarasiṃha, passed away. He established a trust with land donation to ensure the continuation of these practices."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/425bbdb8-54b5-474e-839a-7da85f116aa3> ;
    rdfs:comment "Kālu Siṃ offered Vajravārāhī a silvertoraṇa(decorative arch), anāgapāśa(serpent noose), and a parasol, with a combined weight of 221tolās of silver. He also presented a 15-tolāsilver garland to the buffalo figure (CHG0110-024), Vajravārāhī's animal mount. These offerings were to be displayed during festivals and on Saturdays. The donor further stipulated that Vajravārāhī be worshipped with an animal sacrifice on the 3rd of the dark fortnight of Jyeṣṭha, the day his father, Harṣanarasiṃha, passed away. He established a trust with land donation to ensure the continuation of these practices."@en ;
