<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/425bbdb8-54b5-474e-839a-7da85f116aa3_18> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Establishment of marble inscription"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The upper roof of the Vajravārāhī temple was covered with zinc sheets, while the lower roof was covered with tiles. Due to the deterioration of both roofs, leading to leaks and rotting of the wooden rafters, financial assistance was collected from various sources to replace both roofs with copper sheets. A marble inscription was installed to commemorate this event."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/425bbdb8-54b5-474e-839a-7da85f116aa3> ;
