<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/425bbdb8-54b5-474e-839a-7da85f116aa3_3> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Renovation of the temple"@en ;
    dcterms:description "King Viṣṇu Malla of Lalitpur renovated the Vajravārāhī temple and organized the ‘suvarṇakalaśadhvajārohaṇa’ceremony, involving the installation of a golden finial and the hoisting of a banner. Priests and astrologers like Viśvānanda and Nīlakaṇṭhānanda participated in the ritual. The inscription records the king's donation of land to commemorate the anniversary of the finial installation and mandates annual fire rituals with animal sacrifice. This inscription contradicts the popular belief that the temple has never had a finial."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/425bbdb8-54b5-474e-839a-7da85f116aa3> ;
    rdfs:comment "King Viṣṇu Malla of Lalitpur renovated the Vajravārāhī temple and organized the ‘suvarṇakalaśadhvajārohaṇa’ceremony, involving the installation of a golden finial and the hoisting of a banner. Priests and astrologers like Viśvānanda and Nīlakaṇṭhānanda participated in the ritual. The inscription records the king's donation of land to commemorate the anniversary of the finial installation and mandates annual fire rituals with animal sacrifice. This inscription contradicts the popular belief that the temple has never had a finial."@en ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/agent/antigravity_agent> ;
