<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/425bbdb8-54b5-474e-839a-7da85f116aa3_4> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:TransferOfCustody ;
    rdfs:label "Endowment of lands to repair a phalcā"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Gaṃgāsāgara Bābu of the Bhansāra Ṭola in Cāpāgāũ, along with his wife Rājalakṣmī, renovated aphalcaand established a religious trust by donating land. The income from this land was to be used for repairing thephalca's roof and making ancestral offerings in the name of his uncle Mastarāma on the 3rd of the dark fortnight of Phālguna, prior to the worship at the Vajravārāhī temple. It remains unclear which of the threephalcās—west, north, or south of the temple—was renovated."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/425bbdb8-54b5-474e-839a-7da85f116aa3> ;
    rdfs:comment "Gaṃgāsāgara Bābu of the Bhansāra Ṭola in Cāpāgāũ, along with his wife Rājalakṣmī, renovated aphalcaand established a religious trust by donating land. The income from this land was to be used for repairing thephalca's roof and making ancestral offerings in the name of his uncle Mastarāma on the 3rd of the dark fortnight of Phālguna, prior to the worship at the Vajravārāhī temple. It remains unclear which of the threephalcās—west, north, or south of the temple—was renovated."@en ;
