<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/425bbdb8-54b5-474e-839a-7da85f116aa3_5> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:TransferOfCustody ;
    rdfs:label "Endowment of lands to sweep"@en ;
    dcterms:description "During the reign of King Surendra, Kāyaṣṭha Akabara Bhāro of the Bhansāra Ṭola in Cāpāgāũ established a religious trust by donating land for cleaning the temple premises daily. He made the donation together with his mother Guṇa Thaku and his sons Mānakāji, Kṛṣṇamehera, Syāmamehera, and Rāmamehera, wishing for the deliverance of his ancestors. He also mandated an annual worship of Vajravārāhī on the 8th of the bright fortnight of Caitra, followed by a feast."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/425bbdb8-54b5-474e-839a-7da85f116aa3> ;
    rdfs:comment "During the reign of King Surendra, Kāyaṣṭha Akabara Bhāro of the Bhansāra Ṭola in Cāpāgāũ established a religious trust by donating land for cleaning the temple premises daily. He made the donation together with his mother Guṇa Thaku and his sons Mānakāji, Kṛṣṇamehera, Syāmamehera, and Rāmamehera, wishing for the deliverance of his ancestors. He also mandated an annual worship of Vajravārāhī on the 8th of the bright fortnight of Caitra, followed by a feast."@en ;
