<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/43291104-1bbd-11ea-b9b1-0242ac130002_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Earthquake"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Cābāhāḥ Phalcā collapsed completely in the 2015 earthquakes. Musical instruments, books and statues of deities were all buried under the rubble. The traditional drums stored on the upper floor were later recovered by locals and had suffered some damages. However, a local Maharjan resident tells us that the images of Umāmaheśvaraand some other deities remained buried under the rubble, along with an inscription installed in the Phalcā."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/43291104-1bbd-11ea-b9b1-0242ac130002> ;
    rdfs:comment "Cābāhāḥ Phalcā collapsed completely in the 2015 earthquakes. Musical instruments, books and statues of deities were all buried under the rubble. The traditional drums stored on the upper floor were later recovered by locals and had suffered some damages. However, a local Maharjan resident tells us that the images of Umāmaheśvaraand some other deities remained buried under the rubble, along with an inscription installed in the Phalcā."@en ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/agent/antigravity_agent> ;
