<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/43291104-1bbd-11ea-b9b1-0242ac130002_3> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Renovation of the Phalcā and installation of a statue"@en ;
    dcterms:description "An inscription on thecaityain front of the Phalcā mentions that the Cābāhāḥ Phalcā was renovated and a statue of Umāmaheśvara was installed. The inscription names Harinandana Duvāra Bhāro as the donor of this and other properties in the name of hisīṣṭa devatā. It is likely that he also sponsored the construction of the Caitya and the renovation of the Phalcā, as well as the installation of the statue of Umāmaheśvara.The term 'bhāro'clearly suggests that Harinandana is from the Shrestha community. The extent to which the Phalcā was renovated is not clear. It is worth noting that the renovation was carried out just 12 years after its construction."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/43291104-1bbd-11ea-b9b1-0242ac130002> ;
    rdfs:comment "An inscription on thecaityain front of the Phalcā mentions that the Cābāhāḥ Phalcā was renovated and a statue of Umāmaheśvara was installed. The inscription names Harinandana Duvāra Bhāro as the donor of this and other properties in the name of hisīṣṭa devatā. It is likely that he also sponsored the construction of the Caitya and the renovation of the Phalcā, as well as the installation of the statue of Umāmaheśvara.The term 'bhāro'clearly suggests that Harinandana is from the Shrestha community. The extent to which the Phalcā was renovated is not clear. It is worth noting that the renovation was carried out just 12 years after its construction."@en ;
