<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/43a6124a-0a4b-4f1c-a3b6-f68fcb0e4dc0_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Renovation of a royal water channel"@en ;
    dcterms:description "A Licchavi inscription from Samvat 48 (624 CE) which is not related to this monument is in the temple premises.[1]It is not clear why this was moved to this temple. The inscription records the restoration of a water channel by Aṃśu Varman (see the edition and translation of the inscription inVajrācāryaVS 2030, 401-404).^According to Vajrācārya (VS 2030, 401), this inscription is related to Chinnamastā Mandira."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/43a6124a-0a4b-4f1c-a3b6-f68fcb0e4dc0> ;
    rdfs:comment "A Licchavi inscription from Samvat 48 (624 CE) which is not related to this monument is in the temple premises.[1]It is not clear why this was moved to this temple. The inscription records the restoration of a water channel by Aṃśu Varman (see the edition and translation of the inscription inVajrācāryaVS 2030, 401-404).^According to Vajrācārya (VS 2030, 401), this inscription is related to Chinnamastā Mandira."@en ;
