        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Pavement of stone and installation of a donor statue"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The inscription records that Maṇirāja Thakālī, a resident of Dathutaḥjhyāḥ Ṭola paved stones on the temple premises and installed his and his wife’s statue there. It further informs us that he made Gaṇeśa happy by reciting the texts dedicated to him and meditating on him."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/43a6124a-0a4b-4f1c-a3b6-f68fcb0e4dc0> ;
