<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/4405bb30-4704-432a-9f61-2a7c8912321a_1> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Consecration ;
    rdfs:label "Initial Construction of Buddha Mandira"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The inscription in the sanctum suggests that the construction was completed in 1649 CE (NS 769) and a statue of Śākyamuni was consecrated in the sanctum. In consecration ceromony a fire sacrifice calledlakṣyāhutiyajñais performed, followed by dance and traditional music (consisting of five musical instruments) performances. The kings of Patan, Siddhinarasiṃha Malla and Śrīnivāsa Malla, were present during this ceremony.The inscription further records that a person called Hākuju from a Śākya clan constructed this temple. He also constructed Cvay Bāhāḥ (KIR0011), which is located nearby this temple."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/4405bb30-4704-432a-9f61-2a7c8912321a> ;
    rdfs:comment "The inscription in the sanctum suggests that the construction was completed in 1649 CE (NS 769) and a statue of Śākyamuni was consecrated in the sanctum. In consecration ceromony a fire sacrifice calledlakṣyāhutiyajñais performed, followed by dance and traditional music (consisting of five musical instruments) performances. The kings of Patan, Siddhinarasiṃha Malla and Śrīnivāsa Malla, were present during this ceremony.The inscription further records that a person called Hākuju from a Śākya clan constructed this temple. He also constructed Cvay Bāhāḥ (KIR0011), which is located nearby this temple."@en ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/agent/antigravity_agent> ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/activity/heritagegraph_kg_construction> ;
