<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/440d970c-ea5d-11e9-b125-0242ac130002_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Donations"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Tharapā(the most senior member of thevihāra) Kantāsura offered atoraṇa,a vajraanda silver banner(kikiṃpā)to Maitreya Bodhisattva anddhakiṃ(curtain), garlands, two lotus flowers, one drum (ḍamaru) and onecāmara(a yak tail used for fanning) to Yogāṃbara, the deity of theāgãchẽ. In addition to this, he offered two stone images of lions, a crown,a vajra, anda pātrakhvālāto Viśvakarmā. He also donatedteliyābricks for the house of the esoteric deity (digī)."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/440d970c-ea5d-11e9-b125-0242ac130002> ;
    rdfs:comment "Tharapā(the most senior member of thevihāra) Kantāsura offered atoraṇa,a vajraanda silver banner(kikiṃpā)to Maitreya Bodhisattva anddhakiṃ(curtain), garlands, two lotus flowers, one drum (ḍamaru) and onecāmara(a yak tail used for fanning) to Yogāṃbara, the deity of theāgãchẽ. In addition to this, he offered two stone images of lions, a crown,a vajra, anda pātrakhvālāto Viśvakarmā. He also donatedteliyābricks for the house of the esoteric deity (digī)."@en ;
