<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/445549f9-57cf-4664-bd5b-1da8562e7d4e_2> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Addition of a bell"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The family of Viṣṇulāla offered a bell to their local Sthāna Gaṇeśa. Interestingly, the bell bears a Sanskrit verse dedicated to Gaṇeśa. Compared to other bells from the Rāṇā period, this one shows more elaborate ornamentation, including floral patterns, images of Gaṇeśa, and serpents (nāga) on all sides."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/445549f9-57cf-4664-bd5b-1da8562e7d4e> ;
    rdfs:comment "The family of Viṣṇulāla offered a bell to their local Sthāna Gaṇeśa. Interestingly, the bell bears a Sanskrit verse dedicated to Gaṇeśa. Compared to other bells from the Rāṇā period, this one shows more elaborate ornamentation, including floral patterns, images of Gaṇeśa, and serpents (nāga) on all sides."@en ;
