<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/44bd16fb-9ed4-4e98-88f9-dc697feeb717_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Offering of gilded flags"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Individuals from Jholachẽ, including Śyāma Bhābo, Suryya Bhābo, and Gunadeva Bhābo, collectively lit a large lamp (mahādīpa) at the Gaṇeśa temple and offered gilded flags. On the same occasion, aketakīflower was also offered to Āryāvalokiteśvara located in the Haka Ṭola. Two craftsmen, Hāku Bade and Taodhika Bade from the Jyāthā Ṭola, had jointly crafted these items. The flag can no longer be seen at the temple."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/44bd16fb-9ed4-4e98-88f9-dc697feeb717> ;
    rdfs:comment "Individuals from Jholachẽ, including Śyāma Bhābo, Suryya Bhābo, and Gunadeva Bhābo, collectively lit a large lamp (mahādīpa) at the Gaṇeśa temple and offered gilded flags. On the same occasion, aketakīflower was also offered to Āryāvalokiteśvara located in the Haka Ṭola. Two craftsmen, Hāku Bade and Taodhika Bade from the Jyāthā Ṭola, had jointly crafted these items. The flag can no longer be seen at the temple."@en ;
