<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/479763c6-e90e-11e9-b125-0242ac130002_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Renovation of the Phalcā"@en ;
    dcterms:description "he Prajāpatis, who are also called Avāle (in Patan) of Bherālivi*, led bythakuBhāgideva and including Silhaṃ Bhāvo, Bhāna Singh Bhāvo, Saṃkha Bhāvo, Rakṣmiṣaṃkha Bhāvo and Mimha Bhāvo from the samecapāḥorganization of the same clan, renovated thedharmmaśālāin 1782 CE. Atympanumwas offered.Transliteration of the stone inscription of Phalcā (provided by Nutan Sharma):adya śveta varāhakalpyādi | śreyostu || sabbatasara902 ākhāḍha māsa kṛṣṇa pakṣe  (dvādasyāṃ) pra trayodasyaṃ ti-thva || jāta (Jeṣṭhā) nakṣatre || vajra yyoge yathākrrana mūhurtuke || aṃgāra-vāsare kakrata rāśite savitari mithuna rāśicandramasi || thva kunhu bhera [che͂]livi (Bhelāche͂) thāparaṃ yantāgṛha gṛha prajāpa-ti bhāgideva thakurasanaṃ silhaṃ bhāvo bhāna siṃ bhāvo saṃ-kha bhāvo rakṣmiṣaṃkha bhāvo mimha bhāvo thvti capālapiṃthuti || thao kulasala || saeva bhelogupṭhaṃ_ _ _majyādāsyaṃ cvṃgvalāka vāṣṭavya dharmmasārā jirṇo-dhāra yāsya pratiṣṭhā yāṅā juro ||  || subha ||toraṃ sahintaṃ tayā jula || dhu  || subha ||Provisional translation:On the joint day of 12 and 13th of the dark half of lunar month of Āṣāḍha, in 1782 CE (NS 902), in the installation called Jeṣṭhā, conjunction called Vajra, Yathākaraṇamūhurta (moment?), on Tuesday when the son is in Cancer and moon is in Gemini, the Prajāpatis of Bhera [che͂]livi (Bhelāche͂) led bythe thaku (senior person)Bhāgideva including Silhaṃ bhāvo,  Bhāna Singh Bhāvo, Saṃkha Bhāvo, Rakṣmiṣaṃkha Bhāvo [and] Mimha Bhāvo from the samecapāhof the own clan have renovated thedharmmaśālāsituated in Bhelogupṭhaṃ _ _ _ and established it offering a tympanum with respect. May all be well."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/479763c6-e90e-11e9-b125-0242ac130002> ;
    rdfs:comment "he Prajāpatis, who are also called Avāle (in Patan) of Bherālivi*, led bythakuBhāgideva and including Silhaṃ Bhāvo, Bhāna Singh Bhāvo, Saṃkha Bhāvo, Rakṣmiṣaṃkha Bhāvo and Mimha Bhāvo from the samecapāḥorganization of the same clan, renovated thedharmmaśālāin 1782 CE. Atympanumwas offered.Transliteration of the stone inscription of Phalcā (provided by Nutan Sharma):adya śveta varāhakalpyādi | śreyostu || sabbatasara902 ākhāḍha māsa kṛṣṇa pakṣe  (dvādasyāṃ) pra trayodasyaṃ ti-thva || jāta (Jeṣṭhā) nakṣatre || vajra yyoge yathākrrana mūhurtuke || aṃgāra-vāsare kakrata rāśite savitari mithuna rāśicandramasi || thva kunhu bhera [che͂]livi (Bhelāche͂) thāparaṃ yantāgṛha gṛha prajāpa-ti bhāgideva thakurasanaṃ silhaṃ bhāvo bhāna siṃ bhāvo saṃ-kha bhāvo rakṣmiṣaṃkha bhāvo mimha bhāvo thvti capālapiṃthuti || thao kulasala || saeva bhelogupṭhaṃ_ _ _majyādāsyaṃ cvṃgvalāka vāṣṭavya dharmmasārā jirṇo-dhāra yāsya pratiṣṭhā yāṅā juro ||  || subha ||toraṃ sahintaṃ tayā jula || dhu  || subha ||Provisional translation:On the joint day of 12 and 13th of the dark half of lunar month of Āṣāḍha, in 1782 CE (NS 902), in the installation called Jeṣṭhā, conjunction called Vajra, Yathākaraṇamūhurta (moment?), on Tuesday when the son is in Cancer and moon is in Gemini, the Prajāpatis of Bhera [che͂]livi (Bhelāche͂) led bythe thaku (senior person)Bhāgideva including Silhaṃ bhāvo,  Bhāna Singh Bhāvo, Saṃkha Bhāvo, Rakṣmiṣaṃkha Bhāvo [and] Mimha Bhāvo from the samecapāhof the own clan have renovated thedharmmaśālāsituated in Bhelogupṭhaṃ _ _ _ and established it offering a tympanum with respect. May all be well."@en ;
