<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/47fabacf-d579-4f27-9568-2cfa31345a9e_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:TransferOfCustody ;
    rdfs:label "Initial construction"@en ;
    dcterms:description "During the reign of King Bhāṣkara Malla, Siddhimuni Vajrācārya (text: Vajācājya Siddhimuni) founded the Bāhāḥ and concecrated a statue of Akṣobhya as the main deity (Kvāḥpāḥdyaḥ) inside its sanctum. On the same occasion, he endowed land and established aguthito run and maintain the Bāhāḥ. He also erected acaitya. His wife Herulakṣmī, younger brother Padmamuni, second son Beṣādeva, daughters Dhanalakṣmī and Sarvalakṣmī all assisted him in establishing the Bāhāḥ."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/47fabacf-d579-4f27-9568-2cfa31345a9e> ;
    rdfs:comment "During the reign of King Bhāṣkara Malla, Siddhimuni Vajrācārya (text: Vajācājya Siddhimuni) founded the Bāhāḥ and concecrated a statue of Akṣobhya as the main deity (Kvāḥpāḥdyaḥ) inside its sanctum. On the same occasion, he endowed land and established aguthito run and maintain the Bāhāḥ. He also erected acaitya. His wife Herulakṣmī, younger brother Padmamuni, second son Beṣādeva, daughters Dhanalakṣmī and Sarvalakṣmī all assisted him in establishing the Bāhāḥ."@en ;
