<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/48dc7bc9-effe-43fd-ab20-228d51298ccb_1> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:TransferOfCustody ;
    rdfs:label "Formation of guthi for various worships"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Although being constructed in an area densely populated by the Newars, an inscription at the Temple records a non-Newar family of the Khatrī caste forming aguthiin the late 19thcentury in the name of Bhagavatī. According to the inscription, Dhanavīra Khatrī formed the Guthi for the worship of other deities like Nīlakaṇṭha, Nṛtyeśvara, etc. along with Bhagavatī. There is a clear instruction for descendants of Dhanavīra in the inscription: Carry out the activities at this house and the rent from the shop shall be the income of the Guthi. This suggests that the house with a shop was situated near the Temple.Jayalakṣmī formed a trust of 101 rupees in 1816 CE (VS 1873) for feeding seven Brahmins of Paśupati on the full moon days of Vaiśākha and Kārtika along with a donation of 1paisāeach out of the interest received from the amount. Additionally, the income was to be used to light 21 lamps at the Temple on the full moon day of Kārtika."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/48dc7bc9-effe-43fd-ab20-228d51298ccb> ;
    rdfs:comment "Although being constructed in an area densely populated by the Newars, an inscription at the Temple records a non-Newar family of the Khatrī caste forming aguthiin the late 19thcentury in the name of Bhagavatī. According to the inscription, Dhanavīra Khatrī formed the Guthi for the worship of other deities like Nīlakaṇṭha, Nṛtyeśvara, etc. along with Bhagavatī. There is a clear instruction for descendants of Dhanavīra in the inscription: Carry out the activities at this house and the rent from the shop shall be the income of the Guthi. This suggests that the house with a shop was situated near the Temple.Jayalakṣmī formed a trust of 101 rupees in 1816 CE (VS 1873) for feeding seven Brahmins of Paśupati on the full moon days of Vaiśākha and Kārtika along with a donation of 1paisāeach out of the interest received from the amount. Additionally, the income was to be used to light 21 lamps at the Temple on the full moon day of Kārtika."@en ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/agent/antigravity_agent> ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/activity/heritagegraph_kg_construction> ;
