<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/4a48d563-85d1-4e51-8f78-2254393f85e2_2> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Installation of a Donor Statue (C)"@en ;
    dcterms:description "A pair of donors, carved on a single stone slab, was placed inside the Pīṭha. Names of the donor couple have been inscribed at the arch-shaped top of the statue. It is very difficult to decipher the names in the present-day. However, Shokoohy et all (2014, 86) have read the names as Joganātha and Gaṃgāvati (Gaṅgāvatī)."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/4a48d563-85d1-4e51-8f78-2254393f85e2> ;
    rdfs:comment "A pair of donors, carved on a single stone slab, was placed inside the Pīṭha. Names of the donor couple have been inscribed at the arch-shaped top of the statue. It is very difficult to decipher the names in the present-day. However, Shokoohy et all (2014, 86) have read the names as Joganātha and Gaṃgāvati (Gaṅgāvatī)."@en ;
