<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/4abcfc57-87bc-46d0-9338-add4863dbf46_1> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Photo Kathmandu - Patis in Patan"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Pvāḥsyāḥ Phalcā was one of fourphalcāsselected for the first PhotoKathmandu Festival in 2015 and became a major success among locals and passers-by. Positioned at a main road in Patan, it became a spectacular object of attention during the days of the festival. Many people articulated the desire to hold on to it and for it to stay beyond the festival time. The Pvāḥsyaḥ Phalcā (Pāṭī) at Sundhara was removed in the 1970s and has stood as platform since then. Art students from Kathmandu University's Art and Design Centre were involved in the PhotoKathmandu project and studied its previous form through old postcards, and conversations with locals before reconstructing it. The aim of the reconstruction was to encourage future perspectives on the post-earthquake city, referencing what has been lost, but also what can be gained again, and how important the ‘institution’ of thepatican be in this context."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/4abcfc57-87bc-46d0-9338-add4863dbf46> ;
    rdfs:comment "Pvāḥsyāḥ Phalcā was one of fourphalcāsselected for the first PhotoKathmandu Festival in 2015 and became a major success among locals and passers-by. Positioned at a main road in Patan, it became a spectacular object of attention during the days of the festival. Many people articulated the desire to hold on to it and for it to stay beyond the festival time. The Pvāḥsyaḥ Phalcā (Pāṭī) at Sundhara was removed in the 1970s and has stood as platform since then. Art students from Kathmandu University's Art and Design Centre were involved in the PhotoKathmandu project and studied its previous form through old postcards, and conversations with locals before reconstructing it. The aim of the reconstruction was to encourage future perspectives on the post-earthquake city, referencing what has been lost, but also what can be gained again, and how important the ‘institution’ of thepatican be in this context."@en ;
