<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/4b3adb40-7726-4977-b911-1710edbfa41f_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Enshrinement ;
    rdfs:label "Initial construction of the bāhāḥ"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Kumāraju Śākya commissioned the construction of thebāhāḥon the fifth day of the bright fortnight of Māgha (Śrīpañcamī) in 1678 CE (798 NS) during the joint reign of King Śrīnivāsa and Yoganarendra Malla. During the initial construction, a statue of Akṣobhya was installed in the sanctum as thebāhāh’s primary deity (kvāḥpāḥdyaḥ), and the statues of Cakrasaṃvara-Vajravārāhī, Gaṇeśa and Mahākāla were installed inside theāgaṃ."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/4b3adb40-7726-4977-b911-1710edbfa41f> ;
    rdfs:comment "Kumāraju Śākya commissioned the construction of thebāhāḥon the fifth day of the bright fortnight of Māgha (Śrīpañcamī) in 1678 CE (798 NS) during the joint reign of King Śrīnivāsa and Yoganarendra Malla. During the initial construction, a statue of Akṣobhya was installed in the sanctum as thebāhāh’s primary deity (kvāḥpāḥdyaḥ), and the statues of Cakrasaṃvara-Vajravārāhī, Gaṇeśa and Mahākāla were installed inside theāgaṃ."@en ;
