<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/4b6b1b40-a37c-49a5-a213-20eca5f03346_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Licchavi inscription"@en ;
    dcterms:description "In front of the Phalcā stands the slate of a Licchavi inscription recovered in 2004 CE. It was issued during the reign of King Gaṇadeva in the Śaka Era year 482 i.e., the Vikrama Era year 616. The inscription records a royal order given to the Mukhiyās, Brahmins and other householders of the administrative unit Theñco Grāma (seeŚ. Rājavaṃśī2061, p. 94-95 for an edition and translation of the text)."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/4b6b1b40-a37c-49a5-a213-20eca5f03346> ;
    rdfs:comment "In front of the Phalcā stands the slate of a Licchavi inscription recovered in 2004 CE. It was issued during the reign of King Gaṇadeva in the Śaka Era year 482 i.e., the Vikrama Era year 616. The inscription records a royal order given to the Mukhiyās, Brahmins and other householders of the administrative unit Theñco Grāma (seeŚ. Rājavaṃśī2061, p. 94-95 for an edition and translation of the text)."@en ;
