<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/4bf00773-e1d3-4029-956c-517a7d22ef21_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Earthquake damage"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The 2015 CE earthquakes severely damaged the Gārada Ghara, with half of the uppermost floor and a significant portion of the roof collapsing. The Department of Archaeology engaged the Chinese Academy of Cultural Heritage (CACH) to supervise restoration efforts for Raṅgamahala and adjacent monuments. Scaffoldings and corrugated metal sheets were deployed to shield roofs from rain. However, as of March 2024 CE, renovation has yet to commence."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/4bf00773-e1d3-4029-956c-517a7d22ef21> ;
    rdfs:comment "The 2015 CE earthquakes severely damaged the Gārada Ghara, with half of the uppermost floor and a significant portion of the roof collapsing. The Department of Archaeology engaged the Chinese Academy of Cultural Heritage (CACH) to supervise restoration efforts for Raṅgamahala and adjacent monuments. Scaffoldings and corrugated metal sheets were deployed to shield roofs from rain. However, as of March 2024 CE, renovation has yet to commence."@en ;
