<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/4ef6a4bb-88e5-4b4c-a1c7-9e4fb4553a45_3> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Construction of a house"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Verse 1:In the year 1776 CE (ŚS 1698), on an auspicious day in the month of Kārtika, under theUttarabhādrapadāconstellation and the holy occasion ofHaribodhinī Ekādaśī, when the moon was in Mīnarāśi, and both Jupiter (Guru) and Venus (Śukra) were in favorable positions—at that propitious moment, the minister Śrīkīrtisiṃha commenced the construction of this grand Jaya Maṇḍira.Verse 2:The king, sovereign of the Gaurśācala realm, had a contented land and a joyous populace. His minister, the learned and valiant Kīrtisiṃha, was served by his attendant, Sarūpasiṃha. In thisJayamaṇḍira, Lord Śaṅkara Mahādeva himself dwells in full glory; may the blessings of Lambodara Gaṇeśa ever abide here.Verse 3:May horses and elephants playfully roam here; may dancers perform in every direction; may hymns, devotional songs, andpurāṇarecitations resound daily; may children and subjects remain ever joyful; may kinsmen and women vie in beauty; and may all reside fearlessly in thisJayamaṇḍira, thereby increasing its glory (kīrti)."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/4ef6a4bb-88e5-4b4c-a1c7-9e4fb4553a45> ;
    rdfs:comment "Verse 1:In the year 1776 CE (ŚS 1698), on an auspicious day in the month of Kārtika, under theUttarabhādrapadāconstellation and the holy occasion ofHaribodhinī Ekādaśī, when the moon was in Mīnarāśi, and both Jupiter (Guru) and Venus (Śukra) were in favorable positions—at that propitious moment, the minister Śrīkīrtisiṃha commenced the construction of this grand Jaya Maṇḍira.Verse 2:The king, sovereign of the Gaurśācala realm, had a contented land and a joyous populace. His minister, the learned and valiant Kīrtisiṃha, was served by his attendant, Sarūpasiṃha. In thisJayamaṇḍira, Lord Śaṅkara Mahādeva himself dwells in full glory; may the blessings of Lambodara Gaṇeśa ever abide here.Verse 3:May horses and elephants playfully roam here; may dancers perform in every direction; may hymns, devotional songs, andpurāṇarecitations resound daily; may children and subjects remain ever joyful; may kinsmen and women vie in beauty; and may all reside fearlessly in thisJayamaṇḍira, thereby increasing its glory (kīrti)."@en ;
