<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/503085f6-076f-11ea-8a1c-0242ac130002_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Construction of a  small water tank representing the Capĩgāḥ"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The traditional Capĩgāḥ was covered up during the road construction process. Its name arises from the Newari language, in which a mud mound with grass on top of it is calledcapĩand the water which is stored in a pit is calledcapĩgāḥ. A small water tank has been built 1 m away from the original Capĩgāḥ’s location."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/503085f6-076f-11ea-8a1c-0242ac130002> ;
    rdfs:comment "The traditional Capĩgāḥ was covered up during the road construction process. Its name arises from the Newari language, in which a mud mound with grass on top of it is calledcapĩand the water which is stored in a pit is calledcapĩgāḥ. A small water tank has been built 1 m away from the original Capĩgāḥ’s location."@en ;
