<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/511d9122-2ce9-498a-bac6-0c9b11c528e6_1> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Reconstruction of the monument"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Even though thephalcāwas not heavily damaged in the 2015 CE earthquake (VS 2072), it was reconstructed by the Madhyapura Thimi Municipality in 2024 CE (VS 2080). As discussed above in 'Description', the elders used to say that there had once been ahitiin the phalcā, and people also used to call it Hitiphalcā. Based on this, the reconstruction plan was modified. Using the water stream, a new hiti was included in the design of thephalcā. As part of the reconstruction, the original structure of thephalcāwas slightly changed."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/511d9122-2ce9-498a-bac6-0c9b11c528e6> ;
    rdfs:comment "Even though thephalcāwas not heavily damaged in the 2015 CE earthquake (VS 2072), it was reconstructed by the Madhyapura Thimi Municipality in 2024 CE (VS 2080). As discussed above in 'Description', the elders used to say that there had once been ahitiin the phalcā, and people also used to call it Hitiphalcā. Based on this, the reconstruction plan was modified. Using the water stream, a new hiti was included in the design of thephalcā. As part of the reconstruction, the original structure of thephalcāwas slightly changed."@en ;
