        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Establishment of Śiva, Garuḍanārāyaṇa and Pāñcāyaṇa statues"@en ;
    dcterms:description "This inscription records Gaṃgārāma Bhāro and Purandra Bhāro, two brothers from Bhaktpur’s Yāchẽ Ṭola, installing statues of Śiva, Garuḍanārāyaṇa, and Pāñcāyana. The Śiva statue they installed may be the Umāmaheśvara statue in thehiticomplex, and the Garuḍanārāyaṇa likely refers to the Lakṣmīnārāyaṇa statue, as the inscription is carved beside it. However, the Pāñcāyana statues, which include Gaṇeśa, Sūrya, Viṣṇu, and Durgā, are not visible in the complex."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/5168f38a-94c4-4e8e-995c-ab7e0e1f11ba> ;
    rdfs:comment "This inscription records Gaṃgārāma Bhāro and Purandra Bhāro, two brothers from Bhaktpur’s Yāchẽ Ṭola, installing statues of Śiva, Garuḍanārāyaṇa, and Pāñcāyana. The Śiva statue they installed may be the Umāmaheśvara statue in thehiticomplex, and the Garuḍanārāyaṇa likely refers to the Lakṣmīnārāyaṇa statue, as the inscription is carved beside it. However, the Pāñcāyana statues, which include Gaṇeśa, Sūrya, Viṣṇu, and Durgā, are not visible in the complex."@en ;
