<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/517a1bd2-2894-4d02-a2a7-9a8d0ff28cff_1> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Repair of the temple"@en ;
    dcterms:description "During the reign of King Raṇabahādura Śāha, Bhīma Ṭaksārī (chief officer of the mint) undertook the renovation of theNaksāla Bhagavatītemple. He performedpūjāandyajñato various deities and Brahmins, gave generous sacrificial fees, and completed the restoration in a proper ritual manner. The supervision of the work was carried out by Prema Giri Gusāiṃ. Since the inscription states that bricks were used in the renovation, it suggests that prior to Bhīma Ṭaksārī’s intervention, the temple had been constructed using other materials."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/517a1bd2-2894-4d02-a2a7-9a8d0ff28cff> ;
    rdfs:comment "During the reign of King Raṇabahādura Śāha, Bhīma Ṭaksārī (chief officer of the mint) undertook the renovation of theNaksāla Bhagavatītemple. He performedpūjāandyajñato various deities and Brahmins, gave generous sacrificial fees, and completed the restoration in a proper ritual manner. The supervision of the work was carried out by Prema Giri Gusāiṃ. Since the inscription states that bricks were used in the renovation, it suggests that prior to Bhīma Ṭaksārī’s intervention, the temple had been constructed using other materials."@en ;
