        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Construction of a sataḥ"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Bhīma Ṣavāsa (Khavāsa) of Makhan Tole, Kathmandu, constructed asataḥ(resting platform) in front of the Naksāla Bhagavatī temple at his own expense from the property he possessed. The work was supervised by Dhanadatta Newār from Asan. The Bhīma Ṭaksārī who renovated the temple in 1782 CE (VS 1839) and Bhīma Ṣavāsa who built thesataḥappear to be the same individual."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/517a1bd2-2894-4d02-a2a7-9a8d0ff28cff> ;
    rdfs:comment "Bhīma Ṣavāsa (Khavāsa) of Makhan Tole, Kathmandu, constructed asataḥ(resting platform) in front of the Naksāla Bhagavatī temple at his own expense from the property he possessed. The work was supervised by Dhanadatta Newār from Asan. The Bhīma Ṭaksārī who renovated the temple in 1782 CE (VS 1839) and Bhīma Ṣavāsa who built thesataḥappear to be the same individual."@en ;
