        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Unclear"@en ;
    dcterms:description "An inscription records that Nārān (Nārāyaṇa) and Sīva (Śiva), descendants of Kājī Bhīmā, jointly carried out restoration work, though the inscription does not specify what exactly was restored. Since the inscription is carved on ajaḥdhun, it is probable that they renovated the water spout itself. The Kājī Bhīmā mentioned in the inscription could well be the same Bhīma Ṭaksārī who renovated the temple in 1782 CE (VS 1839)."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/517a1bd2-2894-4d02-a2a7-9a8d0ff28cff> ;
