<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/5394724d-7746-4a10-be2a-d8ea3c79bc18_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Consecration ;
    rdfs:label "Consecration of the statue"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The inscription on the pedestal of the Kālabhairava statue documents its consecration during the reign of King Lakṣmīnarasiṃha Malla (r. 1619-1641 CE). Despite erosion obscuring parts of the inscription, the term \"jajamāna,\" meaning \"the sponsor,\" is discernible before the donor's name. This indicates that the donor was an ordinary citizen, not a member of the royal family."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/5394724d-7746-4a10-be2a-d8ea3c79bc18> ;
    rdfs:comment "The inscription on the pedestal of the Kālabhairava statue documents its consecration during the reign of King Lakṣmīnarasiṃha Malla (r. 1619-1641 CE). Despite erosion obscuring parts of the inscription, the term \"jajamāna,\" meaning \"the sponsor,\" is discernible before the donor's name. This indicates that the donor was an ordinary citizen, not a member of the royal family."@en ;
