<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/54612871-717c-41e1-9a91-cf77d1267bad_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Installation of donor statues"@en ;
    dcterms:description "On the southern wall of the circumambulatory path of thepīṭha, there is a sculpture carved on a single stone slab depicting six figures in the gesture of reverence (namaskāra mudrā). This sculpture was installed in the name of Mahādeva and Caṇḍeśvarī. Among the donors’ names, Manisiṃ (Maṇisiṃha) can be read."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/54612871-717c-41e1-9a91-cf77d1267bad> ;
    rdfs:comment "On the southern wall of the circumambulatory path of thepīṭha, there is a sculpture carved on a single stone slab depicting six figures in the gesture of reverence (namaskāra mudrā). This sculpture was installed in the name of Mahādeva and Caṇḍeśvarī. Among the donors’ names, Manisiṃ (Maṇisiṃha) can be read."@en ;
