<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/54612871-717c-41e1-9a91-cf77d1267bad_4> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Enshrinement ;
    rdfs:label "Addition of a stone toraṇa"@en ;
    dcterms:description "This inscription is located on thetoraṇapositioned on the upper part of a small stone shrine constructed around the central area where the aniconic stone of the goddess is enshrined at the Caṇḍeśvarī pīṭha. Apart from the complete date NS 809 recorded in the inscription, the remaining text cannot be clearly read or meaningfully interpreted. Among the names of the donors, Manasiṃ (Manasiṃha) can be read."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/54612871-717c-41e1-9a91-cf77d1267bad> ;
    rdfs:comment "This inscription is located on thetoraṇapositioned on the upper part of a small stone shrine constructed around the central area where the aniconic stone of the goddess is enshrined at the Caṇḍeśvarī pīṭha. Apart from the complete date NS 809 recorded in the inscription, the remaining text cannot be clearly read or meaningfully interpreted. Among the names of the donors, Manasiṃ (Manasiṃha) can be read."@en ;
