<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/54612871-717c-41e1-9a91-cf77d1267bad_8> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Unknown event"@en ;
    dcterms:description "This inscription is preserved inside aphalcāwithin the Caṇḍeśvarī precinct. A trident is carved at the upper part of the inscription, while donor family figures carved in thenamaskāraposture appear in the lower part. Based on its overall characteristics, this inscription can be identified as belonging to the Late Medieval period. However, since all of its letters have been severely eroded, the written information has become unknown."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/54612871-717c-41e1-9a91-cf77d1267bad> ;
    rdfs:comment "This inscription is preserved inside aphalcāwithin the Caṇḍeśvarī precinct. A trident is carved at the upper part of the inscription, while donor family figures carved in thenamaskāraposture appear in the lower part. Based on its overall characteristics, this inscription can be identified as belonging to the Late Medieval period. However, since all of its letters have been severely eroded, the written information has become unknown."@en ;
