<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/54903008-fc04-46aa-92ac-9b991108224b_1> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Consecration ;
    rdfs:label "Initial construction of the temple, consecration of statues of Mādhavanārayaṇa and Hanumān and land endowment"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Five brothers, including Harikṛṣṇa Bhāro of Dhvakara Ṭola in Sankhu, commissioned the construction of thisśikhara-style temple during the reign of King Bhūpālendra Malla in 1699 CE (NS 819). They also consecrated statues of Viśveśvara Mahādeva, Mādhava Nārāyaṇa (SKH0020-004), and Hanumān (SKH0020-006) on the same occasion, in memory of their parents Madhusudana and Lakṣmīmayi. Upon completion the temple, they endowed several plots of land in order to serve as sources of income for conducting its anniversary celebrations and other obligatory and occasional rituals."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/54903008-fc04-46aa-92ac-9b991108224b> ;
    rdfs:comment "Five brothers, including Harikṛṣṇa Bhāro of Dhvakara Ṭola in Sankhu, commissioned the construction of thisśikhara-style temple during the reign of King Bhūpālendra Malla in 1699 CE (NS 819). They also consecrated statues of Viśveśvara Mahādeva, Mādhava Nārāyaṇa (SKH0020-004), and Hanumān (SKH0020-006) on the same occasion, in memory of their parents Madhusudana and Lakṣmīmayi. Upon completion the temple, they endowed several plots of land in order to serve as sources of income for conducting its anniversary celebrations and other obligatory and occasional rituals."@en ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/agent/antigravity_agent> ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/activity/heritagegraph_kg_construction> ;
