    rdfs:label "Pekhaḥ Jātrā age"@en ;
    dcterms:description "According to the Devamālā Vaṃśāvalī, King Ratna Malla established this village with 300 houses in 1513. He initiated an annual procession on the full moon day of Caitra, and it is likely that this procession was known as Pekhaḥ Jātrā back then."@en ;
