<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/5555d2e1-1920-41fb-a839-3f3acbcd7933_1> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Empact of 1934 CE earthquake on the Bell"@en ;
    dcterms:description "As recorded in the later chronicleDevamālāvaṃśāvalī, a chain of the bell broke in 1933 CE (VS 1990) due to the earthquake's effect. Consequently, the practice of ringing the big bell twice daily was suspended. The tradition was reinstated a year later following the completion of necessary renovations."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/5555d2e1-1920-41fb-a839-3f3acbcd7933> ;
    rdfs:comment "As recorded in the later chronicleDevamālāvaṃśāvalī, a chain of the bell broke in 1933 CE (VS 1990) due to the earthquake's effect. Consequently, the practice of ringing the big bell twice daily was suspended. The tradition was reinstated a year later following the completion of necessary renovations."@en ;
