<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/5555d2e1-1920-41fb-a839-3f3acbcd7933_2> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Restoration and continuation of bell ringing tradition"@en ;
    dcterms:description "After a prolonged interruption, the practice of daily bell ringing was reestablished in 2009 CE (VS 2066). Presently, as of March 2023 CE, Bābukṛṣṇa Maharjana from Damāī ṭola in Kathmandu undertakes the responsibility of ringing the Taḥgaḥ Gaṃ every morning at 9 am, performing 108 strikes. In recognition of this duty, he receives NRs. 7,000 for each morning's bell ringing session."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/5555d2e1-1920-41fb-a839-3f3acbcd7933> ;
    rdfs:comment "After a prolonged interruption, the practice of daily bell ringing was reestablished in 2009 CE (VS 2066). Presently, as of March 2023 CE, Bābukṛṣṇa Maharjana from Damāī ṭola in Kathmandu undertakes the responsibility of ringing the Taḥgaḥ Gaṃ every morning at 9 am, performing 108 strikes. In recognition of this duty, he receives NRs. 7,000 for each morning's bell ringing session."@en ;
