<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/55be585c-411d-48dd-be74-5cd78f2723e1_1> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Installation of a hydrant (kaladhārā)"@en ;
    dcterms:description "A stone inscription is installed on the eastern side of the Ārīthāy Jaḥdhuṃhiti, but it does not belong to the Hiti itself.  The inscription recounts the history of water management in Kirtipur. Since Kirtipur always had shortage of water sources, Juhārī Kumārī, mother of Prime Minister Juddha Śamśera expressed her interest in supplying water to this area. However, she passed away before her interest was materialized. Therefore, her son constructed this hydrant under discussion in memory of his mother and named it after her as ‘Juhārī Kumārī Dhārā’ (see the inscription below)."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/55be585c-411d-48dd-be74-5cd78f2723e1> ;
    rdfs:comment "A stone inscription is installed on the eastern side of the Ārīthāy Jaḥdhuṃhiti, but it does not belong to the Hiti itself.  The inscription recounts the history of water management in Kirtipur. Since Kirtipur always had shortage of water sources, Juhārī Kumārī, mother of Prime Minister Juddha Śamśera expressed her interest in supplying water to this area. However, she passed away before her interest was materialized. Therefore, her son constructed this hydrant under discussion in memory of his mother and named it after her as ‘Juhārī Kumārī Dhārā’ (see the inscription below)."@en ;
