<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/55c2256a-b076-4719-a982-6befe237ff96_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Initial construction"@en ;
    dcterms:description "While there is no inscription that records the temple’s construction, two stones—one in the southeast plinth and another above the door—bear the date “Samvat787,” aligning with Śrīnivāsa Malla’s rule. With the lack of historical sources, the identity of its builder in unknown, but the area was home to affluent communities like Jośī, Pradhāna, and Śreṣṭha castes during the Malla period, suggesting a wealthy patron from the area funded it."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/55c2256a-b076-4719-a982-6befe237ff96> ;
    rdfs:comment "While there is no inscription that records the temple’s construction, two stones—one in the southeast plinth and another above the door—bear the date “Samvat787,” aligning with Śrīnivāsa Malla’s rule. With the lack of historical sources, the identity of its builder in unknown, but the area was home to affluent communities like Jośī, Pradhāna, and Śreṣṭha castes during the Malla period, suggesting a wealthy patron from the area funded it."@en ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/agent/antigravity_agent> ;
