<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/56bfc1ff-204d-452c-8c3c-fda34dadc1e1_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Initial Construction and Icon Installation"@en ;
    dcterms:description "In 1649 CE (NS 769), King Pratāpa Malla undertook the construction of the temple and placed a statue of Kṛṣṇa, accompanied by his consorts, within the sanctum. This arrangement symbolized the king's desire to replicate himself and commemorate his two deceased queens, Rūpamatī and Rājamatī."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/56bfc1ff-204d-452c-8c3c-fda34dadc1e1> ;
    rdfs:comment "In 1649 CE (NS 769), King Pratāpa Malla undertook the construction of the temple and placed a statue of Kṛṣṇa, accompanied by his consorts, within the sanctum. This arrangement symbolized the king's desire to replicate himself and commemorate his two deceased queens, Rūpamatī and Rājamatī."@en ;
