<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/5790999f-7d84-4dc0-b4a9-a65dee5d1481_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Earthquake Damages"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The roof of the temple can be seen completely damaged in the 1850s painting of Henry Ambrose Oldfield (see,http://www.bl.uk/onlinegallery/onlineex/apac/other/019wdz000002844u00000000.html; accessed on 21.10.2020). It is probable that the temple collapsed during the 1833 CE earthquakes and was not renovated until 1850s."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/5790999f-7d84-4dc0-b4a9-a65dee5d1481> ;
    rdfs:comment "The roof of the temple can be seen completely damaged in the 1850s painting of Henry Ambrose Oldfield (see,http://www.bl.uk/onlinegallery/onlineex/apac/other/019wdz000002844u00000000.html; accessed on 21.10.2020). It is probable that the temple collapsed during the 1833 CE earthquakes and was not renovated until 1850s."@en ;
