<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/57a467a3-03bc-4f00-9023-5f839dffc4bf_5> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Unknown event"@en ;
    dcterms:description "On the southern side of the carved stonetoraṇafeaturingChepuinstalled above thepīṭha, an inscription reading “Kājimāna Dhanathakũ” is found. Below this inscription, sculpted figures of a couple innamaskāra mudrāare visible. On this basis, it may be concluded that the toraṇa was offered through the joint contribution of the couple named Kājimāna and Dhanathakũ."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/57a467a3-03bc-4f00-9023-5f839dffc4bf> ;
    rdfs:comment "On the southern side of the carved stonetoraṇafeaturingChepuinstalled above thepīṭha, an inscription reading “Kājimāna Dhanathakũ” is found. Below this inscription, sculpted figures of a couple innamaskāra mudrāare visible. On this basis, it may be concluded that the toraṇa was offered through the joint contribution of the couple named Kājimāna and Dhanathakũ."@en ;
