<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/57a467a3-03bc-4f00-9023-5f839dffc4bf_6> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Unknown event"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Directly in front of the Bālakumārī pīṭha, an upright stone slab with a smalltoraṇahas been installed. Such stone slabs are commonly found atpīṭhas. At the center of this stone, the inscription “Kājimānaṃ Prīti” is carved, which indicates that it was offered by Kājimāna. Below the inscription, a carved triangular symbol can also be seen, which represents a symbolic emblem of the goddess."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/57a467a3-03bc-4f00-9023-5f839dffc4bf> ;
    rdfs:comment "Directly in front of the Bālakumārī pīṭha, an upright stone slab with a smalltoraṇahas been installed. Such stone slabs are commonly found atpīṭhas. At the center of this stone, the inscription “Kājimānaṃ Prīti” is carved, which indicates that it was offered by Kājimāna. Below the inscription, a carved triangular symbol can also be seen, which represents a symbolic emblem of the goddess."@en ;
