<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/5a5dd034-c2c9-494a-ba90-c99c59fdd41e_3> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:TransferOfCustody ;
    rdfs:label "Construction of a capāḥ"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Mucā Bhāro of Thã Bahī (Thamel) constructed a capāḥ on the eastern side of the open ground of Indrāyaṇī. He also endowed land to support the annual rituals associated with the newly built capāḥ. The inscription stipulates that, after his death, apiṇḍashould be offered annually on the anniversary of his passing from the income generated by the endowed land. Additionally, it prescribes offerings to be made on the occasion of the Indrāyaṇī palanquin festival."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/5a5dd034-c2c9-494a-ba90-c99c59fdd41e> ;
    rdfs:comment "Mucā Bhāro of Thã Bahī (Thamel) constructed a capāḥ on the eastern side of the open ground of Indrāyaṇī. He also endowed land to support the annual rituals associated with the newly built capāḥ. The inscription stipulates that, after his death, apiṇḍashould be offered annually on the anniversary of his passing from the income generated by the endowed land. Additionally, it prescribes offerings to be made on the occasion of the Indrāyaṇī palanquin festival."@en ;
