<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/5bfb6d40-eb4c-11e9-b125-0242ac130002_2> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Unknown event"@en ;
    dcterms:description "A tiled pedestal to the east of the temple supports a kneeling Garuḍa whose hands are held in thenamaskāragesture (mudrā). Two stone steles depicting donor figures and an inscription are embedded below the Garuḍa, in two niches on the west side of the pedestal. The stone inscription can no longer be clearly read. The date NS 913 is legible and might relate to the year when the Garuḍa was installed."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/5bfb6d40-eb4c-11e9-b125-0242ac130002> ;
    rdfs:comment "A tiled pedestal to the east of the temple supports a kneeling Garuḍa whose hands are held in thenamaskāragesture (mudrā). Two stone steles depicting donor figures and an inscription are embedded below the Garuḍa, in two niches on the west side of the pedestal. The stone inscription can no longer be clearly read. The date NS 913 is legible and might relate to the year when the Garuḍa was installed."@en ;
