<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/5c063668-e5f6-11e9-b125-0242ac130002_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Initial construction of the monument"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The monument was constructed in 1675 by two ministers of King Śrīnivāsa Malla. One was Bhagīratha Bhaiyāer (cautārā). The kings and princesses of Lalitpur, Kantipur and Bhaktapur including Bhaiyā(?) Rudrasena of Tanahu attended the inauguration ceremony of the Pāṭī.AYajñaritual was also performed at the same time. A person named Rājavãśa Rāvatta Narasiṁha is mentioned as the caretaker (chintāyāka) of the construction work.The inscription established in Taḥ Bahāḥ by order of King Śrīnivāsa Malla gives us a hint that the King placed great trust in Bhagīratha. Part of the inscription reads: “I see no difference between me and Bhagīratha Bhaiyā, [therefore] others also should not see any difference between him and me” (seeVajrācāryaVS 2056, 173 for the inscription). King Yoganarendra Malla, who succeeded Śrīnivāsa, accused Bhagīratha of mistreating the former’s queens and dismissed him from his post on the 5th bright fortnight of Māgha in NS 804 (seeRegmi1966, appendix III, p. 96). Bhagīratha Bhaiyā was killed by order of Yoganarendra on the 3rd dark fortnight of Bhādra in NS 805 (Regmi1966, appendix III, p. 95)."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/5c063668-e5f6-11e9-b125-0242ac130002> ;
    rdfs:comment "The monument was constructed in 1675 by two ministers of King Śrīnivāsa Malla. One was Bhagīratha Bhaiyāer (cautārā). The kings and princesses of Lalitpur, Kantipur and Bhaktapur including Bhaiyā(?) Rudrasena of Tanahu attended the inauguration ceremony of the Pāṭī.AYajñaritual was also performed at the same time. A person named Rājavãśa Rāvatta Narasiṁha is mentioned as the caretaker (chintāyāka) of the construction work.The inscription established in Taḥ Bahāḥ by order of King Śrīnivāsa Malla gives us a hint that the King placed great trust in Bhagīratha. Part of the inscription reads: “I see no difference between me and Bhagīratha Bhaiyā, [therefore] others also should not see any difference between him and me” (seeVajrācāryaVS 2056, 173 for the inscription). King Yoganarendra Malla, who succeeded Śrīnivāsa, accused Bhagīratha of mistreating the former’s queens and dismissed him from his post on the 5th bright fortnight of Māgha in NS 804 (seeRegmi1966, appendix III, p. 96). Bhagīratha Bhaiyā was killed by order of Yoganarendra on the 3rd dark fortnight of Bhādra in NS 805 (Regmi1966, appendix III, p. 95)."@en ;
