<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/5c063668-e5f6-11e9-b125-0242ac130002_3> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Restoration"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The Pāṭī was dismantled in 1994 and rebuilt with projecting windows and a pinnacle. The work was finished in 1995 with financial support from GTZ/UDLE.Gutschow(2011) reports that the upper storey with its projecting windows and the pinnacle were (re)constructed in 1995 with Henry Ambrose Oldfield's watercolour of 1855 used as a blueprint."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/5c063668-e5f6-11e9-b125-0242ac130002> ;
    rdfs:comment "The Pāṭī was dismantled in 1994 and rebuilt with projecting windows and a pinnacle. The work was finished in 1995 with financial support from GTZ/UDLE.Gutschow(2011) reports that the upper storey with its projecting windows and the pinnacle were (re)constructed in 1995 with Henry Ambrose Oldfield's watercolour of 1855 used as a blueprint."@en ;
