        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Nāgasādhanā (Invocation of Serpents)"@en ;
    dcterms:description "During the reign of King Viśṇu Malla (1729-1745 CE), a famine broke out. The king made Sarvānanda Paṇḍita of Mahābauddha performpuraścaraṇaandnāgasādhanā(invocation of serpents) at Kvāche Bālakaumārī shrine. It rained following the rituals."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/5cb98dcd-6658-4b9c-8990-8c2299397aca> ;
