    rdfs:label "Unknown event"@en ;
    dcterms:description "This weathered stone inscription is no longer in readable condition. The few letters that can be deciphered indicate that three donors jointly arranged a certain worship. Locals mention that this inscription was originally placed under a large nettle tree near the Candanabharāṭeśvara temple (Ś. Rupākhetī and Ś. Rājavaṃśī VS 2053, p. 85)."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/5d9e8143-340e-4846-a7a9-4f95bfc10421> ;
