<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/5d9e8143-340e-4846-a7a9-4f95bfc10421_2> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Reconstruction of the temple"@en ;
    dcterms:description "PātravaṃśaRāutaVaikuṇṭha Bhāro, a resident of Datalhāche in Dhvākhābāhāra, constructed the temple for theśivaliṅgaand established a trust. Over time, the temple built by Vaikuṇṭha Bhāro fell into disrepair and was destroyed. Later, Lakṣmīrāja Bhāro, the grandson of Vaikuṇṭha Bhāro, reconstructed the temple, after Candanabharāṭeśvara Mahādeva appeared in a dream and instructed him to rebuild the temple. After consulting with his mother Lakṣmī and brother Lakṣmīdhara, he obtained permission from King Yoganarendra Malla and reconstructed the temple, while also offering a golden finial. Upon completion, Rāmacandra, a brahmin from Bakhanimha Ṭola in Lalitpur, performed a fire ritual."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/5d9e8143-340e-4846-a7a9-4f95bfc10421> ;
    rdfs:comment "PātravaṃśaRāutaVaikuṇṭha Bhāro, a resident of Datalhāche in Dhvākhābāhāra, constructed the temple for theśivaliṅgaand established a trust. Over time, the temple built by Vaikuṇṭha Bhāro fell into disrepair and was destroyed. Later, Lakṣmīrāja Bhāro, the grandson of Vaikuṇṭha Bhāro, reconstructed the temple, after Candanabharāṭeśvara Mahādeva appeared in a dream and instructed him to rebuild the temple. After consulting with his mother Lakṣmī and brother Lakṣmīdhara, he obtained permission from King Yoganarendra Malla and reconstructed the temple, while also offering a golden finial. Upon completion, Rāmacandra, a brahmin from Bakhanimha Ṭola in Lalitpur, performed a fire ritual."@en ;
