<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/5fadd6dc-06b1-11ea-8a1c-0242ac130002_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Construction of water spout"@en ;
    dcterms:description "There is a stone inscription on the southern side of the Jaḥrūhiti. This inscription is not related to this monument but rather recounts the history of water management in this area. Because the Sunaguthi residents had no source of clean water, they were forced to drink water from the well. Juddha Śamśera's mother Juhārī Kumārī expressed interest in constructing a water spout in the Sunāguthi area. However, she passed away before she could carry this work out. After her death, her son Juddha Śamśera constructed a water spout to fulfill his late mother's wish."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/5fadd6dc-06b1-11ea-8a1c-0242ac130002> ;
    rdfs:comment "There is a stone inscription on the southern side of the Jaḥrūhiti. This inscription is not related to this monument but rather recounts the history of water management in this area. Because the Sunaguthi residents had no source of clean water, they were forced to drink water from the well. Juddha Śamśera's mother Juhārī Kumārī expressed interest in constructing a water spout in the Sunāguthi area. However, she passed away before she could carry this work out. After her death, her son Juddha Śamśera constructed a water spout to fulfill his late mother's wish."@en ;
