<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/600ba6fa-8f77-11ea-bd59-0242ac130005_1> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Construction of a new phalcā"@en ;
    dcterms:description "An inscription on a marble slab attests to the construction of the newphalcāin VS 2058 (ca. 2001 CE) by Surajanātha, the third son of a certain Viṣṇucandra. It mentions that the originalphalcābuilt in VS 1981 (ca. 1924 CE) had collapsed. It is said to have been commissioned by Hirālāla, Viṣṇucandra, and Venimādho Rauniyāra, the three sons of Vaccurāma. Later on, thephalcāwas renovated by Śivaprasāda, the elder son of Viṣṇucandra. The VS 2058 reconstruction was supported by Surajanātha, the third son of Viṣṇucandra. It is further mentioned that the land located to the west of Silkhu Phalcā was bestowed upon thephalcāto support its religious functions and upkeep."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/600ba6fa-8f77-11ea-bd59-0242ac130005> ;
    rdfs:comment "An inscription on a marble slab attests to the construction of the newphalcāin VS 2058 (ca. 2001 CE) by Surajanātha, the third son of a certain Viṣṇucandra. It mentions that the originalphalcābuilt in VS 1981 (ca. 1924 CE) had collapsed. It is said to have been commissioned by Hirālāla, Viṣṇucandra, and Venimādho Rauniyāra, the three sons of Vaccurāma. Later on, thephalcāwas renovated by Śivaprasāda, the elder son of Viṣṇucandra. The VS 2058 reconstruction was supported by Surajanātha, the third son of Viṣṇucandra. It is further mentioned that the land located to the west of Silkhu Phalcā was bestowed upon thephalcāto support its religious functions and upkeep."@en ;
