<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/60d8283f-d7d3-4f40-a552-d9e2843a56b6_1> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:TransferOfCustody ;
    rdfs:label "Additional land grant to Hanumantasiṃha"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Hanumantasiṃha Amātya received an additional 25ropanīs of land grant. It was stipulated that anyone settling on this land had to maintain the bridge. That same year, he, along with his brothers—Bhājudhana, Sadāśiva, and Lakṣmīnarasiṃha—established statues of Hanumaṃteśvara Mahādeva, Kṛṣṇa, Gaṇeśa, Bhagavatī, Kaumārī, Naṭyeśvara, Sarasvatī, and others, and also built asataḥ. Matching his own name, he established the Hanumaṃteśvara Mahādeva and Hanumān."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/60d8283f-d7d3-4f40-a552-d9e2843a56b6> ;
    rdfs:comment "Hanumantasiṃha Amātya received an additional 25ropanīs of land grant. It was stipulated that anyone settling on this land had to maintain the bridge. That same year, he, along with his brothers—Bhājudhana, Sadāśiva, and Lakṣmīnarasiṃha—established statues of Hanumaṃteśvara Mahādeva, Kṛṣṇa, Gaṇeśa, Bhagavatī, Kaumārī, Naṭyeśvara, Sarasvatī, and others, and also built asataḥ. Matching his own name, he established the Hanumaṃteśvara Mahādeva and Hanumān."@en ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/agent/antigravity_agent> ;
