<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/61f58f93-7a18-4ef9-9597-0e85aec09513_4> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Consecration ;
    rdfs:label "Consecration of a new statue of Gaṇeśa"@en ;
    dcterms:description "In 2011 CE (VS 2067), a fire broke out at the residence of the temple's caretaker located in Tāhāḥ Nani, resulting in the destruction of the Gaṇeśa statue that was used for the annual procession, as well as its jewelry. A new statue and jewelry were made to replace the ones that were destroyed. Afterward, it was decided that the statue and jewelry would be kept at thetvāḥchẽinstead of the residence of the temple's caretaker, to ensure their safety and accessibility to the local community during festivals and other important occasions."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/61f58f93-7a18-4ef9-9597-0e85aec09513> ;
    rdfs:comment "In 2011 CE (VS 2067), a fire broke out at the residence of the temple's caretaker located in Tāhāḥ Nani, resulting in the destruction of the Gaṇeśa statue that was used for the annual procession, as well as its jewelry. A new statue and jewelry were made to replace the ones that were destroyed. Afterward, it was decided that the statue and jewelry would be kept at thetvāḥchẽinstead of the residence of the temple's caretaker, to ensure their safety and accessibility to the local community during festivals and other important occasions."@en ;
