<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/62c22c28-9633-4f6d-a6e2-f942cf73af1c_2> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Consecration ;
    rdfs:label "Reconsecration (prāṇapratiṣṭhā)"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Upon the initiation of the Jayavāgīśvarī Ṭola Sudhāra Samiti, a local committee formed for the preservation of the area, Rāmakumāra Śreṣṭha and his wife Sīta Śreṣṭha performed the reconsecration of both the Pādaveśvara Śivaliṅga and the temple. Interestingly, the inscription makes mention of theśivaliṅgaas Pādaveśvara. It is possible that theśivaliṅgawithin the sanctum was temporarily removed during the temple's reconstruction, and the inscription was installed after theśivaliṅgaunderwent reconsecration following the completion of the rebuilding. However, it's worth noting that the inscription does not contain any reference to the reconstruction itself."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/62c22c28-9633-4f6d-a6e2-f942cf73af1c> ;
    rdfs:comment "Upon the initiation of the Jayavāgīśvarī Ṭola Sudhāra Samiti, a local committee formed for the preservation of the area, Rāmakumāra Śreṣṭha and his wife Sīta Śreṣṭha performed the reconsecration of both the Pādaveśvara Śivaliṅga and the temple. Interestingly, the inscription makes mention of theśivaliṅgaas Pādaveśvara. It is possible that theśivaliṅgawithin the sanctum was temporarily removed during the temple's reconstruction, and the inscription was installed after theśivaliṅgaunderwent reconsecration following the completion of the rebuilding. However, it's worth noting that the inscription does not contain any reference to the reconstruction itself."@en ;
