        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Addition of a pillar"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Local administrators who took the surname “Duvāra” have been there in Pāṃgā since the Malla period. This inscription at thepīṭhamentions that a certain Beṣārāma Bhāro Duvāla and Devarānimayī erected a Garuḍa pillar. Statues of the two are installed beneath the pillar."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/655e33f0-7d0e-4011-8ec7-816ef7b3f8ab> ;
    rdfs:comment "Local administrators who took the surname “Duvāra” have been there in Pāṃgā since the Malla period. This inscription at thepīṭhamentions that a certain Beṣārāma Bhāro Duvāla and Devarānimayī erected a Garuḍa pillar. Statues of the two are installed beneath the pillar."@en ;
