<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/6594f9ac-fb26-4e95-8c0e-4957e705df7c_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Restoration of the phalcā"@en ;
    dcterms:description "This inscription records the restoration of thephalcāin 1980 which seems unlikely since at this time thephalcāwould not have been older than 7 years. It is possible that the inscription actually refers to the reconstruction of the Samay Phalca (LAL4317) that used to be located just to the south. Could it be that Samay Phalcā was demolished in the late 1970s and subsequently rebuilt in 1980 CE as Nāmasaṅgīti Phalcā, about 10 metres further to the north?"@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/6594f9ac-fb26-4e95-8c0e-4957e705df7c> ;
    rdfs:comment "This inscription records the restoration of thephalcāin 1980 which seems unlikely since at this time thephalcāwould not have been older than 7 years. It is possible that the inscription actually refers to the reconstruction of the Samay Phalca (LAL4317) that used to be located just to the south. Could it be that Samay Phalcā was demolished in the late 1970s and subsequently rebuilt in 1980 CE as Nāmasaṅgīti Phalcā, about 10 metres further to the north?"@en ;
