<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/6700e6dc-ad31-11ea-8ae7-0242ac130005_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Enshrinement ;
    rdfs:label "Donation of strut (initial construction of the temple?)"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The inscription probably documents the donation of the strut by Viṣṇu Māhāta (text: Viṣṇa Māhāta) in 1668 CE (NS 788), offering it as a dedication to Harisiddhi (text: Harasiddhi). Given that this inscription is the earliest known record associated with the temple, it's plausible that the temple itself might have been built during that same year. However, the precise connection between the temple and Harisiddhi, the deity enshrined in a temple situated approximately 8 kilometers southeast of the capital, remains unclear."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/6700e6dc-ad31-11ea-8ae7-0242ac130005> ;
    rdfs:comment "The inscription probably documents the donation of the strut by Viṣṇu Māhāta (text: Viṣṇa Māhāta) in 1668 CE (NS 788), offering it as a dedication to Harisiddhi (text: Harasiddhi). Given that this inscription is the earliest known record associated with the temple, it's plausible that the temple itself might have been built during that same year. However, the precise connection between the temple and Harisiddhi, the deity enshrined in a temple situated approximately 8 kilometers southeast of the capital, remains unclear."@en ;
