<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/672baa74-d5b1-453d-ab12-d3194c3e5976_1> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Renovation of the temple"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Bhājudhana Bhāro of Taṃgaḥ Ṭola renovated the Ādinārāyaṇa and Śiva temples in memory of his late wife, Dhana Thakunī. The Ādinārāyaṇa temple mentioned in the inscription likely refers to the present Hariśaṅkara temple. Similarly, the Śiva temple referred to in the inscription was probably theśikhara-style Śiva temple located south of the Hariśaṅkara temple."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/672baa74-d5b1-453d-ab12-d3194c3e5976> ;
    rdfs:comment "Bhājudhana Bhāro of Taṃgaḥ Ṭola renovated the Ādinārāyaṇa and Śiva temples in memory of his late wife, Dhana Thakunī. The Ādinārāyaṇa temple mentioned in the inscription likely refers to the present Hariśaṅkara temple. Similarly, the Śiva temple referred to in the inscription was probably theśikhara-style Śiva temple located south of the Hariśaṅkara temple."@en ;
