<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/673afbfc-e6f2-11e9-8bc4-0242ac130002_2> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Restoration"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Thesataḥwas rebuilt with support from the Bhindyaḥlāchi Ṭola Sudhāra Samiti, the Lalitpura Vikāsko Lāgi Samāja, the Indian Embassy, and the Lalitpur Sub-Metropolitan City. The Indian Embassy donated 5,985,000 Nepali Rupees and local donations amounted to about 1,000,000 Nepali Rupees. Thesataḥ wasinaugurated on 2 July 2016 CE by H.E. Shri Ranjit Rae, the Indian ambassador to Nepal."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/673afbfc-e6f2-11e9-8bc4-0242ac130002> ;
    rdfs:comment "Thesataḥwas rebuilt with support from the Bhindyaḥlāchi Ṭola Sudhāra Samiti, the Lalitpura Vikāsko Lāgi Samāja, the Indian Embassy, and the Lalitpur Sub-Metropolitan City. The Indian Embassy donated 5,985,000 Nepali Rupees and local donations amounted to about 1,000,000 Nepali Rupees. Thesataḥ wasinaugurated on 2 July 2016 CE by H.E. Shri Ranjit Rae, the Indian ambassador to Nepal."@en ;
