<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/678a9748-073c-4180-9597-e20ffb50f8a3_1> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Offering of a copper ilāṃ"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Kṛṣṇalāla Śreṣṭha offered the copper canopy (ilāṃ) to theśivaliṅgarevered as Candrabhāneśvara Mahādeva. Kṛṣṇalāla originally hailed from Gāḥ Bāhāḥ, Lalitpur, but moved to Triśūlībajāra later and made the offering together with his wife Kṛṣṇamāyā, and sons Kṛṣṇagovinda, Prāṇagovinda, Lālagovinda, and daughter Kṛṣṇamāyā."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/678a9748-073c-4180-9597-e20ffb50f8a3> ;
    rdfs:comment "Kṛṣṇalāla Śreṣṭha offered the copper canopy (ilāṃ) to theśivaliṅgarevered as Candrabhāneśvara Mahādeva. Kṛṣṇalāla originally hailed from Gāḥ Bāhāḥ, Lalitpur, but moved to Triśūlībajāra later and made the offering together with his wife Kṛṣṇamāyā, and sons Kṛṣṇagovinda, Prāṇagovinda, Lālagovinda, and daughter Kṛṣṇamāyā."@en ;
