<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/6841ec23-0b12-4233-bada-cb6c1aa686e9_1> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:RitualEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Erecting stone pillar (dharmastambha)"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Thedharmastambhawas installed at the southeastern corner of the temple by Kavi Prasāda Gautama as part of his wider campaign of Rāma- and Kṛṣṇa-devotion in the Kathmandu Valley and beyond. The inscription instructs that devotional singing (bhajana-kīrtana) should be performed annually on the eleventh day of the dark fortnight of Śrāvaṇa."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/6841ec23-0b12-4233-bada-cb6c1aa686e9> ;
    rdfs:comment "Thedharmastambhawas installed at the southeastern corner of the temple by Kavi Prasāda Gautama as part of his wider campaign of Rāma- and Kṛṣṇa-devotion in the Kathmandu Valley and beyond. The inscription instructs that devotional singing (bhajana-kīrtana) should be performed annually on the eleventh day of the dark fortnight of Śrāvaṇa."@en ;
