<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/687d2b4c-9a21-42d7-90e4-1bb13e45e132_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:TransferOfCustody ;
    rdfs:label "Initial construction"@en ;
    dcterms:description "According to the inscribed stone slab (śilāpatra), the temple was constructed in 1838 CE (VS 1895) by Balabhañjana Pāṇḍe, who held the rank ofsardārat the time. The inscription records that Balabhañjana not only built this temple but also established asattal(rest house),phalchā(public shelter),hiti(stone water spout), pond, surrounding wall, gateways, and several other shrines in the area. The motivation behind his extensive building activity at this location remains a subject of interest. His father, Bhotu Pāṇḍe, was likewise an active figure in the construction of religious structures and the establishment ofguthis(religious endowments) across the Kathmandu Valley. The inscription also mentions the arrangements made for the temple’s maintenance, including grass-cutting, cleaning, and the payment of land taxes from the revenues of the endowed lands."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/687d2b4c-9a21-42d7-90e4-1bb13e45e132> ;
    rdfs:comment "According to the inscribed stone slab (śilāpatra), the temple was constructed in 1838 CE (VS 1895) by Balabhañjana Pāṇḍe, who held the rank ofsardārat the time. The inscription records that Balabhañjana not only built this temple but also established asattal(rest house),phalchā(public shelter),hiti(stone water spout), pond, surrounding wall, gateways, and several other shrines in the area. The motivation behind his extensive building activity at this location remains a subject of interest. His father, Bhotu Pāṇḍe, was likewise an active figure in the construction of religious structures and the establishment ofguthis(religious endowments) across the Kathmandu Valley. The inscription also mentions the arrangements made for the temple’s maintenance, including grass-cutting, cleaning, and the payment of land taxes from the revenues of the endowed lands."@en ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/agent/antigravity_agent> ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/activity/heritagegraph_kg_construction> ;
    hg:eventIndex 0 ;
    hg:extractionMethod "source_table" ;
    hg:isEventOf <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/687d2b4c-9a21-42d7-90e4-1bb13e45e132> .

<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/687d2b4c-9a21-42d7-90e4-1bb13e45e132_1> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:TransferOfCustody ;
    rdfs:label "Construction of a gate"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Sixty-eight years after the construction of this temple and its associated structures, the Pāṇḍe family added a new doorway to the Gokarṇeśvara temple and stipulated that its future maintenance should be carried out using the endowment of the Vāṇeśvara estate."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/687d2b4c-9a21-42d7-90e4-1bb13e45e132> ;
    rdfs:comment "Sixty-eight years after the construction of this temple and its associated structures, the Pāṇḍe family added a new doorway to the Gokarṇeśvara temple and stipulated that its future maintenance should be carried out using the endowment of the Vāṇeśvara estate."@en ;
