<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/6a263bd4-6022-48bd-ba52-b730dd67710c_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Initial Constrution of the Phalcā"@en ;
    dcterms:description "During the reign of King Yoganarendra Malla, thephalcāwas facilitated by a person called Anantadhara. A statue of Garuḍanārāyaṇa was established by making a podium (shrine) behind thephalcā. Anantadhara enforced the construction to fulfill the wish that the soul of his deceased father, Viṣṇudhara, would ascend to heaven. The inscription also records the donation of a piece of land to finance the annual rituals (varṣavardhanapūjā)."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/6a263bd4-6022-48bd-ba52-b730dd67710c> ;
    rdfs:comment "During the reign of King Yoganarendra Malla, thephalcāwas facilitated by a person called Anantadhara. A statue of Garuḍanārāyaṇa was established by making a podium (shrine) behind thephalcā. Anantadhara enforced the construction to fulfill the wish that the soul of his deceased father, Viṣṇudhara, would ascend to heaven. The inscription also records the donation of a piece of land to finance the annual rituals (varṣavardhanapūjā)."@en ;
