<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/6cb38691-558a-4bdc-89b6-74f2dd0c9420_3> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Land endowment"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Upon the completion of the Temple, Bhājurāma had endowed several plots of land to sponsor many religious activities at the Temple such as for performing the daily rituals, organizing its anniversary celebration, making a fire oblation, lighting amahādīpaon the day ofŚivarātrī, caretaking thecaugharāsataḥand offeringpiṇḍa(cooked rice-ball) to him after his death."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/6cb38691-558a-4bdc-89b6-74f2dd0c9420> ;
