<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/6cdaf736-d3f8-4b5f-9b6d-384f21c8d902_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Initial construction of the Sataḥ"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Dhara Bhāro and his wife Chi Thaṃku, residents of Ikhāchẽ Ṭola, initiated the construction of the Sataḥ in 1836 CE (NS 956). After the construction, the donor couple also established aguṭhīto light butter lamps in the nearby Ālko Gaṇeśa Mandira (LAL0991) on the 13thday of the bright fortnight in Bhādra."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/6cdaf736-d3f8-4b5f-9b6d-384f21c8d902> ;
