    dcterms:description "In 1851 CE (VS 1907), Bamabahādura Kũvara, a brother of Jaṅgabahādura, erected a distinctive temple along the banks of the Bāgamatī, known as Tīnadevala (KAT2670). Atāmrapatra(copper-plate) discovered at the site records the simultaneous establishment of the Jagannātha temple (KAT2690). This inscription, installed after the completion of the temple constructions, mentions the surrounding boundary wall and stipulates its repair and maintenance funded throughguṭhīrevenue, indicating the concurrent construction of this gate."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/6ff6a70a-a862-4371-88b5-a388ee2eaa7f> ;
    rdfs:comment "In 1851 CE (VS 1907), Bamabahādura Kũvara, a brother of Jaṅgabahādura, erected a distinctive temple along the banks of the Bāgamatī, known as Tīnadevala (KAT2670). Atāmrapatra(copper-plate) discovered at the site records the simultaneous establishment of the Jagannātha temple (KAT2690). This inscription, installed after the completion of the temple constructions, mentions the surrounding boundary wall and stipulates its repair and maintenance funded throughguṭhīrevenue, indicating the concurrent construction of this gate."@en ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/agent/antigravity_agent> ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/activity/heritagegraph_kg_construction> ;
    hg:eventIndex 0 ;
    hg:extractionMethod "source_table" ;
    hg:isEventOf <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/6ff6a70a-a862-4371-88b5-a388ee2eaa7f> .

<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/6ff6a70a-a862-4371-88b5-a388ee2eaa7f_1> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Reconstruction"@en ;
    dcterms:description "After the 2015 CE earthquake (VS 2072), which inflicted damage upon Tinadevala and various other monuments, the boundary wall also deteriorated significantly. The restoration initiatives for both the wall and gate were led by the Bāgamatī Civilization Integrated Development Committee, functioning under the Ministry of Urban Development, with assistance from the Asian Development Bank. The renovation project reached its completion on October 23rd, 2022 CE."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/6ff6a70a-a862-4371-88b5-a388ee2eaa7f> ;
    rdfs:comment "After the 2015 CE earthquake (VS 2072), which inflicted damage upon Tinadevala and various other monuments, the boundary wall also deteriorated significantly. The restoration initiatives for both the wall and gate were led by the Bāgamatī Civilization Integrated Development Committee, functioning under the Ministry of Urban Development, with assistance from the Asian Development Bank. The renovation project reached its completion on October 23rd, 2022 CE."@en ;
