<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/71d1fd85-b9ac-4ebf-bc1b-0006d6da7f9e_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:RitualEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Initial construction"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The inventory published in 1982 CE (VS 2039) records that it was built in 1816–17 (VS 1873) by a person named Jayadutha (Inventory VS 2039, p.165). It is unclear what source this information is based on, as no additional details or surname are provided. As such, it is not possible to determine his lineage or community. A family from Sitapāla visits the Śivālaya next to the sataḥ four times a year to perform a special pūjā. It is believed that Jayadutha may be their ancestor."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/71d1fd85-b9ac-4ebf-bc1b-0006d6da7f9e> ;
    rdfs:comment "The inventory published in 1982 CE (VS 2039) records that it was built in 1816–17 (VS 1873) by a person named Jayadutha (Inventory VS 2039, p.165). It is unclear what source this information is based on, as no additional details or surname are provided. As such, it is not possible to determine his lineage or community. A family from Sitapāla visits the Śivālaya next to the sataḥ four times a year to perform a special pūjā. It is believed that Jayadutha may be their ancestor."@en ;
