<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/72fbb5ec-849f-482d-8003-7206e8ede0a6_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:TransferOfCustody ;
    rdfs:label "Initial construction and land endowment"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The inscription provides details related to the erection of thestambha. It states that Pratāpa Malla offered six golden pinnacles and a golden umbrella adorned with amālāto his tutelary deity, Taleju Māju. The inscription also mentions his act of lighting 100,000 butter lamps and the creation of statues in gold, representing himself, his consorts, and his sons, with the wish of a favorable rebirth. Additionally, the inscription documents a land endowment of 4ropanīat Dharmasthalī, accompanied by instructions for the pillar's upkeep, including anointing it with 3pāthīof oil sourced from the income generated by the endowed land."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/72fbb5ec-849f-482d-8003-7206e8ede0a6> ;
    rdfs:comment "The inscription provides details related to the erection of thestambha. It states that Pratāpa Malla offered six golden pinnacles and a golden umbrella adorned with amālāto his tutelary deity, Taleju Māju. The inscription also mentions his act of lighting 100,000 butter lamps and the creation of statues in gold, representing himself, his consorts, and his sons, with the wish of a favorable rebirth. Additionally, the inscription documents a land endowment of 4ropanīat Dharmasthalī, accompanied by instructions for the pillar's upkeep, including anointing it with 3pāthīof oil sourced from the income generated by the endowed land."@en ;
