<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/735f3fdf-a3eb-45e9-ac23-d31342ac14b3_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Demolishing the old small temple and building a new big temple"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Under the rule of King Rājendra Vikrama Śāha, the residents of Navālī ṭola, such as Lachinārā, Āsānārā, and Dhamanārā, replaced the existing smaller Gaṇeśa temple with a larger one. Unfortunately, the inscription does not provide details about the size and structure of the old temple."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/735f3fdf-a3eb-45e9-ac23-d31342ac14b3> ;
