        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Offering a pair of flags"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Saṃyacā Saṃgata, son of Indramāna and Harimāyā Saṃgata, offered a pair of brass flags installed on either side of the main deity. He also offered a metaltoraṇaon top of the Gaṇeśa statue and established a pair of lions flanking the statue. Likewise, he offered a metal statue to be placed as a cover for the stone statue."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/735f3fdf-a3eb-45e9-ac23-d31342ac14b3> ;
    rdfs:comment "Saṃyacā Saṃgata, son of Indramāna and Harimāyā Saṃgata, offered a pair of brass flags installed on either side of the main deity. He also offered a metaltoraṇaon top of the Gaṇeśa statue and established a pair of lions flanking the statue. Likewise, he offered a metal statue to be placed as a cover for the stone statue."@en ;
