<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/74763c55-e9d7-447b-9520-14b2adf86c2b_1> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Temple Reconstruction"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Following its collapse in the destructive earthquake of 1934 CE, the temple underwent a reconstruction process that resulted in a two-tiered structure. A photograph of the temple in its two-storied form was published by Pruscha (1975, p. 54)."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/74763c55-e9d7-447b-9520-14b2adf86c2b> ;
    rdfs:comment "Following its collapse in the destructive earthquake of 1934 CE, the temple underwent a reconstruction process that resulted in a two-tiered structure. A photograph of the temple in its two-storied form was published by Pruscha (1975, p. 54)."@en ;
