<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/74931699-c87c-4f08-8469-9f274e617c0a_2> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Lãpu Chāygu (refurbishment of the main statue)"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Every twelve years, the clay statue of Dīpaṅkara, who is the main deity of the Bāhāḥ, is refurbished. The family performing daily rituals here used to sponsor the refurbishment locally known as lãpu chāygu . In 2011 CE, a grand ceremony was held to raise funds for the statue's refurbishment."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/74931699-c87c-4f08-8469-9f274e617c0a> ;
