<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/75171568-d049-4c63-9fce-ddf40dc4e157_3> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Initial construction"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The only inscription related to this temple is on the bell's surface which is hung in the bell stand at the lower plinth. It mentions the offering of an initial bell by King Bhūpatindra Malla on the second day of the bright half of Manśira, 1699 CE.[1]He had performedkotyāhutioblation on this occasion.  Generally, kotyahuti oblation is performed in front of the temple after completion of the construction.Exactly on the same day (second day of the bright half of the Manśira), the annual ritual of this temple is observed in the present as well, which is considered as the anniversary of the monument. Thus, it can be assumed that the initial construction of this temple was finished on this date. TheNepālikabhūpavaṃśāvalīalso mentions this date as the finishing date of the temple's construction.Footnotes^MistakenlyGutschow(2014, 33) has converted the date NS 820 Mārgaśira to January 1700."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/75171568-d049-4c63-9fce-ddf40dc4e157> ;
    rdfs:comment "The only inscription related to this temple is on the bell's surface which is hung in the bell stand at the lower plinth. It mentions the offering of an initial bell by King Bhūpatindra Malla on the second day of the bright half of Manśira, 1699 CE.[1]He had performedkotyāhutioblation on this occasion.  Generally, kotyahuti oblation is performed in front of the temple after completion of the construction.Exactly on the same day (second day of the bright half of the Manśira), the annual ritual of this temple is observed in the present as well, which is considered as the anniversary of the monument. Thus, it can be assumed that the initial construction of this temple was finished on this date. TheNepālikabhūpavaṃśāvalīalso mentions this date as the finishing date of the temple's construction.Footnotes^MistakenlyGutschow(2014, 33) has converted the date NS 820 Mārgaśira to January 1700."@en ;
