<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/762a6cae-da62-4065-96f1-b9e1e6aee8ae_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Initial construction"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The Phalcā was initially commissioned and built under a person named Dhanathaku from Cakna Kebā ṭola, and in the name of three of his family members: the parents and the younger brother. The donor also made an arrangement to dedicate a regular income (from land) for the conduct of annual rituals. The four family members mentioned in the inscription are said to be respinsible for the ritual conduct. Other details recorded are the position of the planets and a list of objects that must be used in the annual rituals."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/762a6cae-da62-4065-96f1-b9e1e6aee8ae> ;
    rdfs:comment "The Phalcā was initially commissioned and built under a person named Dhanathaku from Cakna Kebā ṭola, and in the name of three of his family members: the parents and the younger brother. The donor also made an arrangement to dedicate a regular income (from land) for the conduct of annual rituals. The four family members mentioned in the inscription are said to be respinsible for the ritual conduct. Other details recorded are the position of the planets and a list of objects that must be used in the annual rituals."@en ;
