<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/77324817-37bf-452e-a41b-d1dc705432b3_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:TransferOfCustody ;
    rdfs:label "Installation of a Vāmana Statue"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The Inscription installed in 538 CE (ŚS 460) during the reign of King Vāmanadeva is the earliest dated inscription of Sankhu. The inscription on the pedestal of the statue records King Vāmanadeva installing a statue of the Vāmana incarnation of Lord Viṣṇu and endowed plots of land to establish aguthi. However, the Vāmana Statue is already lost and is replaced by another statue on the Pedestal."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/77324817-37bf-452e-a41b-d1dc705432b3> ;
    rdfs:comment "The Inscription installed in 538 CE (ŚS 460) during the reign of King Vāmanadeva is the earliest dated inscription of Sankhu. The inscription on the pedestal of the statue records King Vāmanadeva installing a statue of the Vāmana incarnation of Lord Viṣṇu and endowed plots of land to establish aguthi. However, the Vāmana Statue is already lost and is replaced by another statue on the Pedestal."@en ;
