<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/776a4b78-3709-406d-bdb5-7f65590d125d_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Initial construction of the pillar (?)"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Two Hanuman statues stand in front of the Bāghabhairava shrine.  An inscription has been inscribed on the pedestal of one of these two. The inscription informs about the establishment of these Hanuman statues by a group of Bhāva from Dathu Tvāra (tole), Kirtipur. This inscription does not inform anything about this Hanuman pillar. However, this pillar is erected exactly parallel to the shrine. Thus, it can be assumed that the pillar was also erected at the same time when other two Hanuman statues were established in front of the shrine."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/776a4b78-3709-406d-bdb5-7f65590d125d> ;
    rdfs:comment "Two Hanuman statues stand in front of the Bāghabhairava shrine.  An inscription has been inscribed on the pedestal of one of these two. The inscription informs about the establishment of these Hanuman statues by a group of Bhāva from Dathu Tvāra (tole), Kirtipur. This inscription does not inform anything about this Hanuman pillar. However, this pillar is erected exactly parallel to the shrine. Thus, it can be assumed that the pillar was also erected at the same time when other two Hanuman statues were established in front of the shrine."@en ;
