<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/788cd320-e6a8-11e9-8bc4-0242ac130002_6> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Consecration ;
    rdfs:label "Offering of three golden kalaśa"@en ;
    dcterms:description "A copperplate inscription details the consecration of the monastic building. The Vihāra was consecrated in the presence of King Jayajyotira Malla. An offering of three golden kalaśa was made and a play namedVīrabāhuand written by Rām Bhāro was performed. The chief of Vajrācārya played Śrī Panḍuju of Bubāhā and Karma Vajrācārya was played by Śrī Lokarāmaju from Taḥbāhā. It is written that Jyantarāma Mulmi worked hard to complete the monastic building. This copper plate inscription was made by Udaya Rāut."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/788cd320-e6a8-11e9-8bc4-0242ac130002> ;
    rdfs:comment "A copperplate inscription details the consecration of the monastic building. The Vihāra was consecrated in the presence of King Jayajyotira Malla. An offering of three golden kalaśa was made and a play namedVīrabāhuand written by Rām Bhāro was performed. The chief of Vajrācārya played Śrī Panḍuju of Bubāhā and Karma Vajrācārya was played by Śrī Lokarāmaju from Taḥbāhā. It is written that Jyantarāma Mulmi worked hard to complete the monastic building. This copper plate inscription was made by Udaya Rāut."@en ;
