<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/7cd87778-19a1-48c8-9cc0-5adf5682cff5_1> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:TransferOfCustody ;
    rdfs:label "Construction of bāhāḥ"@en ;
    dcterms:description "During the reign of King Bhūpatīndra Malla, Bīradeva Vajrācārya, along with his wife Pūrṇa and other family members established the Jīsvāṃ Bāhā. They adorned thebāhāḥwith a goldencaityaand parasol (chatra) as its finial. To ensure the monastery’s sustainability, Bīradeva endowed eightropanīs of land as a religious trust, dedicated to the perpetual worship of Akṣobhya and Dīpaṅkara and the recitation of thePrajñāpāramitā, a revered Buddhist scripture."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/7cd87778-19a1-48c8-9cc0-5adf5682cff5> ;
    rdfs:comment "During the reign of King Bhūpatīndra Malla, Bīradeva Vajrācārya, along with his wife Pūrṇa and other family members established the Jīsvāṃ Bāhā. They adorned thebāhāḥwith a goldencaityaand parasol (chatra) as its finial. To ensure the monastery’s sustainability, Bīradeva endowed eightropanīs of land as a religious trust, dedicated to the perpetual worship of Akṣobhya and Dīpaṅkara and the recitation of thePrajñāpāramitā, a revered Buddhist scripture."@en ;
