        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Reconstruction of the phalcā"@en ;
    dcterms:description "A newphalcāwas built here on a stone plinth that had survived from its previous construction. Commencing in November 2013 and in collaboration with UN-Habitat, CIUD, and local communities, a project named \"Revitalization of Open Spaces in Kirtipur\" oversaw the reconstruction of thisphalcāalong with the restoration of Deypukhū, and the erection of a boundary wall. The reconstruction, which was finalized in March 2014, also included the installation of a statue of Lokeśvara within thephalcā. As even the elderly residents of the area had no recollection of a properphalcāat this location, its former structure is unknown. There is no inscription shedding light on the initial construction of thephalcā."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/7d94b4e0-a6ea-436c-bf82-773714bf03aa> ;
    rdfs:comment "A newphalcāwas built here on a stone plinth that had survived from its previous construction. Commencing in November 2013 and in collaboration with UN-Habitat, CIUD, and local communities, a project named \"Revitalization of Open Spaces in Kirtipur\" oversaw the reconstruction of thisphalcāalong with the restoration of Deypukhū, and the erection of a boundary wall. The reconstruction, which was finalized in March 2014, also included the installation of a statue of Lokeśvara within thephalcā. As even the elderly residents of the area had no recollection of a properphalcāat this location, its former structure is unknown. There is no inscription shedding light on the initial construction of thephalcā."@en ;
