<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/7f65c791-011e-43e9-8249-60d1c8614c2f_9> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Consecration ;
    rdfs:label "Destruction of Dyaḥchẽ by fire"@en ;
    dcterms:description "During the reign of King Tribhuvana and the prime ministership of Candra Śamśera, the Agnimaṭha at the Dyaḥchẽ caused a massive fire that gutted the statues in the building except the head-figure of the Buddha and the Karāhī. All the statues at the Dyaḥchẽ were then shifted to the Caugharā Sataḥ. Candra Śamśera disbursed necessary funds for reinstating the damaged statues and performing consecration rituals."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/7f65c791-011e-43e9-8249-60d1c8614c2f> ;
    rdfs:comment "During the reign of King Tribhuvana and the prime ministership of Candra Śamśera, the Agnimaṭha at the Dyaḥchẽ caused a massive fire that gutted the statues in the building except the head-figure of the Buddha and the Karāhī. All the statues at the Dyaḥchẽ were then shifted to the Caugharā Sataḥ. Candra Śamśera disbursed necessary funds for reinstating the damaged statues and performing consecration rituals."@en ;
