<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/7fd5e55f-876c-48f9-b974-357b58fec2c3_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Construction of the Temple and offering of a golden pinnacle"@en ;
    dcterms:description "An inscription dated NS 785 (1665 CE) records Bhavānīśaṅkara Bābu and Śivaśaṅkara Bābu, the brothers from Lalitpur, constructing the Vaiṣṇavī (Viṣṇudevī) Temple in Satuṅgala and offering a golden finial (D. Vajrācārya VS 2056, p. 138-139). This inscription is no longer available at the Temple premises."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/7fd5e55f-876c-48f9-b974-357b58fec2c3> ;
    rdfs:comment "An inscription dated NS 785 (1665 CE) records Bhavānīśaṅkara Bābu and Śivaśaṅkara Bābu, the brothers from Lalitpur, constructing the Vaiṣṇavī (Viṣṇudevī) Temple in Satuṅgala and offering a golden finial (D. Vajrācārya VS 2056, p. 138-139). This inscription is no longer available at the Temple premises."@en ;
