<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/81b361fb-d1f6-480c-8741-e08d7a1ec834_2> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Renovation of the caitya (KAT0350-007)?"@en ;
    dcterms:description "During the reign of King Surendra Vikrama Śāha, Bha Thakuṃ of the Olāchi Ṭola renovated (?) thecaityatogether with her daughter Bekhālakṣmī.(The inscription does not mention the event. Only few letters survive from another inscription on the plinth of the Caitya, which probably records the constructions of the Caitya. Therefore, this inscription of 1859 CE (NS 979) is possibly the record of the Caitya’s renovation.)"@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/81b361fb-d1f6-480c-8741-e08d7a1ec834> ;
