<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/82516dc9-a9d3-42bf-a614-e6ce59aba15a_5> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Construction of the temple"@en ;
    dcterms:description "A proper temple was built for Nṛsiṃha with funding from the Kathmandu Metropolitan City and local residents. The Nṛsiṃha temple began as a simple roadside shrine. Over time, as the road was repeatedly paved, the level of the Nṛsiṃha shrine gradually sank below the road's surface, leading to water accumulation and an unclean environment. During this construction, the floor level was raised above the road to prevent future water problems. Reflecting its origins as an open-air shrine, the new temple incorporates a small opening in the roof."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/82516dc9-a9d3-42bf-a614-e6ce59aba15a> ;
    rdfs:comment "A proper temple was built for Nṛsiṃha with funding from the Kathmandu Metropolitan City and local residents. The Nṛsiṃha temple began as a simple roadside shrine. Over time, as the road was repeatedly paved, the level of the Nṛsiṃha shrine gradually sank below the road's surface, leading to water accumulation and an unclean environment. During this construction, the floor level was raised above the road to prevent future water problems. Reflecting its origins as an open-air shrine, the new temple incorporates a small opening in the roof."@en ;
