<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/85bd4cee-da51-4014-8b9b-b7d18e47ba23_1> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Consecration ;
    rdfs:label "Establishment of the caitya and procession"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The inscription fixed on the wall of the house east of thecaityarecords that in NS 941 (1821 CE), Jagajyoti Vajrācārya, Lakṣmījyoti Vajrācārya, and other families established thecaityaand installed Mahāmañjuśrī, Gaṇeśa, and Mahākāla on the house wall. The inscription also mentions the construction of the house and courtyard along with the well. After the consecration of thecaitya, the Vajrācārya families and locals jointly performed worship and conducted a city circumambulation (parikramā) in 1822 CE (NS 942)."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/85bd4cee-da51-4014-8b9b-b7d18e47ba23> ;
    rdfs:comment "The inscription fixed on the wall of the house east of thecaityarecords that in NS 941 (1821 CE), Jagajyoti Vajrācārya, Lakṣmījyoti Vajrācārya, and other families established thecaityaand installed Mahāmañjuśrī, Gaṇeśa, and Mahākāla on the house wall. The inscription also mentions the construction of the house and courtyard along with the well. After the consecration of thecaitya, the Vajrācārya families and locals jointly performed worship and conducted a city circumambulation (parikramā) in 1822 CE (NS 942)."@en ;
