    rdfs:label "Erection of two Pillars"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Canakamāna Bandepālī and Mathurādevī erected two pillars in front of the temple with the implements of Viṣṇu on top. One of the pillars contains a mace (gadā) and discus (cakra) on top while the other one is topped with a conch shell (śaṅkha) and lotus (padma)."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/87c885ca-8c0a-4bad-9c69-682de1e22b2e> ;
