    rdfs:label "Renovation of the Dyaḥchẽ"@en ;
    dcterms:description "According to a copperplate inscription on the third floor, the Dyaḥchẽ was built by Subbā Dharma Nārāyaṇa Mānandhara of the Maru Ṭola. As the building was in a poor state, it was renovated with funds from the Kathmandu Metropolis and donations collected from the trust members."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/89c68953-0d12-428c-86ef-5e6ddc36a313> ;
