<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/89c9360f-f709-4ff5-91fc-955e3263562a_4> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:TransferOfCustody ;
    rdfs:label "Endowment of lands"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Mahanta Hirālāla Bhārati endowed lands for daily rituals and worships at the Maṭha. The inscription also mentions about the territory of the Maṭha, names of annual festivities which were observed in honour of the deity and procedure for daily worships. The inscription states that themahantas who abide by the rules of the arrangements shall attain the virtues that will never be lost and warns those who discontinue the tradition that doing so will equal committing the five great sins (pañcamahāpāpa)."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/89c9360f-f709-4ff5-91fc-955e3263562a> ;
    rdfs:comment "Mahanta Hirālāla Bhārati endowed lands for daily rituals and worships at the Maṭha. The inscription also mentions about the territory of the Maṭha, names of annual festivities which were observed in honour of the deity and procedure for daily worships. The inscription states that themahantas who abide by the rules of the arrangements shall attain the virtues that will never be lost and warns those who discontinue the tradition that doing so will equal committing the five great sins (pañcamahāpāpa)."@en ;
