<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/8d927bbc-dbda-4ce1-b186-23a58e990fb6_2> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Offering of unknown objects"@en ;
    dcterms:description "An unidentified donor from Macchegāuṅ performed some act of dedication in the name of Viṣṇudevī. Since the lower portion of the inscription is worn away, the precise nature of this act is unclear. Dhanavajra (VS 2056, p. 425) records the full text, although with numerous inaccuracies. Judging from that corrupted reading, it seems that amukha(possibly an icon or mask) of Viṣṇudevī was established and certain ritual elements (pusidhāma,gatutadhika?) were affixed. The act was carried out by theGopālī(also calledGopārikaorGwālā) group, including Dhanarāma Gopārika of Macchegāuṅ. Although theGopālīcommunity has long inhabited areas such as Kīrtipura, Macchegāũ, Cobhāra, and Thānakoṭa, there are very few inscriptions attesting to their historical presence; therefore, this record is of particular importance."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/8d927bbc-dbda-4ce1-b186-23a58e990fb6> ;
    rdfs:comment "An unidentified donor from Macchegāuṅ performed some act of dedication in the name of Viṣṇudevī. Since the lower portion of the inscription is worn away, the precise nature of this act is unclear. Dhanavajra (VS 2056, p. 425) records the full text, although with numerous inaccuracies. Judging from that corrupted reading, it seems that amukha(possibly an icon or mask) of Viṣṇudevī was established and certain ritual elements (pusidhāma,gatutadhika?) were affixed. The act was carried out by theGopālī(also calledGopārikaorGwālā) group, including Dhanarāma Gopārika of Macchegāuṅ. Although theGopālīcommunity has long inhabited areas such as Kīrtipura, Macchegāũ, Cobhāra, and Thānakoṭa, there are very few inscriptions attesting to their historical presence; therefore, this record is of particular importance."@en ;
