<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/8dcbb3fa-adcb-44ba-a375-698e466bb94d_1> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Repair of the main deity (kvāḥpāḥdyaḥ) and offering of ritual objects"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Binayaśvarī Tulādhara (text: Tulādhari Vinyaśvarī) and her sons Chatrasiṃha Tulādhara (text: Turādhra Chatrasiṃ), Jayalundrasiṃ, Bālagovindasiṃha (text: Bālagvaviṃdrasiṃ), and other family members refurbished and painted the Bāhāḥ’s main deity (kvāḥpāḥdyaḥ). On the occasion, they also presented two bells, a flywhisk (cāmara), a plate, a ceremonial mirror (jvalānhāykaṃ), and a pair of copper-made ritual slippers (pādukā) to the Bāhāḥ."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/8dcbb3fa-adcb-44ba-a375-698e466bb94d> ;
    rdfs:comment "Binayaśvarī Tulādhara (text: Tulādhari Vinyaśvarī) and her sons Chatrasiṃha Tulādhara (text: Turādhra Chatrasiṃ), Jayalundrasiṃ, Bālagovindasiṃha (text: Bālagvaviṃdrasiṃ), and other family members refurbished and painted the Bāhāḥ’s main deity (kvāḥpāḥdyaḥ). On the occasion, they also presented two bells, a flywhisk (cāmara), a plate, a ceremonial mirror (jvalānhāykaṃ), and a pair of copper-made ritual slippers (pādukā) to the Bāhāḥ."@en ;
