        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Construction of a caitya and installation of some deities"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Cikāji Tulādhara (text: Torādhra Cikāji) Dānavirasiṃ, Sameratna, and his other family members built a caitya in front of the Bāhāḥ and laid floor tiles (cikaṃaḥpā) in the courtyard. On the same occasion, they also installed statues of two of the Buddha’s closest disciples Sāriputra and Maudgalyāyana, Sarasvatī, and Gaṇeśa, and covered the sanctum door with brass sheets."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/8ec14107-7e3a-4657-aa0e-b2a9d8a643d9> ;
