<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/8f5e6a23-ea42-4a90-b496-cca35276d255_1> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Erection of a stone pillar"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The inscription on the pillar is partially eroded, making it unclear for what specific purpose it was originally installed. However, it can be inferred that the pillar was erected to mark a boundary. A warning is inscribed stating that if anyone damages the pillar, they will incur the sin of the five great offenses (pañcamahāpāpa), equivalent to the sin of defiling the sacred Cā̃gunārāyaṇa. According to locals, this pillar does not originally belong to the Bhavānīśaṅkara temple but was brought from somewhere else and placed in the temple's southwest corner."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/8f5e6a23-ea42-4a90-b496-cca35276d255> ;
    rdfs:comment "The inscription on the pillar is partially eroded, making it unclear for what specific purpose it was originally installed. However, it can be inferred that the pillar was erected to mark a boundary. A warning is inscribed stating that if anyone damages the pillar, they will incur the sin of the five great offenses (pañcamahāpāpa), equivalent to the sin of defiling the sacred Cā̃gunārāyaṇa. According to locals, this pillar does not originally belong to the Bhavānīśaṅkara temple but was brought from somewhere else and placed in the temple's southwest corner."@en ;
