<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/8f92f98f-8441-4f10-955e-4f03b4e29849_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Offering of golden ornaments and crowning jewel"@en ;
    dcterms:description "King Bhūpālendra Malla's reign, gold ornaments and a crowning jewel (cūḍāmaṇi) were offered to \"Khatadeva,\" likely referring to Kumāra, as he is worshipped on the 6th lunar day, with \"ṣa\" often pronounced as \"kha.\" These offerings were probably for the Kumāra temple, whose finial still bears similar ornaments. A finial was also offered to the thrice-venerated Parameśvarī, though the goddess receiving this offering remains unclear, possibly indicating a previous statue in the temple."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/8f92f98f-8441-4f10-955e-4f03b4e29849> ;
    rdfs:comment "King Bhūpālendra Malla's reign, gold ornaments and a crowning jewel (cūḍāmaṇi) were offered to \"Khatadeva,\" likely referring to Kumāra, as he is worshipped on the 6th lunar day, with \"ṣa\" often pronounced as \"kha.\" These offerings were probably for the Kumāra temple, whose finial still bears similar ornaments. A finial was also offered to the thrice-venerated Parameśvarī, though the goddess receiving this offering remains unclear, possibly indicating a previous statue in the temple."@en ;
