<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/8fa97d24-02ff-11ea-a389-0242ac130002_2> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Initial construction"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Jagamaru Pukhū Phalcā is said to have been built by Lākhes from Pimbahal, though the concrete date is unknown. According toU. Śreṣṭha(2012), thebhajana phalcāand the small Kṛṣṇa temple were destroyed during the earthquake of 1934and later rebuilt by Subbā (government officer) Motilal Shrestha (Lākhe). It is said that Subbā brought a tree over the river Bagmati to Pimbahal with the permission of the then Rana Prime minister Juddha Shamsher and consequently rebuilt the temple andphalcāin 1940 CE."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/8fa97d24-02ff-11ea-a389-0242ac130002> ;
    rdfs:comment "Jagamaru Pukhū Phalcā is said to have been built by Lākhes from Pimbahal, though the concrete date is unknown. According toU. Śreṣṭha(2012), thebhajana phalcāand the small Kṛṣṇa temple were destroyed during the earthquake of 1934and later rebuilt by Subbā (government officer) Motilal Shrestha (Lākhe). It is said that Subbā brought a tree over the river Bagmati to Pimbahal with the permission of the then Rana Prime minister Juddha Shamsher and consequently rebuilt the temple andphalcāin 1940 CE."@en ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/agent/antigravity_agent> ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/activity/heritagegraph_kg_construction> ;
    hg:eventIndex 2 ;
