<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/8fa97d24-02ff-11ea-a389-0242ac130002_3> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Reconstruction"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Subbā Motilāla Śreṣṭha (from the Lākhe clan) of Pimbahal reconstructed Jagamaru Pukhū Phalcā and the small Krishna temple in the 1940s.According to Ratneswor Lal Shrestha, 76, his grandfather Motilal Shrestha rebuilt thephalcāin the 1940s CE. The donors of thephalcāare unknown. Jagamaru Pukhū Phalcā's was converted into a one-story building with door and windows and covered with a tin roof. A library was run inside."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/8fa97d24-02ff-11ea-a389-0242ac130002> ;
    rdfs:comment "Subbā Motilāla Śreṣṭha (from the Lākhe clan) of Pimbahal reconstructed Jagamaru Pukhū Phalcā and the small Krishna temple in the 1940s.According to Ratneswor Lal Shrestha, 76, his grandfather Motilal Shrestha rebuilt thephalcāin the 1940s CE. The donors of thephalcāare unknown. Jagamaru Pukhū Phalcā's was converted into a one-story building with door and windows and covered with a tin roof. A library was run inside."@en ;
