<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/8fa97d24-02ff-11ea-a389-0242ac130002_4> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Restoration"@en ;
    dcterms:description "In circa 1998, GTZ/udle supported thephalcā's reconstruction to its original configuration: supported by 12 newly carved pillars, open to all sides and covered with a traditonal tile (jhĩgaṭī) roof. The pillars were carved in a hybrid design with modern carvings on the shafts and traditional motifs on the upper registers."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/8fa97d24-02ff-11ea-a389-0242ac130002> ;
    rdfs:comment "In circa 1998, GTZ/udle supported thephalcā's reconstruction to its original configuration: supported by 12 newly carved pillars, open to all sides and covered with a traditonal tile (jhĩgaṭī) roof. The pillars were carved in a hybrid design with modern carvings on the shafts and traditional motifs on the upper registers."@en ;
