<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/90ae9fac-535a-4b18-9034-d97dda03d621_4> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Replacement of the old bell with new one"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Candra Śamśera, one of the sons of Dhīra Śamśera, installed a new bell at the temple after the original bell that his father had installed was broken. The inscription on the new bell only mentions “Śrī 3 Mahārāja” as the donor without specifying the name. Given that Candra Śamśera was the prime minister at that time, it appears he donated the new bell to the temple his father had built."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/90ae9fac-535a-4b18-9034-d97dda03d621> ;
    rdfs:comment "Candra Śamśera, one of the sons of Dhīra Śamśera, installed a new bell at the temple after the original bell that his father had installed was broken. The inscription on the new bell only mentions “Śrī 3 Mahārāja” as the donor without specifying the name. Given that Candra Śamśera was the prime minister at that time, it appears he donated the new bell to the temple his father had built."@en ;
