        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Offering of a strut?"@en ;
    dcterms:description "A copper-plate inscription is nailed against the bottom of one of the struts of the southern façade of the Temple. Since it records only names of two persons: Śāntimāyā Mānandhar from the Thãhiti Ṭola and … Khaḍkā (this name is covered due to the bulb fixed just below the inscription), it remains obscure whether these persons sponsored the strut or did something else."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/92728a2b-bed1-4630-bd28-b92b1a822459> ;
    rdfs:comment "A copper-plate inscription is nailed against the bottom of one of the struts of the southern façade of the Temple. Since it records only names of two persons: Śāntimāyā Mānandhar from the Thãhiti Ṭola and … Khaḍkā (this name is covered due to the bulb fixed just below the inscription), it remains obscure whether these persons sponsored the strut or did something else."@en ;
