        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Restoration"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The land of Luchẽnani (to the eastern side of the Bahī) belonged to that monastic building. It contained some houses with roofs made of straw. The roof of theākhāchẽ(a cultural house where musical instruments, masks and dresses are stored) was tiled by a group of volunteers led by Narami Bhāvo."@en ;
