        hg:Enshrinement ;
    rdfs:label "Offering of two Nandī statues"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Two statues of Nandī (one made of brass and the other one made of stone) were installed inside the sanctum on the same day. The brass statue was offered by Rāju Rājopādhyāya, the priest of the Temple, and the stone one was offered by a police officer."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/937f42c4-d4a7-41c8-b259-3272b9a37638> ;
