<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/94b79277-7564-4a74-9880-e2c877569fa6_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Renovation of phalcā"@en ;
    dcterms:description "During King Pratāpa Malla's reign, Suṣurī Bhāro, an assistant (bhaṇḍārī) at the Paśupatinātha Mandira, renovated thephalcācontaining the Matsyendragaṇeśa statue, dedicating it to his deceased son. After the renovation, he reestablished the statue in thephalcāthrough a fire oblation. This inscription reveals that Matsyendragaṇeśa was initially established in aphalcāand a temple was built for him only later."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/94b79277-7564-4a74-9880-e2c877569fa6> ;
    rdfs:comment "During King Pratāpa Malla's reign, Suṣurī Bhāro, an assistant (bhaṇḍārī) at the Paśupatinātha Mandira, renovated thephalcācontaining the Matsyendragaṇeśa statue, dedicating it to his deceased son. After the renovation, he reestablished the statue in thephalcāthrough a fire oblation. This inscription reveals that Matsyendragaṇeśa was initially established in aphalcāand a temple was built for him only later."@en ;
