<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/95846732-e5e4-11e9-b125-0242ac130002_5> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Installation of a stone toraṇa and formation of a group of devotees"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Vijarāja Vajrācārya (of Guru Bāhāla) formed theGaṇeśaSevā(probablyKhalaḥ, which means a group of devotees). Gvamirāja was thethakāli,and the other group members were: Vijasiña, Jagarāma, Yandrarā, Gumisiña, Asiña, Jñokita, Tethā, Manisiña, Gumirāma, Hākusiña, Suṣudeva,  Suṣucā,  Silāma, Mālasiña, Madhasiña Kihima(Kimhi)siña and Amirāja, among others. The inscription also records that a group was formed to acceptYināya Mataor the Gaṇeśa flame (probably butter lamps), with the people named in the inscription as its members. The team installed a stonetoraṇaover the entrance of the Gaṇeśa shrine in the temple. A special worship calleddahrūwas performed on the same day one year later."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/95846732-e5e4-11e9-b125-0242ac130002> ;
    rdfs:comment "Vijarāja Vajrācārya (of Guru Bāhāla) formed theGaṇeśaSevā(probablyKhalaḥ, which means a group of devotees). Gvamirāja was thethakāli,and the other group members were: Vijasiña, Jagarāma, Yandrarā, Gumisiña, Asiña, Jñokita, Tethā, Manisiña, Gumirāma, Hākusiña, Suṣudeva,  Suṣucā,  Silāma, Mālasiña, Madhasiña Kihima(Kimhi)siña and Amirāja, among others. The inscription also records that a group was formed to acceptYināya Mataor the Gaṇeśa flame (probably butter lamps), with the people named in the inscription as its members. The team installed a stonetoraṇaover the entrance of the Gaṇeśa shrine in the temple. A special worship calleddahrūwas performed on the same day one year later."@en ;
