<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/95846732-e5e4-11e9-b125-0242ac130002_9> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Enshrinement ;
    rdfs:label "An institution of devotees (Sakebāra Sevā) was formed and two images of lions were installed"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The inscription records two events: one is the formation of thesakebāra sevā,a group performing certain activities in honor of Gaṇeśa, and the other is the installation of two images of lions in the Bāhāḥ or Dupātṭola. Fortunately, the date is very clear.Thesakebāra sevāconsisted of ten people; this was agroup of devotees that performed certain activities on Tuesdays in honor of the localGaṇeśaand installed two images ofsiṃbāhāna(likely two lion statues). Some of the names mentioned are Mādhava Siṃha Bhāvo, Māla Siṃha Bhāvo, Hari (Siṃha??) Bhāvo and Bābu Deva Bhāvo. The leader of these ten men appears to be Biṣṇu Siṃha Bhāvo. It is clear that ten people of the Bhāvo (Jyāpu) community were involved in the event."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/95846732-e5e4-11e9-b125-0242ac130002> ;
    rdfs:comment "The inscription records two events: one is the formation of thesakebāra sevā,a group performing certain activities in honor of Gaṇeśa, and the other is the installation of two images of lions in the Bāhāḥ or Dupātṭola. Fortunately, the date is very clear.Thesakebāra sevāconsisted of ten people; this was agroup of devotees that performed certain activities on Tuesdays in honor of the localGaṇeśaand installed two images ofsiṃbāhāna(likely two lion statues). Some of the names mentioned are Mādhava Siṃha Bhāvo, Māla Siṃha Bhāvo, Hari (Siṃha??) Bhāvo and Bābu Deva Bhāvo. The leader of these ten men appears to be Biṣṇu Siṃha Bhāvo. It is clear that ten people of the Bhāvo (Jyāpu) community were involved in the event."@en ;
