<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/959482f1-8473-456a-ba8a-37ee44b9ba7f_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:TransferOfCustody ;
    rdfs:label "Offering a pair of lions"@en ;
    dcterms:description "A pair of stone lions were offered to Mahākāla in 1663 CE (NS 783). Members of the Caturdaśī Sevā Guthi, a religious service performed on the 14thof the dark fortnight of every lunar month, including Śiva, Candrasiṃ, Rāmadeva had made the offering (D. Sharma and T. Shrestha2016, p. 413)."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/959482f1-8473-456a-ba8a-37ee44b9ba7f> ;
