<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/959482f1-8473-456a-ba8a-37ee44b9ba7f_2> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Performance of rituals for auspiciousness after a sharp discuss (cakra) installed at the Vajrayoginī temple premises fell off"@en ;
    dcterms:description "There are records of Mahākāla receiving animal sacrifices at times of any impediment at and around the Vajrayoginī temple. A sharp discuss (cakra) installed at the Vajrayoginī temple premises fell off in 1683 CE (NS 803). Special rituals for auspiciousness were performed along with a sacrifice of a buffalo to Mahākāla following the incident (T. Siṃha1136, p. 12, folio 17B-18A)."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/959482f1-8473-456a-ba8a-37ee44b9ba7f> ;
    rdfs:comment "There are records of Mahākāla receiving animal sacrifices at times of any impediment at and around the Vajrayoginī temple. A sharp discuss (cakra) installed at the Vajrayoginī temple premises fell off in 1683 CE (NS 803). Special rituals for auspiciousness were performed along with a sacrifice of a buffalo to Mahākāla following the incident (T. Siṃha1136, p. 12, folio 17B-18A)."@en ;
