<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/959482f1-8473-456a-ba8a-37ee44b9ba7f_3> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Performance of rituals for auspiciousness after Caughrā Sataḥ caught fire"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Caugharā Sataḥ (SKH0560) caught fire in 1795 CE (NS 915). Following the incident, King Raṇa Bahādura Śāha performed special rituals for auspiciousness by sacrificing a buffalo, two goats, and five ducks to Mahākāla."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/959482f1-8473-456a-ba8a-37ee44b9ba7f> ;
