<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/95b952e2-e8c5-11e9-8bc4-0242ac130002_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Restoration"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The entire Capāḥ was dismantled and rebuilt in 1995 with the support of the German Technical Cooperation (GTZ-udle).According to locals from the neighbourhood, the wood that was used for restoration came from a large tree that stood in front of Thalbuṃ Phalcā (LAL4150). Vegetable vendors used to sit underneath the tree: there is a myth is that everyone who touched the tree with a vegetable would then be able to sell it immediately."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/95b952e2-e8c5-11e9-8bc4-0242ac130002> ;
    rdfs:comment "The entire Capāḥ was dismantled and rebuilt in 1995 with the support of the German Technical Cooperation (GTZ-udle).According to locals from the neighbourhood, the wood that was used for restoration came from a large tree that stood in front of Thalbuṃ Phalcā (LAL4150). Vegetable vendors used to sit underneath the tree: there is a myth is that everyone who touched the tree with a vegetable would then be able to sell it immediately."@en ;
