<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/96d763ae-020a-11ea-a389-0242ac130002_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:TransferOfCustody ;
    rdfs:label "Initial construction of the Phalcā"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Queen Siddhimaṅgalādevī Thakunī (wife of King Śrīnivāsa Malla) initiated the construction of this Phalcā in 1686 CE. She endowed the site with four different areas of land so that aguṭhīmight be organised to look after the construction and take care of the monument. The inscription placed in the Phalcā mentions that the Queen commissioned the monument in memory of the King, and an image of Umāmaheśvara was installed in the Phalcā in his name."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/96d763ae-020a-11ea-a389-0242ac130002> ;
    rdfs:comment "Queen Siddhimaṅgalādevī Thakunī (wife of King Śrīnivāsa Malla) initiated the construction of this Phalcā in 1686 CE. She endowed the site with four different areas of land so that aguṭhīmight be organised to look after the construction and take care of the monument. The inscription placed in the Phalcā mentions that the Queen commissioned the monument in memory of the King, and an image of Umāmaheśvara was installed in the Phalcā in his name."@en ;
