<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/97276b3d-0f4d-4844-8d79-08aa48295358_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Paving the courtyard"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The Dathu Nani courtyard was laid with bricks with the joint efforts from Cāka Bāhāra’s Devamuni Bhāro, who was the local administrative officer (pramāna), along with Punarāma, Bāsurāma, Sivaharī, Madhurāma, Harigovinda, and Manhahosiṃ. The inscription also enforced rules that prohibited bringing cows and bulls in the courtyard, along with other acts like urination and defecation, grinding of wheat, and driving nails on to the ground."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/97276b3d-0f4d-4844-8d79-08aa48295358> ;
    rdfs:comment "The Dathu Nani courtyard was laid with bricks with the joint efforts from Cāka Bāhāra’s Devamuni Bhāro, who was the local administrative officer (pramāna), along with Punarāma, Bāsurāma, Sivaharī, Madhurāma, Harigovinda, and Manhahosiṃ. The inscription also enforced rules that prohibited bringing cows and bulls in the courtyard, along with other acts like urination and defecation, grinding of wheat, and driving nails on to the ground."@en ;
