<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/972f5123-13f3-4fc6-b812-3592870cd4cf_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Initial construction"@en ;
    dcterms:description "An inventory published in 1982 CE (VS 2039) refers to an inscription stating that akājīfrom Chāgaḍola, Kathmandu, built thesataḥaround 1915–16 CE (VS 1972), although the individual's name is not recorded. The current residents are unaware of the existence or content of this inscription. In the vicinity, Dirghalakṣmī—wife of Vīrabhadra Kũvara and sister-in-law of Balabhadra—constructed anothersataḥalong with a Śivālaya, suggesting that the Teku Sataḥ may also have been built by akājīfrom the same Kũvara lineage. However, due to the loss of the inscription, further details remain unavailable."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/972f5123-13f3-4fc6-b812-3592870cd4cf> ;
    rdfs:comment "An inventory published in 1982 CE (VS 2039) refers to an inscription stating that akājīfrom Chāgaḍola, Kathmandu, built thesataḥaround 1915–16 CE (VS 1972), although the individual's name is not recorded. The current residents are unaware of the existence or content of this inscription. In the vicinity, Dirghalakṣmī—wife of Vīrabhadra Kũvara and sister-in-law of Balabhadra—constructed anothersataḥalong with a Śivālaya, suggesting that the Teku Sataḥ may also have been built by akājīfrom the same Kũvara lineage. However, due to the loss of the inscription, further details remain unavailable."@en ;
