<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/97bdacd9-8de4-4c7d-bbc0-ca2259cc2a1d_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:TransferOfCustody ;
    rdfs:label "Land grant"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The earliest historical record of Kirāteśvara dates back to 1728 CE (NS 848), when King Jagajjaya Malla (r. 1722-1734 CE) of Kathmandu granted land for the establishment of a trust responsible for conducting daily and periodic rituals at various deities in the Paśupati area, including Kirāteśvara Mahādeva."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/97bdacd9-8de4-4c7d-bbc0-ca2259cc2a1d> ;
    rdfs:comment "The earliest historical record of Kirāteśvara dates back to 1728 CE (NS 848), when King Jagajjaya Malla (r. 1722-1734 CE) of Kathmandu granted land for the establishment of a trust responsible for conducting daily and periodic rituals at various deities in the Paśupati area, including Kirāteśvara Mahādeva."@en ;
