    rdfs:label "Unknown (recorded in the Licchavi inscriptions)"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The Licchavi inscription kept at the northeast corner of the temple does not belong to the temple itself. According toVajrācārya(VS 2030, 391), it seem to be issued during the reign of Aṃśuvarman (VajrācāryaVS 2030, 391). TheJaḥdhuṃhiti(see the object number LAL2120-006 above), too, bears a Licchavi inscription."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/97f7c7ff-da96-44f3-9841-9e708675d5b4> ;
