        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Construction of a shrine of a family deity"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Jagata Siñ Bhāvo, Jugi Rāma Bhāvo and other Bhāvos constructed a shrine. Relying upon the inscription (LAL1490_I_20181203_06.JPG),Pruscha(1975,170) assumes that the Gaṇeśa temple was constructed in 1681. However, the inscription suggests that some other shrine was constructed at the date. Regarding the object, only the last letter of the word ( ‘ri’ ) is retained in the inscription; the first two letters of the word are effaced. With this in mind,Siṃha(2018, XX) postulates that the rubbed word is‘gajuri’(i.e. pinnacle), but that it could also be read as‘deguri’(a temple of family deity) because there are several such shrines in this temple area."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/9884d7b8-e92d-11e9-8bc4-0242ac130002> ;
    rdfs:comment "Jagata Siñ Bhāvo, Jugi Rāma Bhāvo and other Bhāvos constructed a shrine. Relying upon the inscription (LAL1490_I_20181203_06.JPG),Pruscha(1975,170) assumes that the Gaṇeśa temple was constructed in 1681. However, the inscription suggests that some other shrine was constructed at the date. Regarding the object, only the last letter of the word ( ‘ri’ ) is retained in the inscription; the first two letters of the word are effaced. With this in mind,Siṃha(2018, XX) postulates that the rubbed word is‘gajuri’(i.e. pinnacle), but that it could also be read as‘deguri’(a temple of family deity) because there are several such shrines in this temple area."@en ;
