<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/989f4dde-8eee-11ea-8e56-0242ac130005_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Reconstruction of the temple"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The inscription of NS 977 mentions that there was no temple for the deity at that time. The statue of Gaṇeśa was simply covered with a small roof. In NS 977, Raghuvaṃśa Rāotta (Rāvuta) and Bhavā[nīrā]ma Babu from Ikhāchẽ Dvaka dismantled the old, dilapidated roof and built a new temple in its place."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/989f4dde-8eee-11ea-8e56-0242ac130005> ;
    rdfs:comment "The inscription of NS 977 mentions that there was no temple for the deity at that time. The statue of Gaṇeśa was simply covered with a small roof. In NS 977, Raghuvaṃśa Rāotta (Rāvuta) and Bhavā[nīrā]ma Babu from Ikhāchẽ Dvaka dismantled the old, dilapidated roof and built a new temple in its place."@en ;
