<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/98b92c2f-f4d6-439b-8f42-b34bab291ad4_1> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Addition of lion statues"@en ;
    dcterms:description "A pair of lion statues were installed in the temple. The inscription is covered with ghee and oil and parts of it are diificult to decipher. The text at the bottom refers to political events between the kingdoms of Kantipur, Lalitpur and Bhaktapur. The names of King Śrīnivāsa Malla and Pratāpa Malla are mentioned."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/98b92c2f-f4d6-439b-8f42-b34bab291ad4> ;
