<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/98dd8989-b385-4834-b405-b04eaf60fe49_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Initial construction"@en ;
    dcterms:description "King Rājendra issued alālamohara(K_0008_0040B) approving land parcels donated in the name of Mālikeśvara and Kapileśvara Mandira for performing daily and other rituals of the deities using the rent from the land. Given that thelālamoharaaddressed to Dalakeśara Pā̃ḍe is related to the temple built by his wife, it is evident that the temple already existed in 1846 CE."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/98dd8989-b385-4834-b405-b04eaf60fe49> ;
    rdfs:comment "King Rājendra issued alālamohara(K_0008_0040B) approving land parcels donated in the name of Mālikeśvara and Kapileśvara Mandira for performing daily and other rituals of the deities using the rent from the land. Given that thelālamoharaaddressed to Dalakeśara Pā̃ḍe is related to the temple built by his wife, it is evident that the temple already existed in 1846 CE."@en ;
