<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/98e982ee-dae3-41ad-988c-dfcd2c339e30_10> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Reconstruction of the āgaṃchẽ west"@en ;
    dcterms:description "In 2023, theāgaṃchẽwest was reconstructed from ground-up. None of the original doors, windows and carved pillars were reused and their whereabouts are not know. A photograph by John Huntington from 1970 shows threetoraṇaabove the first floor windows. In Hugh Down's photo from 1980 thetoraṇaabove the windows on the left and right are missing.All threetoraṇawere likely lost or stolen over time."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/98e982ee-dae3-41ad-988c-dfcd2c339e30> ;
    rdfs:comment "In 2023, theāgaṃchẽwest was reconstructed from ground-up. None of the original doors, windows and carved pillars were reused and their whereabouts are not know. A photograph by John Huntington from 1970 shows threetoraṇaabove the first floor windows. In Hugh Down's photo from 1980 thetoraṇaabove the windows on the left and right are missing.All threetoraṇawere likely lost or stolen over time."@en ;
