<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/995c1376-9e84-42a2-8f05-38b8d8a32a23_7> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Installation of copperplate inscription recording ancestors' contributions"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The members of Nī Bāhāḥ installed a copper plaque to honor their ancestors' contributions to art. The inscription mentions Guṇasiṃhadeva’s death in 1646 CE (NS 766) and records that his grandsons—Sabhākara, Guṇākara, and Ratikara—constructed the famous Lũ Dhvākhā (Golden Gate, BKT0080) in Bhaktapur’s palace area in 1753 CE (NS 874). The plaque also states that the three brothers jointly offered a diamond-studded necklace (herāphvaḥ) to Viśvakarmā in 1751 CE (NS 871). However, this date appears to be an error, as other inscriptions confirm that the offering was made in 1755 CE (NS 875), shortly after the Lũ Dhvākhā’s completion (S. Śākya NS 1141, p. 28)."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/995c1376-9e84-42a2-8f05-38b8d8a32a23> ;
    rdfs:comment "The members of Nī Bāhāḥ installed a copper plaque to honor their ancestors' contributions to art. The inscription mentions Guṇasiṃhadeva’s death in 1646 CE (NS 766) and records that his grandsons—Sabhākara, Guṇākara, and Ratikara—constructed the famous Lũ Dhvākhā (Golden Gate, BKT0080) in Bhaktapur’s palace area in 1753 CE (NS 874). The plaque also states that the three brothers jointly offered a diamond-studded necklace (herāphvaḥ) to Viśvakarmā in 1751 CE (NS 871). However, this date appears to be an error, as other inscriptions confirm that the offering was made in 1755 CE (NS 875), shortly after the Lũ Dhvākhā’s completion (S. Śākya NS 1141, p. 28)."@en ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/agent/antigravity_agent> ;
