<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/9d5039d0-e979-11e9-8bc4-0242ac130002_6> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Completion of construction"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Construction of Mahabuddha Temple was completed by Abhayarāja Śākya's grandson Jīvarāja and great grandson Jayamuni, following a model that Abhayarāja allegedly brought with him from Bodh Gaya (Gutschow2011, 516). King Shivasiṃha Malla was invited to participate in the worship ritual that was organised upon completion of the work. Siddhidevaju was the chiefācāryaon this occasion."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/9d5039d0-e979-11e9-8bc4-0242ac130002> ;
    rdfs:comment "Construction of Mahabuddha Temple was completed by Abhayarāja Śākya's grandson Jīvarāja and great grandson Jayamuni, following a model that Abhayarāja allegedly brought with him from Bodh Gaya (Gutschow2011, 516). King Shivasiṃha Malla was invited to participate in the worship ritual that was organised upon completion of the work. Siddhidevaju was the chiefācāryaon this occasion."@en ;
