<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/9d5039d0-e979-11e9-8bc4-0242ac130002_7> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Enshrinement ;
    rdfs:label "Donation to Red Matsyendranātha"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Paṇḍita Jīvarāja and Jayamuni went to Sikkim and offered a plate ofprasādafrom the Mahabuddha enshrined in thisvihārato the King of Sikkim. Grateful for this offering, the king filled the plate with gold. When Jayamuni returned with the gold, he called a meeting of the members of thesaṅghato determine what to do with it. They decided to make fixtures (side panels for the four sides, thetoraṇas, and the decorations above thetoraṇasfor the chariot) of the Red Matsyendranātha. These fixtures were placed upon the chariot for the first time in NS 774 upon its arrival to Gāḥ Bāhāḥ. Aguṭhīwas then set up to ensure the safekeeping and maintenance of the fixtures. Thisguṭhīwas known as theLusa Guṭhī,"@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/9d5039d0-e979-11e9-8bc4-0242ac130002> ;
    rdfs:comment "Paṇḍita Jīvarāja and Jayamuni went to Sikkim and offered a plate ofprasādafrom the Mahabuddha enshrined in thisvihārato the King of Sikkim. Grateful for this offering, the king filled the plate with gold. When Jayamuni returned with the gold, he called a meeting of the members of thesaṅghato determine what to do with it. They decided to make fixtures (side panels for the four sides, thetoraṇas, and the decorations above thetoraṇasfor the chariot) of the Red Matsyendranātha. These fixtures were placed upon the chariot for the first time in NS 774 upon its arrival to Gāḥ Bāhāḥ. Aguṭhīwas then set up to ensure the safekeeping and maintenance of the fixtures. Thisguṭhīwas known as theLusa Guṭhī,"@en ;
