<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/9d98c866-edfe-4172-9754-b538421ac2a1_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Enshrinement ;
    rdfs:label "Installation of pillar"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The lintel of the main temple's door is a repurposed stone memorial pillar. The pillar's typology dates it to the mid-14th century. Astūpais carved on the top of the pillar and a heavily eroded inscription written in Nāgarī script can be seen beneath thestūpa. Posterior to this original inscription are other more recent inscriptions and carvings, such as the central arch with round decorative patterns. To the right is a more legible inscription with the date 1976 (on the image). This date corresponds to 1919 CE when expressed in the Vikram era."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/9d98c866-edfe-4172-9754-b538421ac2a1> ;
    rdfs:comment "The lintel of the main temple's door is a repurposed stone memorial pillar. The pillar's typology dates it to the mid-14th century. Astūpais carved on the top of the pillar and a heavily eroded inscription written in Nāgarī script can be seen beneath thestūpa. Posterior to this original inscription are other more recent inscriptions and carvings, such as the central arch with round decorative patterns. To the right is a more legible inscription with the date 1976 (on the image). This date corresponds to 1919 CE when expressed in the Vikram era."@en ;
