<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/9f7e7e0a-af62-47e3-991d-e1efdddaba8d_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Donation (possibly the building of the sataḥ)"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Hailing from Prasannaśīla Mahāvihāra, Siṃhanarasiṃha Buddhācārya (text: Siṃghanarasiṃ Buddhācāryye), together with his wife Thakuṃlāni, sons Narasiṃha and Naramāna, as well as his daughter-in-law Mohanamāyā, made a charitable offering in honor of Nāmasaṅgīti, a revered figure within the Buddhist pantheon. While the specifics of the donation are not expounded upon, it is plausible that he was involved in the construction of thesataḥ, which was likely presented in dedication to the aforementioned deity. The inscription further documents Siṃharanasiṃha Buddhācārya's directive to commission a statue of Nāmasaṅgīti within thesataḥ, with the necessary funds originating from the rental income of his ancestral residence in the Bikumāḥchẽ Ṭola."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/9f7e7e0a-af62-47e3-991d-e1efdddaba8d> ;
    rdfs:comment "Hailing from Prasannaśīla Mahāvihāra, Siṃhanarasiṃha Buddhācārya (text: Siṃghanarasiṃ Buddhācāryye), together with his wife Thakuṃlāni, sons Narasiṃha and Naramāna, as well as his daughter-in-law Mohanamāyā, made a charitable offering in honor of Nāmasaṅgīti, a revered figure within the Buddhist pantheon. While the specifics of the donation are not expounded upon, it is plausible that he was involved in the construction of thesataḥ, which was likely presented in dedication to the aforementioned deity. The inscription further documents Siṃharanasiṃha Buddhācārya's directive to commission a statue of Nāmasaṅgīti within thesataḥ, with the necessary funds originating from the rental income of his ancestral residence in the Bikumāḥchẽ Ṭola."@en ;
