<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/9f7e7e0a-af62-47e3-991d-e1efdddaba8d_2> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:RitualEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Lakha Caitya Pūjā"@en ;
    dcterms:description "On the upper level of thesataḥ, a ritual known as \"Lakha Caitya Pūjā\" was conducted. This unique worship practice involves crafting one hundred thousandcaityas out of black clay. Similar ceremonies are periodically arranged by Buddhist monasteries across the Kathmandu Valley."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/9f7e7e0a-af62-47e3-991d-e1efdddaba8d> ;
    rdfs:comment "On the upper level of thesataḥ, a ritual known as \"Lakha Caitya Pūjā\" was conducted. This unique worship practice involves crafting one hundred thousandcaityas out of black clay. Similar ceremonies are periodically arranged by Buddhist monasteries across the Kathmandu Valley."@en ;
