    rdfs:label "Installation of the object on the toraṇa"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Thetoraṇaplaced above the temple’s entrance bears an inscription dating to 1820 CE (NS 940), installed by the Pañcadeśa group (KAT3380_I_001). Just below this inscription, another inscription is carved, stating that the central idol in thetoraṇawas made by the brothers of Cochẽ, representing the Daughter Goddess."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/a26fce6a-a88a-490d-b7af-0f1f556caeb1> ;
