<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/a2a8efa0-91ee-4242-b0be-1b8223a088c6_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:TransferOfCustody ;
    rdfs:label "Reconstruction"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Dr. Bal Gopal Shrestha and his wife, both from Sankhu, played pivotal roles in fundraising for the temple's reconstruction. Various organizations, including the Netherlands Nepal Association, Haliṃ Nevāḥ Dabū, Guthi Australia, and governmental entities such as the Shankharapur Municipality, provided financial support. The reconstruction process also included the addition of intricately carved struts, toraṇa, and pillars."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/a2a8efa0-91ee-4242-b0be-1b8223a088c6> ;
    rdfs:comment "Dr. Bal Gopal Shrestha and his wife, both from Sankhu, played pivotal roles in fundraising for the temple's reconstruction. Various organizations, including the Netherlands Nepal Association, Haliṃ Nevāḥ Dabū, Guthi Australia, and governmental entities such as the Shankharapur Municipality, provided financial support. The reconstruction process also included the addition of intricately carved struts, toraṇa, and pillars."@en ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/agent/antigravity_agent> ;
