<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/a2c08676-6005-4033-89f9-0b918c2bb663_9> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Unknown event"@en ;
    dcterms:description "A copper-plate inscription listing the names of Rājamāna Siṃha, Dinanātha, Nandalāla, Juju Ratna, Kāji Bahādura, and others is mounted on the upper storey of the temple. Although undated, the inscription appears, upon close observation, to be composed of fragments of a much larger inscription originally from another location, later brought here and reassembled on the temple wall."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/a2c08676-6005-4033-89f9-0b918c2bb663> ;
    rdfs:comment "A copper-plate inscription listing the names of Rājamāna Siṃha, Dinanātha, Nandalāla, Juju Ratna, Kāji Bahādura, and others is mounted on the upper storey of the temple. Although undated, the inscription appears, upon close observation, to be composed of fragments of a much larger inscription originally from another location, later brought here and reassembled on the temple wall."@en ;
