<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/a2cfeca7-18cd-4ba6-8793-4390725a1375_3> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Rebuilding of the monument"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The Department of Archeology reconstructed the temple. A photograph published by Pruscha (1975, p. 230) reveals that the temple's upper section featured a bell-shaped design, and its finial was notably tall. The recent reconstruction, however, replaced the bell-shaped dome with a dome and reduced the finial's height."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/a2cfeca7-18cd-4ba6-8793-4390725a1375> ;
    rdfs:comment "The Department of Archeology reconstructed the temple. A photograph published by Pruscha (1975, p. 230) reveals that the temple's upper section featured a bell-shaped design, and its finial was notably tall. The recent reconstruction, however, replaced the bell-shaped dome with a dome and reduced the finial's height."@en ;
