    hg:isEventOf <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/a32d51f6-544b-42f6-b432-481d4632c08d> .

<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/a3394b46-8421-4260-9385-6a5379527e60_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:ConditionAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Establishment of statues"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Statues of Śiva, Sarasvatī, Viṣṇu, Lokeśvara, Gaṇeśa, and others were established at theghāṭa. Although Topabahādura Khatrī oversaw their installation, his name is not mentioned in the inscription recording the event. However, his contribution is documented in another inscription he installed in 1978 CE."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/a3394b46-8421-4260-9385-6a5379527e60> ;
    rdfs:comment "Statues of Śiva, Sarasvatī, Viṣṇu, Lokeśvara, Gaṇeśa, and others were established at theghāṭa. Although Topabahādura Khatrī oversaw their installation, his name is not mentioned in the inscription recording the event. However, his contribution is documented in another inscription he installed in 1978 CE."@en ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/agent/antigravity_agent> ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/activity/heritagegraph_kg_construction> ;
    hg:eventIndex 0 ;
    hg:extractionMethod "source_table" ;
    hg:isEventOf <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/a3394b46-8421-4260-9385-6a5379527e60> .

<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/a3394b46-8421-4260-9385-6a5379527e60_1> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Enshrinement ;
    rdfs:label "Installation of inscription"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Thisghāṭaand itssataḥwere established by the ancestors of Topabahādura Khatrī, a local Panchyat-era zonal commissioner. He contributed various statues to theghāṭaand organized its religious functions by setting up a religious trust. An inscription by Khatrī details his religious devotion, the religious structures he founded, and his development initiatives, aiming to document his life's achievements. It mentions his installation of deities, the novel concept of apitṛ guṭhī, a religious trust dedicated to his ancestors, with donated properties intended for lineal descendants (including daughters in the absence of sons), and the income from this land being designated for weekly worship of deities in Sanepa and at theghāṭa. The inscription also mandates monthly full-moon worship and devotional singing at theghāṭa, and a Rāma Navamī exhibition of historical books and related images at thesataḥ. Furthermore, it outlines the deposit of principal in a bank for managing daily worship and annual tree planting through the interest. Interestingly, Khatrī even made provisions for his post-mortem devotional singing. As the head of the local construction improvement committee, a list of his accomplishments is included in the inscription. Following damage to thesataḥfrom a recent earthquake, the resident Girī family undertook partial repairs."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/a3394b46-8421-4260-9385-6a5379527e60> ;
    rdfs:comment "Thisghāṭaand itssataḥwere established by the ancestors of Topabahādura Khatrī, a local Panchyat-era zonal commissioner. He contributed various statues to theghāṭaand organized its religious functions by setting up a religious trust. An inscription by Khatrī details his religious devotion, the religious structures he founded, and his development initiatives, aiming to document his life's achievements. It mentions his installation of deities, the novel concept of apitṛ guṭhī, a religious trust dedicated to his ancestors, with donated properties intended for lineal descendants (including daughters in the absence of sons), and the income from this land being designated for weekly worship of deities in Sanepa and at theghāṭa. The inscription also mandates monthly full-moon worship and devotional singing at theghāṭa, and a Rāma Navamī exhibition of historical books and related images at thesataḥ. Furthermore, it outlines the deposit of principal in a bank for managing daily worship and annual tree planting through the interest. Interestingly, Khatrī even made provisions for his post-mortem devotional singing. As the head of the local construction improvement committee, a list of his accomplishments is included in the inscription. Following damage to thesataḥfrom a recent earthquake, the resident Girī family undertook partial repairs."@en ;
