        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "First mention of Arkhu Bahī"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The earliest historical reference to the Arakhu Bahī is a stone inscription from 1685 CE (NS 805) at Vijayevar Temple (KAT3200), which is located to the east of the Buddha statue in the bhaviṣyavyākaraṇamudrā (object number KAT3200-007). The inscription commemorates a donation made by a monk named  Bhikṣu Jinideva and his family, from Italaṅṣu Mahāvihāra, Arkhu Bahī of Yatkhā, Kathmandu."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/aa8a44d5-9ad3-4f85-9263-512d5afd1011> ;
    rdfs:comment "The earliest historical reference to the Arakhu Bahī is a stone inscription from 1685 CE (NS 805) at Vijayevar Temple (KAT3200), which is located to the east of the Buddha statue in the bhaviṣyavyākaraṇamudrā (object number KAT3200-007). The inscription commemorates a donation made by a monk named  Bhikṣu Jinideva and his family, from Italaṅṣu Mahāvihāra, Arkhu Bahī of Yatkhā, Kathmandu."@en ;
