        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Establishment of the Sataḥ and Rādhākṛṣṇa Temple (KAT2710)"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The foundation of the Sataḥ and Rādhākṛṣṇa Temple was laid in honor of Bhāgavatabhakta Māthemā's commitment. Sardāra Haribhakta Māthemā, a poet who expressed his literary prowess in Nepalbhasa, was the father of Bhāgavatabhakta Māthemā. Among the four martyrs, Dharmabhakta Māthemā was Bhāgavatabhakta Māthemā's grandson (L. Śākya NS 1122, p.17). Kājī Bhāgavatbhakta, driven by his dedication, pledged to establish the Rādhākṛṣṇa temple (KAT2710) along with this Sataḥ. Despite his passing, he designated 20murīsof paddy and 1murī10pāṭhī(9ropanī-s, 12ānā) of land for the annual rituals of the Sataḥ and temple. He couldn't fulfill his commitment during his lifetime. In fulfillment of his wish, Bhāgavatbhakta Māthemā's five sons, named Subbā Vedabhakta, Subbā Ādībhakta, Subbā Lilābhakta, Kharidāra Haṃśabhakta, and Kharidāra Ratnabhakta, undertook the construction of both the Sataḥ and the Rādhakṛṣṇa temple (KAT2710)."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/aabd2eaa-8fcb-4043-b307-0b431934f800> ;
    rdfs:comment "The foundation of the Sataḥ and Rādhākṛṣṇa Temple was laid in honor of Bhāgavatabhakta Māthemā's commitment. Sardāra Haribhakta Māthemā, a poet who expressed his literary prowess in Nepalbhasa, was the father of Bhāgavatabhakta Māthemā. Among the four martyrs, Dharmabhakta Māthemā was Bhāgavatabhakta Māthemā's grandson (L. Śākya NS 1122, p.17). Kājī Bhāgavatbhakta, driven by his dedication, pledged to establish the Rādhākṛṣṇa temple (KAT2710) along with this Sataḥ. Despite his passing, he designated 20murīsof paddy and 1murī10pāṭhī(9ropanī-s, 12ānā) of land for the annual rituals of the Sataḥ and temple. He couldn't fulfill his commitment during his lifetime. In fulfillment of his wish, Bhāgavatbhakta Māthemā's five sons, named Subbā Vedabhakta, Subbā Ādībhakta, Subbā Lilābhakta, Kharidāra Haṃśabhakta, and Kharidāra Ratnabhakta, undertook the construction of both the Sataḥ and the Rādhakṛṣṇa temple (KAT2710)."@en ;
