<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/ac18b25b-3750-43c5-b210-30375b978271_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Establishment of Mahākāla"@en ;
    dcterms:description "This inscription on the pedestal of the Mahākāla statue is erroneously dated \"Saṃvat7009,\" which can be accurately dated to NS 709 (1589 CE) based on the mention of King Śivasiṃhadeva (r. 1578-1619 CE) and his brother, Raṇajitasiṃha. While some names like Hāku, Lavasiṃha, and Gunasiṃha are legible, the inscription remains largely indecipherable. It is plausible that these individuals collectively commissioned the establishment of this Mahākāla statue, along with the accompanying sculpture of Sarasvatī."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/ac18b25b-3750-43c5-b210-30375b978271> ;
    rdfs:comment "This inscription on the pedestal of the Mahākāla statue is erroneously dated \"Saṃvat7009,\" which can be accurately dated to NS 709 (1589 CE) based on the mention of King Śivasiṃhadeva (r. 1578-1619 CE) and his brother, Raṇajitasiṃha. While some names like Hāku, Lavasiṃha, and Gunasiṃha are legible, the inscription remains largely indecipherable. It is plausible that these individuals collectively commissioned the establishment of this Mahākāla statue, along with the accompanying sculpture of Sarasvatī."@en ;
