<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/ad1fdb35-7451-40e3-a06f-5423bc025d6d_1> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Enshrinement ;
    rdfs:label "Offering a bell"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Kāśīrāja Panḍita Satyāla, along with his wife Bhavānīdevī and son Śivarāja Paṇḍita Satyāla, made an offering by presenting a bell (object no. KAT2730-013) to the Dvārikānātha Mandira. This temple was constructed by Kāśīrāja Panḍita Satyāla, where a statue of Viṣṇu (KAT2730-012) was enshrined. This offering possibly coincided with the time of the construction of the shrines."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/ad1fdb35-7451-40e3-a06f-5423bc025d6d> ;
    rdfs:comment "Kāśīrāja Panḍita Satyāla, along with his wife Bhavānīdevī and son Śivarāja Paṇḍita Satyāla, made an offering by presenting a bell (object no. KAT2730-013) to the Dvārikānātha Mandira. This temple was constructed by Kāśīrāja Panḍita Satyāla, where a statue of Viṣṇu (KAT2730-012) was enshrined. This offering possibly coincided with the time of the construction of the shrines."@en ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/agent/antigravity_agent> ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/activity/heritagegraph_kg_construction> ;
    hg:eventIndex 1 ;
    hg:extractionMethod "source_table" ;
    hg:isEventOf <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/ad1fdb35-7451-40e3-a06f-5423bc025d6d> .

<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/ad1fdb35-7451-40e3-a06f-5423bc025d6d_2> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:TransferOfCustody ;
    rdfs:label "Endowment of lands"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Kāśīrāja Panḍita Satyāla, along with his wife Bhavānīdevī, son Śivarāja Paṇḍita Satyāla, and daughter-in-law, made endowments of land. These endowments established a trust aimed at facilitating the observance of daily and anniversary rituals for the temples, the provision of musical instruments during the daily rituals, and the offering of alms to mendicants on the occasion of Śivarātrī, the 14th day of the dark fortnight of the month Phālguna"@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/ad1fdb35-7451-40e3-a06f-5423bc025d6d> ;
    rdfs:comment "Kāśīrāja Panḍita Satyāla, along with his wife Bhavānīdevī, son Śivarāja Paṇḍita Satyāla, and daughter-in-law, made endowments of land. These endowments established a trust aimed at facilitating the observance of daily and anniversary rituals for the temples, the provision of musical instruments during the daily rituals, and the offering of alms to mendicants on the occasion of Śivarātrī, the 14th day of the dark fortnight of the month Phālguna"@en ;
