<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/adad44a2-9ffc-4a05-ba82-ad6d39f10c17_1> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Establishment of the śivaliṅga?"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The inscription on thejalaharībase of theśivaliṅgainside the sanctum cannot be fully understood due to chips coming off it. While its content appears to deal with the establishment of aśivaliṅga, the name of the donor is unclear but the term \"rājendra,\" meaning \"the king of kings,\" is legible. Possibly, Pārthivendra Malla also established theśivaliṅgarevered as Kapileśvara while also installing the inscription (NWK0650_I_001) with verses dedicated to Brahmeśvara Mahādeva."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/adad44a2-9ffc-4a05-ba82-ad6d39f10c17> ;
    rdfs:comment "The inscription on thejalaharībase of theśivaliṅgainside the sanctum cannot be fully understood due to chips coming off it. While its content appears to deal with the establishment of aśivaliṅga, the name of the donor is unclear but the term \"rājendra,\" meaning \"the king of kings,\" is legible. Possibly, Pārthivendra Malla also established theśivaliṅgarevered as Kapileśvara while also installing the inscription (NWK0650_I_001) with verses dedicated to Brahmeśvara Mahādeva."@en ;
