        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Establishment of the Padmasambhava statue"@en ;
    dcterms:description "A statue of Guru Padmasambhava, brought from New Delhi, India, was established west of the Kapileśvara Mandira. Followers of Tibetan Buddhism believe that Guru Padmasambhava meditated on the Kabilāsa hill before heading to Tibet."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/adad44a2-9ffc-4a05-ba82-ad6d39f10c17> ;
