<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/adfd2472-e808-11e9-8bc4-0242ac130002_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:RitualEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Construction of the Sataḥ"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The Sataḥwas built by Nārāyaṇa Jośī. The inscription mentions that he built the Sataḥwith the help of Kājī Śamśera Jaṅga Pāṇḍe. However, it not clear whether Kāji Śamśera provided him with money, land or something else in helping him to construct the Sataḥ.The inscription begins with the name of Lord Gaṇeśa and also mentions a special worship (pūjā) to him on the day of Indrajātrā, thus clearly connecting the Sataḥ to a shrine of Gaṇeśa."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/adfd2472-e808-11e9-8bc4-0242ac130002> ;
    rdfs:comment "The Sataḥwas built by Nārāyaṇa Jośī. The inscription mentions that he built the Sataḥwith the help of Kājī Śamśera Jaṅga Pāṇḍe. However, it not clear whether Kāji Śamśera provided him with money, land or something else in helping him to construct the Sataḥ.The inscription begins with the name of Lord Gaṇeśa and also mentions a special worship (pūjā) to him on the day of Indrajātrā, thus clearly connecting the Sataḥ to a shrine of Gaṇeśa."@en ;
