<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/af614ba6-19ef-4239-aeea-fb3a9106e659_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Consecration ;
    rdfs:label "Initial construction"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Visarāma Bhābo, his wife Lakṣmī (text: Rakṣmī), and his family members commissioned the Mandaḥ Phalcā (text:maṇḍapa), along with ajaḥdhuṃwater tank. The inscription is primarily a stonedalūlampstand with a small statue of Padmapāṇi Lokeśvara atop it, along with what appear to be two standing figures of donors. Thephalcāwas consecrated on the 1st of the bright fortnight of Vaiśākha, the same day the statue of Buṅgadyaḥ is placed on the chariot in Pulcoka."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/af614ba6-19ef-4239-aeea-fb3a9106e659> ;
    rdfs:comment "Visarāma Bhābo, his wife Lakṣmī (text: Rakṣmī), and his family members commissioned the Mandaḥ Phalcā (text:maṇḍapa), along with ajaḥdhuṃwater tank. The inscription is primarily a stonedalūlampstand with a small statue of Padmapāṇi Lokeśvara atop it, along with what appear to be two standing figures of donors. Thephalcāwas consecrated on the 1st of the bright fortnight of Vaiśākha, the same day the statue of Buṅgadyaḥ is placed on the chariot in Pulcoka."@en ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/agent/antigravity_agent> ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/activity/heritagegraph_kg_construction> ;
    hg:eventIndex 0 ;
    hg:extractionMethod "source_table" ;
    hg:isEventOf <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/af614ba6-19ef-4239-aeea-fb3a9106e659> .

<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/af614ba6-19ef-4239-aeea-fb3a9106e659_1> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Establishment of trust"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Bhikṣu Indraśvari, Manasiṅa Bhābo, Punasiṅa Bhābo, Majurāma Bhābo, and Bhaginī Mayi made cash donations for the worship of Buṅgadyaḥ and the main deity of a nearbybahī, and for the distribution ofsamaybaji. The formation of the trust came five years after the inception of thephalcā."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/af614ba6-19ef-4239-aeea-fb3a9106e659> ;
    rdfs:comment "Bhikṣu Indraśvari, Manasiṅa Bhābo, Punasiṅa Bhābo, Majurāma Bhābo, and Bhaginī Mayi made cash donations for the worship of Buṅgadyaḥ and the main deity of a nearbybahī, and for the distribution ofsamaybaji. The formation of the trust came five years after the inception of thephalcā."@en ;
