<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/b03b206c-7c4e-4669-9a85-ac8f53e8b22e_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:RitualEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Erection of a dharmastambha"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The Vaiṣṇava reformer Kaviprasāda conductedbhajana-kīrtana, charitable donations, and a continuousahorātra yajñain front of the Varāha image, erecting a stone pillar (dharma-stambha) to commemorate the event. The inscription on this pillar instructs that such observances should continue annually on the same day. Since the Newar community traditionally performed goat sacrifices duringdegu-pūjās near the image, the inscription explicitly declares this site to be aViṣṇu-kṣetra, forbidding all acts of violence (hiṃsā)."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/b03b206c-7c4e-4669-9a85-ac8f53e8b22e> ;
    rdfs:comment "The Vaiṣṇava reformer Kaviprasāda conductedbhajana-kīrtana, charitable donations, and a continuousahorātra yajñain front of the Varāha image, erecting a stone pillar (dharma-stambha) to commemorate the event. The inscription on this pillar instructs that such observances should continue annually on the same day. Since the Newar community traditionally performed goat sacrifices duringdegu-pūjās near the image, the inscription explicitly declares this site to be aViṣṇu-kṣetra, forbidding all acts of violence (hiṃsā)."@en ;
