<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/b071cb98-09af-42ce-8334-6ea037aacb5e_2> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Offering of oil lamp stand"@en ;
    dcterms:description "A partially damaged stone oil lamp is kept within the sanctum. An inscription is engraved on its surface, though nearly half of it has weathered away. The stand bears carved figures of the donor family, with their names inscribed in the lower  part of the images. The donors of this object were Ganasiṃ and Cikuti. It remains uncertain whether the oil lamp stand was originally dedicated to this temple or brought here from elsewhere, where it might have been simply lying around."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/b071cb98-09af-42ce-8334-6ea037aacb5e> ;
    rdfs:comment "A partially damaged stone oil lamp is kept within the sanctum. An inscription is engraved on its surface, though nearly half of it has weathered away. The stand bears carved figures of the donor family, with their names inscribed in the lower  part of the images. The donors of this object were Ganasiṃ and Cikuti. It remains uncertain whether the oil lamp stand was originally dedicated to this temple or brought here from elsewhere, where it might have been simply lying around."@en ;
