        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Construction of a caitya"@en ;
    dcterms:description "In the northwestern corner of the temple is a small courtyard containing two caitya and a historic well. One of the caitya bears an inscription on the lower part of its eastern surface. According to the inscription, a Persian resident of the same courtyard, named Kehemāna, along with his family members, constructed this caitya."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/b071cb98-09af-42ce-8334-6ea037aacb5e> ;
