<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/b1db9a43-c69d-4054-b063-57a9d72eb2d9_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Addition of a statue"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Bhagīratha Bhaiyā, a trusted minister of King Śrīnivāsa Malla, dedicated a Garuḍa image to Śikharanārāyaṇa (also known as Śeṣanārāyaṇa). The responsibility for its preservation was entrusted to Amātya Naraharī Bhāro, a resident of the Ikhālakhu quarter in Patan. Today, this Garuḍa image is no longer placed in front of Śeṣanārāyaṇa but instead stands before the Kṛṣṇa Temple (PRN0080-001). It appears that at some point in time, likely out of ignorance, the image was relocated to its current position."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/b1db9a43-c69d-4054-b063-57a9d72eb2d9> ;
    rdfs:comment "Bhagīratha Bhaiyā, a trusted minister of King Śrīnivāsa Malla, dedicated a Garuḍa image to Śikharanārāyaṇa (also known as Śeṣanārāyaṇa). The responsibility for its preservation was entrusted to Amātya Naraharī Bhāro, a resident of the Ikhālakhu quarter in Patan. Today, this Garuḍa image is no longer placed in front of Śeṣanārāyaṇa but instead stands before the Kṛṣṇa Temple (PRN0080-001). It appears that at some point in time, likely out of ignorance, the image was relocated to its current position."@en ;
