<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/b21b09ef-1998-4f1f-8e8b-ffe6b99f9116_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:TransferOfCustody ;
    rdfs:label "Initial construction of the capāḥ (Gaṇeśa Bhajana Phalcā)"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The Phalcā was constructed on the plots of land endowed by three persons from the Su Bāhāḥ Ṭola—Jivarāma Bhābo, Hṛdāma Bhābo, and Jayarāma Bhābo.  Its initial construction took place when a person named Jyoti was thethakāliof a group that used to conductaṣṭamīvrata, a ritual fast observed on the 8thlunar day. Although it is aphalcāat present, its inscription refers to the building as acapāḥ."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/b21b09ef-1998-4f1f-8e8b-ffe6b99f9116> ;
    rdfs:comment "The Phalcā was constructed on the plots of land endowed by three persons from the Su Bāhāḥ Ṭola—Jivarāma Bhābo, Hṛdāma Bhābo, and Jayarāma Bhābo.  Its initial construction took place when a person named Jyoti was thethakāliof a group that used to conductaṣṭamīvrata, a ritual fast observed on the 8thlunar day. Although it is aphalcāat present, its inscription refers to the building as acapāḥ."@en ;
