<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/b47cd1c2-cf8d-4070-9369-56e87e14606c_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Initial construction of the Phalcā"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The Phalcā was constructed by the ‘Māheśvarī Pīṭha Saṃrakṣaṇa tathā Vikāsa Samiti’, a committee of locals formed in 2000 CE (VS 2057) for the conservation of the Pīṭha premises. According to senior citizens from the area, there used to be a three-bayedphalcāsouth of the Māheśvarī Pīṭha. It was destroyed in the early 1960s due to the lack of timely maintenance and was never rebuilt. In 2004 CE, a new Phalcā was built a few meters northeast of the spot where the lost Phalcā once stood."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/b47cd1c2-cf8d-4070-9369-56e87e14606c> ;
    rdfs:comment "The Phalcā was constructed by the ‘Māheśvarī Pīṭha Saṃrakṣaṇa tathā Vikāsa Samiti’, a committee of locals formed in 2000 CE (VS 2057) for the conservation of the Pīṭha premises. According to senior citizens from the area, there used to be a three-bayedphalcāsouth of the Māheśvarī Pīṭha. It was destroyed in the early 1960s due to the lack of timely maintenance and was never rebuilt. In 2004 CE, a new Phalcā was built a few meters northeast of the spot where the lost Phalcā once stood."@en ;
