<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/b53e45b8-ebf5-11e9-b125-0242ac130002_1> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Consecration ;
    rdfs:label "Consecration of image of wooden Vajrasattva"@en ;
    dcterms:description "During the reign of King Yakṣa Malla, the Mahāpātras of the Piṃ Bāhāla area of Patan performed a great fire worship (yajña) and established a wooden image of Vajrasattva Tathāgata. On the same occasion they offered a bronze image of the moon, two bells and abhṛṅgāra. However, the image of the Vajrasattva kept inside the sanctum of the Bāhāḥ has since been stolen."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/b53e45b8-ebf5-11e9-b125-0242ac130002> ;
    rdfs:comment "During the reign of King Yakṣa Malla, the Mahāpātras of the Piṃ Bāhāla area of Patan performed a great fire worship (yajña) and established a wooden image of Vajrasattva Tathāgata. On the same occasion they offered a bronze image of the moon, two bells and abhṛṅgāra. However, the image of the Vajrasattva kept inside the sanctum of the Bāhāḥ has since been stolen."@en ;
