<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/b590981b-1498-4400-9cd7-f263bdaf4131_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Restoration of the Hiti"@en ;
    dcterms:description "With the permission of the Vajrayoginī Sevā Samiti-a local organization formed for the conservation of the area, the family of Kṛṣṇa Kumārī Śreṣṭha belonging to a clan named Baḥsimākva Khalaḥ had commissioned the reconstruction of the Hiti. Concrete was used on the wall from which the spouts protrude and marble slabs with line carvings of the figures of the moon deity (Candra) and the sun deity (Sūrya) were also posted on the Wall."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/b590981b-1498-4400-9cd7-f263bdaf4131> ;
    rdfs:comment "With the permission of the Vajrayoginī Sevā Samiti-a local organization formed for the conservation of the area, the family of Kṛṣṇa Kumārī Śreṣṭha belonging to a clan named Baḥsimākva Khalaḥ had commissioned the reconstruction of the Hiti. Concrete was used on the wall from which the spouts protrude and marble slabs with line carvings of the figures of the moon deity (Candra) and the sun deity (Sūrya) were also posted on the Wall."@en ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/agent/antigravity_agent> ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/activity/heritagegraph_kg_construction> ;
    hg:eventIndex 0 ;
    hg:extractionMethod "source_table" ;
    hg:isEventOf <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/b590981b-1498-4400-9cd7-f263bdaf4131> .

<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/b591fd8e-c93c-4ddc-929d-f8ae35c530a0_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Establishment of the śivaliṅga (?)"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The tip of thejalaharīfaces north while an inscription from the era of King Rāmadeva is found on its western side. According to the inscription, in 546 CE (Śaka Era 467), a woman named Mānamatī donated land to establish a trust in the name of Nātheśvara. However, it remains unclear from the inscription whether she solely founded the trust or also established the Nātheśvara Śivaliṅga. It also records the donation of land for a sage named Khuḍu Svāmī. This inscription holds significant historical value, as it not only introduced King Rāmadeva into the Licchavi lineage but also illuminated the rising influence of a courtier named Kramalīna during that period."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/b591fd8e-c93c-4ddc-929d-f8ae35c530a0> ;
    rdfs:comment "The tip of thejalaharīfaces north while an inscription from the era of King Rāmadeva is found on its western side. According to the inscription, in 546 CE (Śaka Era 467), a woman named Mānamatī donated land to establish a trust in the name of Nātheśvara. However, it remains unclear from the inscription whether she solely founded the trust or also established the Nātheśvara Śivaliṅga. It also records the donation of land for a sage named Khuḍu Svāmī. This inscription holds significant historical value, as it not only introduced King Rāmadeva into the Licchavi lineage but also illuminated the rising influence of a courtier named Kramalīna during that period."@en ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/agent/antigravity_agent> ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/activity/heritagegraph_kg_construction> ;
