    rdfs:label "Donation of land"@en ;
    dcterms:description "It is likely that the Phalcā got the name Maṇikula Phalcā ('the Phalcā of the jewel clan') because it belonged to a man called Maniratna of Maṇikula Bahā. The donor offered 5ropanisof land (called Thacheṣelakṣetra) to finance the renovation of the Phalcā. The descendants of the donors were allowed to use any surplus money.Donation of land, 5ropanīs"@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/b7910d9c-e915-11e9-b125-0242ac130002> ;
    rdfs:comment "It is likely that the Phalcā got the name Maṇikula Phalcā ('the Phalcā of the jewel clan') because it belonged to a man called Maniratna of Maṇikula Bahā. The donor offered 5ropanisof land (called Thacheṣelakṣetra) to finance the renovation of the Phalcā. The descendants of the donors were allowed to use any surplus money.Donation of land, 5ropanīs"@en ;
