<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/b8c5d7c9-4fb2-4c4d-ac48-4f42756f1174_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Consecration ;
    rdfs:label "Installation of statue of Dakṣiṇakālī"@en ;
    dcterms:description "According to tradition, the goddess appeared to King Pratāpa Malla in a dream and commanded him to fashion and install her image; in obedience to this injunction, the king had the image made and consecrated. TheBhāṣā Vaṃśāvalīprovides further details of this event, stating that Pratāpa Malla performed the full rites of consecration (pratiṣṭhākarman) by completing themahāpūjā,sahasrabali, andnarabali, and formally installed the image on third of bright fortnight of Vaiśākha."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/b8c5d7c9-4fb2-4c4d-ac48-4f42756f1174> ;
    rdfs:comment "According to tradition, the goddess appeared to King Pratāpa Malla in a dream and commanded him to fashion and install her image; in obedience to this injunction, the king had the image made and consecrated. TheBhāṣā Vaṃśāvalīprovides further details of this event, stating that Pratāpa Malla performed the full rites of consecration (pratiṣṭhākarman) by completing themahāpūjā,sahasrabali, andnarabali, and formally installed the image on third of bright fortnight of Vaiśākha."@en ;
