    rdfs:label "Offering of gilded caduvā, kikiṃpā, crown, and silver"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Among the series of stone inscriptions erected behind the Dakṣiṇakālī Temple, one records that Śrī Bhuvanakumārī, the wife of Kāji Amṛtasiṃha Thāpā, donated to the goddess a gildedcaduvā(ilāṃ), akikiṃpā, a crown, and 108tolāof silver."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/b8c5d7c9-4fb2-4c4d-ac48-4f42756f1174> ;
