<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/b8f4c2b9-7ba1-4c7d-bc70-40d99b5c4a81_2> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Renovation of the bridge"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Bālanarasiṃha Kũvara, father of Jaṅga Bahādura Rāṇā, constructed a metal bridge following the construction of a bridge by Candravīra and Raṇajita Kũvara that had been damaged. Simultaneously, Vīrabhadra Kũvara, son of Candravīra, built another bridge over the Balkhu river, established a Gaṇeśa statue nearby that he named Vīravināyaka after himself, and constructed Sataḥ there. He additionally set up a trust that offered food to people coming forpiṇḍadāna, the annual offering of rice balls to deceased ancestors, at Mātātīrtha on the new moon day of Vaiśākha."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/b8f4c2b9-7ba1-4c7d-bc70-40d99b5c4a81> ;
    rdfs:comment "Bālanarasiṃha Kũvara, father of Jaṅga Bahādura Rāṇā, constructed a metal bridge following the construction of a bridge by Candravīra and Raṇajita Kũvara that had been damaged. Simultaneously, Vīrabhadra Kũvara, son of Candravīra, built another bridge over the Balkhu river, established a Gaṇeśa statue nearby that he named Vīravināyaka after himself, and constructed Sataḥ there. He additionally set up a trust that offered food to people coming forpiṇḍadāna, the annual offering of rice balls to deceased ancestors, at Mātātīrtha on the new moon day of Vaiśākha."@en ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/agent/antigravity_agent> ;
