<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/b8f4c2b9-7ba1-4c7d-bc70-40d99b5c4a81_3> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:TransferOfCustody ;
    rdfs:label "Construction of bridge and Sarasvatī Sataḥ"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Vīrabhadra Kũvara built a bridge over the Bagmati river near the Vatsalā temple (PPK0224) and established avāṇaliṅga(naturally-formedśivaliṅga) to the east of the bridge, naming it Vīrabhadreśvara - after himself. On the same day, he initiated the construction of two Sataḥs: one next to Vīrabhadreśvara, the second next to the Maṅgalā Gaurī temple. The one he built next to the Maṅgalā Gaurī temple is Sarasvatī Sataḥ. Vīrabhadra also established a statue of himself and his wife south of the Paśupatinātha temple and set up a trust by endowing land parcels for performing regular worships there. The two bridges east of the Vatsalā temple are probably initiated by him."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/b8f4c2b9-7ba1-4c7d-bc70-40d99b5c4a81> ;
    rdfs:comment "Vīrabhadra Kũvara built a bridge over the Bagmati river near the Vatsalā temple (PPK0224) and established avāṇaliṅga(naturally-formedśivaliṅga) to the east of the bridge, naming it Vīrabhadreśvara - after himself. On the same day, he initiated the construction of two Sataḥs: one next to Vīrabhadreśvara, the second next to the Maṅgalā Gaurī temple. The one he built next to the Maṅgalā Gaurī temple is Sarasvatī Sataḥ. Vīrabhadra also established a statue of himself and his wife south of the Paśupatinātha temple and set up a trust by endowing land parcels for performing regular worships there. The two bridges east of the Vatsalā temple are probably initiated by him."@en ;
