<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/b947bd74-dc11-46f3-afd4-189d70f64e3c_2> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Endowment of lands"@en ;
    dcterms:description "This inscription does not seem to be related to the Satyanārāyaṇa temple and was probably brought from elsewhere to be placed within the temple. The inscription mentions that Muni Thakuṃ and Dhanamāyā Śreṣṭha constructed aphalcāon the road leading from the east to the west of Hā̃ḍīgāũ. Due topotātax imposed on the tworopanīs of land allocated for thephalcā, they donated it to a trust. The trust members performed fire oblations in front of thephalcāonce a year and offered refreshments to travelers."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/b947bd74-dc11-46f3-afd4-189d70f64e3c> ;
    rdfs:comment "This inscription does not seem to be related to the Satyanārāyaṇa temple and was probably brought from elsewhere to be placed within the temple. The inscription mentions that Muni Thakuṃ and Dhanamāyā Śreṣṭha constructed aphalcāon the road leading from the east to the west of Hā̃ḍīgāũ. Due topotātax imposed on the tworopanīs of land allocated for thephalcā, they donated it to a trust. The trust members performed fire oblations in front of thephalcāonce a year and offered refreshments to travelers."@en ;
