<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/b947bd74-dc11-46f3-afd4-189d70f64e3c_7> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "GPR survey"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Durham University in the UK, in partnership with the Department of Archaeology, conducted a Ground Penetrating Radar (GPR) survey primarily focusing on the western and southern areas within the temple courtyard. The GPR survey revealed buried heaps of stone and brick. These remains could be the scattered remnants of walls collapsed in an earthquake. The survey suggested that further archaeological excavations should be undertaken to explore the possibility of an ancient urban settlement within the temple complex."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/b947bd74-dc11-46f3-afd4-189d70f64e3c> ;
    rdfs:comment "Durham University in the UK, in partnership with the Department of Archaeology, conducted a Ground Penetrating Radar (GPR) survey primarily focusing on the western and southern areas within the temple courtyard. The GPR survey revealed buried heaps of stone and brick. These remains could be the scattered remnants of walls collapsed in an earthquake. The survey suggested that further archaeological excavations should be undertaken to explore the possibility of an ancient urban settlement within the temple complex."@en ;
