<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/ba4a96ce-5b25-4ede-9c17-7bf5f88b5534_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Initial construction of the Dhāmī Ghara"@en ;
    dcterms:description "An inscription at the Bhairavī temple (NWK0040) suggests its initial construction. The inscription records the \"construction of a house\" by the then Bhelu (Dhāmī) Kṛṣṇa and Bhulu (Dhaminī) Sūryalakṣmī, and it further instructs their eldest son and daughter-in-law, who are the inheritors of the Bhelu and Bhulu titles, to \"reside in this house and maintain it.\" It is most likely that the house discussed in the inscription is the Dhāmī Ghara."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/ba4a96ce-5b25-4ede-9c17-7bf5f88b5534> ;
    rdfs:comment "An inscription at the Bhairavī temple (NWK0040) suggests its initial construction. The inscription records the \"construction of a house\" by the then Bhelu (Dhāmī) Kṛṣṇa and Bhulu (Dhaminī) Sūryalakṣmī, and it further instructs their eldest son and daughter-in-law, who are the inheritors of the Bhelu and Bhulu titles, to \"reside in this house and maintain it.\" It is most likely that the house discussed in the inscription is the Dhāmī Ghara."@en ;
