<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/bba70d79-c208-408d-97b7-9872385c6376_2> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Covering of the pinnacle"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The work of covering the upper part of the caitya—from the harmikā upward—with gilded brass was done by Kṛṣṇabahādura Citrakāra in 1935 CE (NS 1055). Judging by the style of the images and the stone carvings used in thecaitya, it appears to have been built in the early Śāha period; however, in the absence of an inscription, this cannot be stated with certainty."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/bba70d79-c208-408d-97b7-9872385c6376> ;
    rdfs:comment "The work of covering the upper part of the caitya—from the harmikā upward—with gilded brass was done by Kṛṣṇabahādura Citrakāra in 1935 CE (NS 1055). Judging by the style of the images and the stone carvings used in thecaitya, it appears to have been built in the early Śāha period; however, in the absence of an inscription, this cannot be stated with certainty."@en ;
