<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/bc3c1b44-e60d-11e9-8bc4-0242ac130002_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Construction of the Phalcā"@en ;
    dcterms:description "This inscription from NS 785 is attached to the eastern wall of the Phalcā. According to the inscription, the Phalcā was constructed with three bays by a group of Bhāvos. This inscription indicates that there used to be two bays previously, thus allowing for the addition of a third one. Above of the inscription one can see a statue of Padmapāṇi Lokeśvara standing intribaṅga āsanawith two hands. The statue is holding a flower of lotus in its left hand and holding its right hand in a gesture ofvarad.Candraandsūryahave also been inscribed on Lokeśvara's left and right sides respectively.This is a fine example of inscription worship. On the top of the inscription, there is an icon of Bungadyaḥ. Worshipping of the inscription equals worshipping the deity. Some say that itt is not allowed there to sit in thephalcāin front of the inscription showing the back of the body. It is considered as an insult like to a king."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/bc3c1b44-e60d-11e9-8bc4-0242ac130002> ;
    rdfs:comment "This inscription from NS 785 is attached to the eastern wall of the Phalcā. According to the inscription, the Phalcā was constructed with three bays by a group of Bhāvos. This inscription indicates that there used to be two bays previously, thus allowing for the addition of a third one. Above of the inscription one can see a statue of Padmapāṇi Lokeśvara standing intribaṅga āsanawith two hands. The statue is holding a flower of lotus in its left hand and holding its right hand in a gesture ofvarad.Candraandsūryahave also been inscribed on Lokeśvara's left and right sides respectively.This is a fine example of inscription worship. On the top of the inscription, there is an icon of Bungadyaḥ. Worshipping of the inscription equals worshipping the deity. Some say that itt is not allowed there to sit in thephalcāin front of the inscription showing the back of the body. It is considered as an insult like to a king."@en ;
