<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/bc3ed96d-1b65-4a64-86e6-f1543bfb5f3c_1> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Consecration ;
    rdfs:label "Construction of the temple and endowment of lands"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The queen of King Bhūpatīndra Malla of Bhaktapur and Viśvalakṣmīdevī, the mother of King Rañajita Malla, built the Brahmāyaṇī temple with a gilded finial (molamba). She endowed twentyropanīof agricultural land asguṭhīfor the temple’s maintenance, with provisions for ritual worship at both Brahmāyaṇī and Indreśvara temples on nineth of bright fortnight of Āṣāḍha. The meat of the sacrificial goat offered during the worship was to be distributed to the king, the prince, and the queen-mother as consecrated food (prasāda). She also arranged for an annual state offering of twotolasof silver to Brahmāyaṇī and donated various utensils."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/bc3ed96d-1b65-4a64-86e6-f1543bfb5f3c> ;
    rdfs:comment "The queen of King Bhūpatīndra Malla of Bhaktapur and Viśvalakṣmīdevī, the mother of King Rañajita Malla, built the Brahmāyaṇī temple with a gilded finial (molamba). She endowed twentyropanīof agricultural land asguṭhīfor the temple’s maintenance, with provisions for ritual worship at both Brahmāyaṇī and Indreśvara temples on nineth of bright fortnight of Āṣāḍha. The meat of the sacrificial goat offered during the worship was to be distributed to the king, the prince, and the queen-mother as consecrated food (prasāda). She also arranged for an annual state offering of twotolasof silver to Brahmāyaṇī and donated various utensils."@en ;
