<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/bc3ed96d-1b65-4a64-86e6-f1543bfb5f3c_6> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Unknown"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Because many of the characters of the inscription (śilāpatra) are broken, the date and most details cannot be deciphered. Names such asAnanta Bhari,Lele Bhari, andRāma Bhārocan be read. Judging from the script, the inscription appears to belong to the early medieval period. Thus, it likely predates the conversion of the open Brahmāyaṇīpīṭhainto the present temple."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/bc3ed96d-1b65-4a64-86e6-f1543bfb5f3c> ;
