        hg:ConditionAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Invitation to Samyak Mahādāna"@en ;
    dcterms:description "This copper plate inscription documents Jitāja Bhāro, a Tulādhara from Asana, Kathmandu, inviting the Dipaṅkara Buddha statue of thebāhāḥto take part in theSamyak Mahādāna, a grand alms-giving ceremony hosted during the reign of King Sadāśiva Malla. The invitation requested the participation of thebāhāḥ’sthapāḥju(seniormost member) and other members, along with the ornaments, parasol (chatra), and flag (dhvaja) of the Dipaṅkara statue. However, the inscription does not clarify whether both of thebāhāḥ’s two Dipaṅkara statues were invited or just one."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/bca05125-f950-410b-ae42-6f5cf2303dfc> ;
    rdfs:comment "This copper plate inscription documents Jitāja Bhāro, a Tulādhara from Asana, Kathmandu, inviting the Dipaṅkara Buddha statue of thebāhāḥto take part in theSamyak Mahādāna, a grand alms-giving ceremony hosted during the reign of King Sadāśiva Malla. The invitation requested the participation of thebāhāḥ’sthapāḥju(seniormost member) and other members, along with the ornaments, parasol (chatra), and flag (dhvaja) of the Dipaṅkara statue. However, the inscription does not clarify whether both of thebāhāḥ’s two Dipaṅkara statues were invited or just one."@en ;
