    rdfs:label "Renovation"@en ;
    dcterms:description "During the reign of King Jitāmitra Malla, Daṇḍapāṇi Vajrācārya undertook renovation of the Bāhāḥ'skvāḥpāḥchẽ. His contributions included installing a gilded parasol on the finial and erecting a pillar bearing his own statue. His wife Ratnamaṇi, son Manamohanasiṃ Vajrācārya, and other family members also supported the renovation efforts."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/bca05125-f950-410b-ae42-6f5cf2303dfc> ;
