<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/bcb297bf-c0dc-4a2b-96f3-f4a8228683c9_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Construction of the Phalcā?"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Most of the letters on the inscription installed at the Phalcā are unreadable. Therefore, it is unclear when the Phalcā was first constructed. The script and language of the inscription suggest that the Phalcā was constructed during the Śāha period. The term ‘divaṃgata’, which means ‘the late’, is legible in the inscription. Probably, Putalināni, Bhājudeva, Jayalachimi, Lādhāmuni, and Gyānavira–the names featured in the inscription–constructed the Phalcā in memory of a deceased member of their family."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/bcb297bf-c0dc-4a2b-96f3-f4a8228683c9> ;
    rdfs:comment "Most of the letters on the inscription installed at the Phalcā are unreadable. Therefore, it is unclear when the Phalcā was first constructed. The script and language of the inscription suggest that the Phalcā was constructed during the Śāha period. The term ‘divaṃgata’, which means ‘the late’, is legible in the inscription. Probably, Putalināni, Bhājudeva, Jayalachimi, Lādhāmuni, and Gyānavira–the names featured in the inscription–constructed the Phalcā in memory of a deceased member of their family."@en ;
