<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/bcb98cfb-bc5a-44a0-b497-d6b87ac4e77d_2> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Endowment of lands"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Devamuni of Bāḍegāũ donated one-third of a plot of land located in Dhvapagāma to set up a trust to fund a fire oblation in front of thecaityaon the full moon day of Māgha, along with a sacrifice of a duck to Gaṇeśa, and to perform asinhaḥpūjā(a worship involving vermillion powder) at the shrine of the esoteric deity. A balconied tower (phucā) was also added to the esoteric shrine on the same occasion. Viśvambhara Bhāro of Cākra Bāhāra was thepramānaof the area when these works were carried out."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/bcb98cfb-bc5a-44a0-b497-d6b87ac4e77d> ;
    rdfs:comment "Devamuni of Bāḍegāũ donated one-third of a plot of land located in Dhvapagāma to set up a trust to fund a fire oblation in front of thecaityaon the full moon day of Māgha, along with a sacrifice of a duck to Gaṇeśa, and to perform asinhaḥpūjā(a worship involving vermillion powder) at the shrine of the esoteric deity. A balconied tower (phucā) was also added to the esoteric shrine on the same occasion. Viśvambhara Bhāro of Cākra Bāhāra was thepramānaof the area when these works were carried out."@en ;
