<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/bddc9722-2a25-48d6-a849-f9d0ae2b3f26_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:TransferOfCustody ;
    rdfs:label "Renovation of phalcā"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Purṇasiṃha Bhāro, Basundharā Mayī, and Dhanadeva Bhāro from the Jelā ṭola were instrumental in the renovation of one of the phalcās within the premises of the pīṭha. Additionally, Basundharā endowed land at a location known as Ithari to observe the anniversary ritual (varṣavarddhana) of the phalcā. However, it is currently unclear whether the inscription found in the Maheśvarī Mandira (BKT0300) is directly related to these activities or if it pertains to another aspect of the site's history."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/bddc9722-2a25-48d6-a849-f9d0ae2b3f26> ;
    rdfs:comment "Purṇasiṃha Bhāro, Basundharā Mayī, and Dhanadeva Bhāro from the Jelā ṭola were instrumental in the renovation of one of the phalcās within the premises of the pīṭha. Additionally, Basundharā endowed land at a location known as Ithari to observe the anniversary ritual (varṣavarddhana) of the phalcā. However, it is currently unclear whether the inscription found in the Maheśvarī Mandira (BKT0300) is directly related to these activities or if it pertains to another aspect of the site's history."@en ;
