<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/befb8373-194a-4bc4-9fa5-7a736ab73196_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Initial construction"@en ;
    dcterms:description "King Jitamitra Malla, during the tenure of Prime Minister Bhāgirāma, constructedHiticuka—a hiti (stone water spout) with a fine flow of water, along with a beautiful pond—to please his tutelary deity (iṣṭadevatā). He also built an arched gateway with a door for the Hiti. Above the arch, atoraṇa(decorative tympanum) was placed, and inside the gateway golden images were installed. Around the same time, Tuthacuka (a square with a well), Lakṣmīvilāsa Chowk, Dumāju Chowk, and Kisigara (an elephant stable) were also built."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/befb8373-194a-4bc4-9fa5-7a736ab73196> ;
    rdfs:comment "King Jitamitra Malla, during the tenure of Prime Minister Bhāgirāma, constructedHiticuka—a hiti (stone water spout) with a fine flow of water, along with a beautiful pond—to please his tutelary deity (iṣṭadevatā). He also built an arched gateway with a door for the Hiti. Above the arch, atoraṇa(decorative tympanum) was placed, and inside the gateway golden images were installed. Around the same time, Tuthacuka (a square with a well), Lakṣmīvilāsa Chowk, Dumāju Chowk, and Kisigara (an elephant stable) were also built."@en ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/agent/antigravity_agent> ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/activity/heritagegraph_kg_construction> ;
    hg:eventIndex 0 ;
    hg:extractionMethod "source_table" ;
    hg:isEventOf <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/befb8373-194a-4bc4-9fa5-7a736ab73196> .

<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/befb8373-194a-4bc4-9fa5-7a736ab73196_1> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:TransferOfCustody ;
    rdfs:label "Endowment of lands"@en ;
    dcterms:description "A few months after the construction of the Hiti, King Jitamitra Malla endowed 10ropaniof land as aguthifor the upkeep of the Hitiand for the worship of Taleju. The inscription records that the revenue from this land was to be used every year on the 3rd day of bright fortnight of Vaiśākha (Akṣaya Tṛtīyā) to perform theVarṣavardhana Pūjā(annual ritual) of the Hiti, as well as for various other ritual observances dedicated to Taleju. For this purpose, one Rājopādhyāya Brahmin, along with Candraśekhara Rāya and Bhāyarāma Karmācārya of the Vidyāpīṭha, were appointed as theguṭhī-members. As witnesses to this deed, the king’s brother Ugra Malla, his son Bhūpatindra Malla, and Prime Minister Bhāgirama Pradhānāṅga were named."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/befb8373-194a-4bc4-9fa5-7a736ab73196> ;
    rdfs:comment "A few months after the construction of the Hiti, King Jitamitra Malla endowed 10ropaniof land as aguthifor the upkeep of the Hitiand for the worship of Taleju. The inscription records that the revenue from this land was to be used every year on the 3rd day of bright fortnight of Vaiśākha (Akṣaya Tṛtīyā) to perform theVarṣavardhana Pūjā(annual ritual) of the Hiti, as well as for various other ritual observances dedicated to Taleju. For this purpose, one Rājopādhyāya Brahmin, along with Candraśekhara Rāya and Bhāyarāma Karmācārya of the Vidyāpīṭha, were appointed as theguṭhī-members. As witnesses to this deed, the king’s brother Ugra Malla, his son Bhūpatindra Malla, and Prime Minister Bhāgirama Pradhānāṅga were named."@en ;
