<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/c13af8a3-4e4b-438f-9dd5-2ad28cf0ea42_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Decreasing of revenue"@en ;
    dcterms:description "This 614 CE Licchavi inscription is not directly related to the caitya, but it records that King Aṃśuvarmā remitted themalla kara(a form of state tax) that had been levied upon the inhabitants of Ahiduṃkoṭṭa-grāma—present-day Bālūvagā̃—where theRājavihārawas located."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/c13af8a3-4e4b-438f-9dd5-2ad28cf0ea42> ;
    rdfs:comment "This 614 CE Licchavi inscription is not directly related to the caitya, but it records that King Aṃśuvarmā remitted themalla kara(a form of state tax) that had been levied upon the inhabitants of Ahiduṃkoṭṭa-grāma—present-day Bālūvagā̃—where theRājavihārawas located."@en ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/agent/antigravity_agent> ;
