<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/c13af8a3-4e4b-438f-9dd5-2ad28cf0ea42_1> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Enshrinement ;
    rdfs:label "Construction of a temple"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The local residents of Bālūvagāṃ hold a long-standing belief that the ancient image of Mahākāla once enshrined at this site was transferred to Tundikhel by King Pratāpa Malla. On the basis of this local tradition, the aniconic stone formerly worshipped as Mahākāla was replaced in 2016 CE by a new anthropomorphic image, and a two-storied temple was constructed over it."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/c13af8a3-4e4b-438f-9dd5-2ad28cf0ea42> ;
    rdfs:comment "The local residents of Bālūvagāṃ hold a long-standing belief that the ancient image of Mahākāla once enshrined at this site was transferred to Tundikhel by King Pratāpa Malla. On the basis of this local tradition, the aniconic stone formerly worshipped as Mahākāla was replaced in 2016 CE by a new anthropomorphic image, and a two-storied temple was constructed over it."@en ;
