<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/c317a5dd-be86-4098-9654-5f667d35a368_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Renovation of the Hiti"@en ;
    dcterms:description "After the Hiti’s water source failed and remained dry for about twenty to twenty-five years, Queen Gambhīrakumārīdevī, the youngest wife of Rana Prime Minister Juddha Śamaśera, funded its restoration. The work involved repairing the structure, restoring the water source and supply channel, and embedding marker stones along the route to trace future blockages. One marker was placed on the main road from Guita ṭola’s Guita Bahi to Bh̃uḍe Gaṇeśasthana, another twenty-five feet north, and additional drainage channels (maṃgāla) were installed at one-hundred-foot intervals to reestablish both the source and outlet."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/c317a5dd-be86-4098-9654-5f667d35a368> ;
    rdfs:comment "After the Hiti’s water source failed and remained dry for about twenty to twenty-five years, Queen Gambhīrakumārīdevī, the youngest wife of Rana Prime Minister Juddha Śamaśera, funded its restoration. The work involved repairing the structure, restoring the water source and supply channel, and embedding marker stones along the route to trace future blockages. One marker was placed on the main road from Guita ṭola’s Guita Bahi to Bh̃uḍe Gaṇeśasthana, another twenty-five feet north, and additional drainage channels (maṃgāla) were installed at one-hundred-foot intervals to reestablish both the source and outlet."@en ;
