<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/c32183e8-9922-48ad-89f0-2e6ac93ecc30_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "King's proclamation"@en ;
    dcterms:description "This stone inscription from MS 39, affixed to the wall in front of the Jaḥdhuṃ near the main outer gate of Paśupati (but unrelated to the present monument, the Dakṣiṇāmūrti Jaḥdhuṃ), records a royal decree issued by King Aṃśuvarmā. The inscription states that the king entrusted the administrative authority over three temples—Śūrabhogeśvara, founded by his sister Bhogadevī; Laḍitamaheśvara, founded by his niece Bhāgya Devī; and Dakṣiṇeśvara, founded by the ancestor of his niece’s lineage—to the Pāñcālikas."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/c32183e8-9922-48ad-89f0-2e6ac93ecc30> ;
    rdfs:comment "This stone inscription from MS 39, affixed to the wall in front of the Jaḥdhuṃ near the main outer gate of Paśupati (but unrelated to the present monument, the Dakṣiṇāmūrti Jaḥdhuṃ), records a royal decree issued by King Aṃśuvarmā. The inscription states that the king entrusted the administrative authority over three temples—Śūrabhogeśvara, founded by his sister Bhogadevī; Laḍitamaheśvara, founded by his niece Bhāgya Devī; and Dakṣiṇeśvara, founded by the ancestor of his niece’s lineage—to the Pāñcālikas."@en ;
