<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/c32183e8-9922-48ad-89f0-2e6ac93ecc30_1> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Initial construction of the Jaḥdhuṃ"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Dated to 1317 CE (NS 437), the inscription attests to the joint rule (saṃyuktaśāsana) of Ānandadeva and Rudra Malla, distinguished by the use of threeśrīsfor Ānandadeva and two for Rudra Malla. It records that the Jaḥdhuṃ was commissioned by a royal physician (rājavaidya) on behalf of a patron for the spiritual benefit of his ancestors. The text concludes by proclaiming the merit of both offering and drinking water."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/c32183e8-9922-48ad-89f0-2e6ac93ecc30> ;
    rdfs:comment "Dated to 1317 CE (NS 437), the inscription attests to the joint rule (saṃyuktaśāsana) of Ānandadeva and Rudra Malla, distinguished by the use of threeśrīsfor Ānandadeva and two for Rudra Malla. It records that the Jaḥdhuṃ was commissioned by a royal physician (rājavaidya) on behalf of a patron for the spiritual benefit of his ancestors. The text concludes by proclaiming the merit of both offering and drinking water."@en ;
