<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/c501bcf1-1a77-4259-99b9-f5cb452c8f82_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Construction of a Bhuvaneśvarī Shrine"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Bāghanasiṃha (Bāghanarasiṃha Śākya) of the Gautamagotra, a member of the Śākya lineage residing in the southwest corner of Hiranyavarṇa Mahāvihāra, Kwāḥ Bahāḥ, undertook the renovation of the dilapidated Lokākīrti Mahāvihāra at Naḥ Bahī (LAL0880). As part of this project, he constructed a three-tiered stone staircase in front of thebahī, built the Bhvaneśvara shrine, and performed asahasrāhuti yajña(fire offering with a thousand oblations). He was assisted in these activities by his wife Hel Thakuṃ, his sons Bāhadursiṃha and Lakṣmīnārasiṃha, his nephew Kubersiṃha, and his grandsons Harṣanārasiṃha, Byasanārasiṃha, Harṣamānasiṃha, Ratnanārasiṃha, and Samyakanārasiṃha, as well as other family members."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/c501bcf1-1a77-4259-99b9-f5cb452c8f82> ;
    rdfs:comment "Bāghanasiṃha (Bāghanarasiṃha Śākya) of the Gautamagotra, a member of the Śākya lineage residing in the southwest corner of Hiranyavarṇa Mahāvihāra, Kwāḥ Bahāḥ, undertook the renovation of the dilapidated Lokākīrti Mahāvihāra at Naḥ Bahī (LAL0880). As part of this project, he constructed a three-tiered stone staircase in front of thebahī, built the Bhvaneśvara shrine, and performed asahasrāhuti yajña(fire offering with a thousand oblations). He was assisted in these activities by his wife Hel Thakuṃ, his sons Bāhadursiṃha and Lakṣmīnārasiṃha, his nephew Kubersiṃha, and his grandsons Harṣanārasiṃha, Byasanārasiṃha, Harṣamānasiṃha, Ratnanārasiṃha, and Samyakanārasiṃha, as well as other family members."@en ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/agent/antigravity_agent> ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/activity/heritagegraph_kg_construction> ;
