<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/c501bcf1-1a77-4259-99b9-f5cb452c8f82_1> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:RitualEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Organizing annual worship"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The worship of the tenMahāvidyāgoddesses, which had been initiated at Bagalāmukhī in VS 2025 (1968 CE), was later discontinued for various reasons. In VS 2074 (2017 CE), a rotational system was introduced in which the ten neighborhoods (ṭola) housing theMahāvidyāshrines would take turns organizing the annual worship. That year, Pūlchok’s Tārā/Khadvayoginī (LAL0630) shrine hosted the festival, followed the next year by Naḥ Bahī Ṭola, where Bhuvaneśvarī is located."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/c501bcf1-1a77-4259-99b9-f5cb452c8f82> ;
    rdfs:comment "The worship of the tenMahāvidyāgoddesses, which had been initiated at Bagalāmukhī in VS 2025 (1968 CE), was later discontinued for various reasons. In VS 2074 (2017 CE), a rotational system was introduced in which the ten neighborhoods (ṭola) housing theMahāvidyāshrines would take turns organizing the annual worship. That year, Pūlchok’s Tārā/Khadvayoginī (LAL0630) shrine hosted the festival, followed the next year by Naḥ Bahī Ṭola, where Bhuvaneśvarī is located."@en ;
