<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/c5819d99-b25f-46a9-93d5-6ade84d2cc16_3> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Offering toraṇa (BKT0210-003)"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Harihara (text: Halihara), resident of the Yachẽ Ṭola, offered atoraṇawith the carvings of the scene ofMāraVijaya, i.e., the victory over Māra, a malignant celestial king who is known for his failed attempt to disrupt the meditation of Prince Siddhartha while he was on the verge of attaining the enlightenment to become the Buddha. He also offered a window on the same occasion. However, it is unclear which window it was."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/c5819d99-b25f-46a9-93d5-6ade84d2cc16> ;
    rdfs:comment "Harihara (text: Halihara), resident of the Yachẽ Ṭola, offered atoraṇawith the carvings of the scene ofMāraVijaya, i.e., the victory over Māra, a malignant celestial king who is known for his failed attempt to disrupt the meditation of Prince Siddhartha while he was on the verge of attaining the enlightenment to become the Buddha. He also offered a window on the same occasion. However, it is unclear which window it was."@en ;
