<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/c65d730c-e80b-11e9-b125-0242ac130002_2> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Enshrinement ;
    rdfs:label "Construction of the Priukhā temple at Aśoka Stūpa"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Brahmacarya Bhikṣu Cintāmaṇi of Yampi Vihāra, Rām Bhāro of Konimha and otherguṭhīmembers made the Priukhā temple at the Aśoka Stūpaduring the reign of King Yoganarendra Malla. It is possible that, at that time, the Buddha statues were enshrined in the niches of thestūpa,and that those niches are addressed as the Stūpa temple in the inscription."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/c65d730c-e80b-11e9-b125-0242ac130002> ;
    rdfs:comment "Brahmacarya Bhikṣu Cintāmaṇi of Yampi Vihāra, Rām Bhāro of Konimha and otherguṭhīmembers made the Priukhā temple at the Aśoka Stūpaduring the reign of King Yoganarendra Malla. It is possible that, at that time, the Buddha statues were enshrined in the niches of thestūpa,and that those niches are addressed as the Stūpa temple in the inscription."@en ;
