<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/c6a2761c-ee3a-48c6-ab37-10c5bb775af3_2> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Paving with floor tiles"@en ;
    dcterms:description "A guild dedicated to chanting Buddhist hymns in Thecva paved the open space in front of the Brahmāyaṇī temple and the area around the Kvaylāchicaityawith floor tiles. The guild was led by Kṛṣṇadeva at the time with Viśvahari, Sūrjjarāma, Raghu, Siddhirāma, and others involved as members. The inscription recording this event bears a carving of acaityaon its upper portion. Thecaityamentioned in the inscription is Kvaylāchi Cībhāḥ (THC0130)."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/c6a2761c-ee3a-48c6-ab37-10c5bb775af3> ;
    rdfs:comment "A guild dedicated to chanting Buddhist hymns in Thecva paved the open space in front of the Brahmāyaṇī temple and the area around the Kvaylāchicaityawith floor tiles. The guild was led by Kṛṣṇadeva at the time with Viśvahari, Sūrjjarāma, Raghu, Siddhirāma, and others involved as members. The inscription recording this event bears a carving of acaityaon its upper portion. Thecaityamentioned in the inscription is Kvaylāchi Cībhāḥ (THC0130)."@en ;
