<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/c6ce5cc1-ed5f-468a-90e7-4afe5d723128_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Demolition of the phalcā"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Some elderly locals recall that thephalcāwas in a dismal state of disrepair, deemed as visual pollution in 1972 CE, just as King Vīrendra was scheduled to pass through with a foreign dignitary en route to Godāvarī, a town in southeastern Lalitpur. Consequently, it was dismantled."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/c6ce5cc1-ed5f-468a-90e7-4afe5d723128> ;
    rdfs:comment "Some elderly locals recall that thephalcāwas in a dismal state of disrepair, deemed as visual pollution in 1972 CE, just as King Vīrendra was scheduled to pass through with a foreign dignitary en route to Godāvarī, a town in southeastern Lalitpur. Consequently, it was dismantled."@en ;
