<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/c76b8185-0984-4605-a47f-4b49422805a5_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Enshrinement ;
    rdfs:label "Construction of the hiti"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Jāminī Mayī, a resident of Tupulāchi, not only commissioned the water fountain but also installed the sacred images of Umāmaheśvara and Viśveśvara Mahādeva. An inscription from the time of thehiti’s construction issues a warning that any act of desecration or damage would invite the wrath of Umāmaheśvara, Viśveśvara, and Cāmuṇḍādevī."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/c76b8185-0984-4605-a47f-4b49422805a5> ;
    rdfs:comment "Jāminī Mayī, a resident of Tupulāchi, not only commissioned the water fountain but also installed the sacred images of Umāmaheśvara and Viśveśvara Mahādeva. An inscription from the time of thehiti’s construction issues a warning that any act of desecration or damage would invite the wrath of Umāmaheśvara, Viśveśvara, and Cāmuṇḍādevī."@en ;
