<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/c76fb177-1c2d-4e05-9bb8-3a0764a5abcd_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Construction of a caitya"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Bhājunarasiṃha, a member of the Śākya lineage of Dyaḥnanī (LAL2650), established acaityaat Taḥdhananī. With achepuon itsharmikā, thiscaityafeatures a unique form, style, and craftsmanship. Unlike the more commoncaityas found in the Valley, this one (object no. LAL2651-006) exhibits a distinct appearance. The design reflects an experimental approach by the artist of that period."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/c76fb177-1c2d-4e05-9bb8-3a0764a5abcd> ;
    rdfs:comment "Bhājunarasiṃha, a member of the Śākya lineage of Dyaḥnanī (LAL2650), established acaityaat Taḥdhananī. With achepuon itsharmikā, thiscaityafeatures a unique form, style, and craftsmanship. Unlike the more commoncaityas found in the Valley, this one (object no. LAL2651-006) exhibits a distinct appearance. The design reflects an experimental approach by the artist of that period."@en ;
