    rdfs:label "Addition of a bell"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Siṃharāja of the Śākya lineage and his wife Aṣṭamāyā offered a bell with a stone pedestal on the northern side of thepīṭha. The chain of this bell is adorned with a distinctive leaf-vine design that is rarely seen elsewhere. During the Rāṇā period, various innovations in metalwork emerged in Patan—such as rows of stylized leaves added totoraṇas of courtyards, altered lion figures, and the uniquedalūof the Kṛṣṇa Mandira. Similar innovation can also be observed on the upper part of this bell."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/c76fb177-1c2d-4e05-9bb8-3a0764a5abcd> ;
    rdfs:comment "Siṃharāja of the Śākya lineage and his wife Aṣṭamāyā offered a bell with a stone pedestal on the northern side of thepīṭha. The chain of this bell is adorned with a distinctive leaf-vine design that is rarely seen elsewhere. During the Rāṇā period, various innovations in metalwork emerged in Patan—such as rows of stylized leaves added totoraṇas of courtyards, altered lion figures, and the uniquedalūof the Kṛṣṇa Mandira. Similar innovation can also be observed on the upper part of this bell."@en ;
