<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/c88cdb20-cc04-4918-89fa-9e278e8aa5fd_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Consecration ;
    rdfs:label "Consecration of Buddha statue (Construction of Bāhāḥ)"@en ;
    dcterms:description "As mentioned above in ‘description’ both Pruscha (1975, 32 [K-80]) and Locke (1985, p. 348) mention, by referring to a now-missing inscription on the pedestal of the buddha statue in the sanctum, that the statue was consecrated by a Śākya monk Cakrapati Deva. However, the former mentions the year as 1754 CE and latter NS 865 (i.e., 1745 CE). Though Locke may have misread the date or Pruscha may have converted the year given in the Nepal Samvat to Common Era incorrectly, we use Locke’s dating for documentation because he has mentioned the date in the local era (Nepal Samvat)."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/c88cdb20-cc04-4918-89fa-9e278e8aa5fd> ;
    rdfs:comment "As mentioned above in ‘description’ both Pruscha (1975, 32 [K-80]) and Locke (1985, p. 348) mention, by referring to a now-missing inscription on the pedestal of the buddha statue in the sanctum, that the statue was consecrated by a Śākya monk Cakrapati Deva. However, the former mentions the year as 1754 CE and latter NS 865 (i.e., 1745 CE). Though Locke may have misread the date or Pruscha may have converted the year given in the Nepal Samvat to Common Era incorrectly, we use Locke’s dating for documentation because he has mentioned the date in the local era (Nepal Samvat)."@en ;
