<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/c8aa02e8-8f4e-45a2-8830-558edb70c685_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Renovation and transformation: rebuilding the temple"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The Gaṇeśa Mandira, once aśikhara-style temple, underwent a significant makeover. Its evolution took place during the broader restoration efforts that preceded the SAARC summit in Kathmandu in 1987 CE (VS 2044). Divya Pradhāna, associated with the Kulu Cuka at Makhana Ṭola, played an important role by offering financial support for the temple's reconstruction. The exact reconstruction date may have faded from memory, but locals recall the earlier temple as a simpleśikhara-style structure."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/c8aa02e8-8f4e-45a2-8830-558edb70c685> ;
    rdfs:comment "The Gaṇeśa Mandira, once aśikhara-style temple, underwent a significant makeover. Its evolution took place during the broader restoration efforts that preceded the SAARC summit in Kathmandu in 1987 CE (VS 2044). Divya Pradhāna, associated with the Kulu Cuka at Makhana Ṭola, played an important role by offering financial support for the temple's reconstruction. The exact reconstruction date may have faded from memory, but locals recall the earlier temple as a simpleśikhara-style structure."@en ;
