<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/ca2cb4c6-e6b6-11e9-b125-0242ac130002_1> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Unidentified"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Attached to the western plinth of the Hiṭī is an inscription of Licchavi King Jayadeva II (r.713-733).Vajrācārya(2030, 539-42) has read this inscription. The inscription mentions Narāyaṇa as a lineage deity. It is possible that the image of Narāyaṇa was also established close to the inscription. The Hiṭī, thus named Nārāyaṇahiṭī, lated called as Nāya Hiṭī (Khanal2068, 225). It is 131cm tall and has 50cm breadth."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/ca2cb4c6-e6b6-11e9-b125-0242ac130002> ;
    rdfs:comment "Attached to the western plinth of the Hiṭī is an inscription of Licchavi King Jayadeva II (r.713-733).Vajrācārya(2030, 539-42) has read this inscription. The inscription mentions Narāyaṇa as a lineage deity. It is possible that the image of Narāyaṇa was also established close to the inscription. The Hiṭī, thus named Nārāyaṇahiṭī, lated called as Nāya Hiṭī (Khanal2068, 225). It is 131cm tall and has 50cm breadth."@en ;
