<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/cb193cf8-529c-4656-9468-05af05cdcdc5_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Initial construction"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Dhana Mānāndhara and his wife Tuyudhari and their other family members jointly constructed the Caitya and made arrangements for a regular income to sponsor the annual rituals here. A group of five Mānandharas (Tavadhika, Bhāgivṃta, Rachimi Nārā and Dharma Nārā) are mentioned as ‘caretakers’ of the Catiya. For the inscription seeKIR4027(KIR4027_I_001)."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/cb193cf8-529c-4656-9468-05af05cdcdc5> ;
    rdfs:comment "Dhana Mānāndhara and his wife Tuyudhari and their other family members jointly constructed the Caitya and made arrangements for a regular income to sponsor the annual rituals here. A group of five Mānandharas (Tavadhika, Bhāgivṃta, Rachimi Nārā and Dharma Nārā) are mentioned as ‘caretakers’ of the Catiya. For the inscription seeKIR4027(KIR4027_I_001)."@en ;
