<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/cd98e62e-a9d9-43b9-91a4-7c8100ce0d8a_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:TransferOfCustody ;
    rdfs:label "Renovation of the caitya"@en ;
    dcterms:description "During the reign of King Tribhuvana, Rājamānasiṃha (text: Lājamāṃsī) and his wife Āsāthakuṃ of Koṣāchẽ Nani in Thecva undertook restoration work on thecaitya. The donor couple also laid the surrounding area with stones on the occasion. Additionally, they established a land endowment and a non-expendable fund of Rs. 200 to support its upkeep. The income generated from the land endowment and interest from the fund was designated for the regular maintenance of thecaitya. It was also stipulated that lamps should be lit at thecaityaon the full moon day of Āśvina. Ten trustees were appointed to oversee these arrangements and were provided with meals on the full moon day of Āśvina and the following day."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/cd98e62e-a9d9-43b9-91a4-7c8100ce0d8a> ;
    rdfs:comment "During the reign of King Tribhuvana, Rājamānasiṃha (text: Lājamāṃsī) and his wife Āsāthakuṃ of Koṣāchẽ Nani in Thecva undertook restoration work on thecaitya. The donor couple also laid the surrounding area with stones on the occasion. Additionally, they established a land endowment and a non-expendable fund of Rs. 200 to support its upkeep. The income generated from the land endowment and interest from the fund was designated for the regular maintenance of thecaitya. It was also stipulated that lamps should be lit at thecaityaon the full moon day of Āśvina. Ten trustees were appointed to oversee these arrangements and were provided with meals on the full moon day of Āśvina and the following day."@en ;
