        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Offering of a lion (siṃha) and a banner (dhvaja)"@en ;
    dcterms:description "According to an inscription from the reign of King Nṛpendra Malla, son of King Pratāpa Malla, a certain Vīrabhadrafrom Kāntipura (Kathmandu) had offered a lion (siṃha) and a banner (dhvaja) to the goddess. However, as part of the inscription is damaged and the letters are worn, the exact date inscribed cannot be determined."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/cdf3de81-c5a5-4f35-85cc-d61ecaacdf9d> ;
