<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/d145d273-016e-4866-93cf-a4468db44435_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Construction of the Jaḥdhuṃ"@en ;
    dcterms:description "With devotion to their tutelary deity, two brothers, Śivakṛṣṇa Bhāro and Bhima Bhāro, living in Khaṇḍachuka within Yaṃparācha ṭola in Bhaktapur, built theJaḥdhuṃtogether. Local Pañcas were given the responsibility for its maintenance. In this inscription, theJaḥdhuṃis referred to asJaradhārā, meaning a water source or spout. The inscription records the address of those who established the Jaḥdhuṃ as Yaṃparācha ṭola. Over time, the pronunciation of Yaṃparācha ṭolā gradually changed, leading to the current name Jelā̃ ṭolā."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/d145d273-016e-4866-93cf-a4468db44435> ;
    rdfs:comment "With devotion to their tutelary deity, two brothers, Śivakṛṣṇa Bhāro and Bhima Bhāro, living in Khaṇḍachuka within Yaṃparācha ṭola in Bhaktapur, built theJaḥdhuṃtogether. Local Pañcas were given the responsibility for its maintenance. In this inscription, theJaḥdhuṃis referred to asJaradhārā, meaning a water source or spout. The inscription records the address of those who established the Jaḥdhuṃ as Yaṃparācha ṭola. Over time, the pronunciation of Yaṃparācha ṭolā gradually changed, leading to the current name Jelā̃ ṭolā."@en ;
