<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/d1b6c182-d63d-4673-91f1-e59d4ed98a32_4> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Reconstruction of the temple"@en ;
    dcterms:description "As the temple is located adjacent to a busy road, vehicles passing by would often collide with its eastern roof. Once, a large vehicle collided and completely destroyed the eastern roof. The locals collectively managed the finances and reconstructed the temple. The temple was reconstructed into a two-tiered structure, conforming to its original appearance prior to the 1934 earthquakes. However, the eastern and western sides of the temple were open in the previous construction, but were walled in the reconstruction."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/d1b6c182-d63d-4673-91f1-e59d4ed98a32> ;
    rdfs:comment "As the temple is located adjacent to a busy road, vehicles passing by would often collide with its eastern roof. Once, a large vehicle collided and completely destroyed the eastern roof. The locals collectively managed the finances and reconstructed the temple. The temple was reconstructed into a two-tiered structure, conforming to its original appearance prior to the 1934 earthquakes. However, the eastern and western sides of the temple were open in the previous construction, but were walled in the reconstruction."@en ;
