<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/d30593b5-c63b-47d9-90a0-b101b2ebac77_13> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Gilding objects with gold"@en ;
    dcterms:description "A donor of the Tulādhara caste from Asana offers two statues to the temple and gilds the quarter-round design (nāḥgvaḥ) and frill pattern designs of the temple during the reign of King Prithvī Vikrama Śāha (r. 1881-1911 CE). The full name of the donor and the year of the donation cannot be traced, as a portion of the inscription is covered by the temple’storaṇa. Only the first two digits of the year are visible. The event took place between 1881-1911 CE."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/d30593b5-c63b-47d9-90a0-b101b2ebac77> ;
    rdfs:comment "A donor of the Tulādhara caste from Asana offers two statues to the temple and gilds the quarter-round design (nāḥgvaḥ) and frill pattern designs of the temple during the reign of King Prithvī Vikrama Śāha (r. 1881-1911 CE). The full name of the donor and the year of the donation cannot be traced, as a portion of the inscription is covered by the temple’storaṇa. Only the first two digits of the year are visible. The event took place between 1881-1911 CE."@en ;
