<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/d509cc77-2c10-48fb-a4a4-7b94d4a6af04_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Consecration ;
    rdfs:label "Dharmadatta's vow to build a temple"@en ;
    dcterms:description "As mentioned in the inscription on the site, Dharmadatta Pauḍela (the son of Jayanārāyaṇa, grandson of Lakṣmaṇa, and great-grandson of Harinārāyaṇa Pauḍela), made a ritual vow (saṅkalpa) to consecrate aśivaliṅgaat Phirkyāpa on the banks of the Trishuli river in Devīghāṭa. This vow was made while he was taken to the Āryaghāṭa cremation ground at Paśupati during his final days, after falling gravely ill, with the aim of attaining Śivaloka (the world of Śiva) after his death. Unfortunately, he was unable to fulfill his vow and passed away in Āryaghāṭa.The inscription is edited in D. Vajrācārya and Ṭ. Śreṣṭha VS 2032, second part, pp. 60-64, and their edition reads as follows:"@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/d509cc77-2c10-48fb-a4a4-7b94d4a6af04> ;
    rdfs:comment "As mentioned in the inscription on the site, Dharmadatta Pauḍela (the son of Jayanārāyaṇa, grandson of Lakṣmaṇa, and great-grandson of Harinārāyaṇa Pauḍela), made a ritual vow (saṅkalpa) to consecrate aśivaliṅgaat Phirkyāpa on the banks of the Trishuli river in Devīghāṭa. This vow was made while he was taken to the Āryaghāṭa cremation ground at Paśupati during his final days, after falling gravely ill, with the aim of attaining Śivaloka (the world of Śiva) after his death. Unfortunately, he was unable to fulfill his vow and passed away in Āryaghāṭa.The inscription is edited in D. Vajrācārya and Ṭ. Śreṣṭha VS 2032, second part, pp. 60-64, and their edition reads as follows:"@en ;
