<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/d52dcb5c-6f3b-4b23-86d0-de4e40dddda0_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Temple and rest house construction"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Lakṣmīdevī, the third concubine of King Raṇabahādura Śāha, undertook the initiative to build the temple. Alongside the temple, she also oversaw the construction of thecaugharā sataḥ, the cluster of rest houses encircling the temple. Lakṣmīdevī hailed from the lineage of Gaṇeśadatta Bauḍīdvā, a notable figure from the Garmiñā village in Patna, India."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/d52dcb5c-6f3b-4b23-86d0-de4e40dddda0> ;
    rdfs:comment "Lakṣmīdevī, the third concubine of King Raṇabahādura Śāha, undertook the initiative to build the temple. Alongside the temple, she also oversaw the construction of thecaugharā sataḥ, the cluster of rest houses encircling the temple. Lakṣmīdevī hailed from the lineage of Gaṇeśadatta Bauḍīdvā, a notable figure from the Garmiñā village in Patna, India."@en ;
