<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/d6327d2c-6457-4406-89aa-4ea448ce22e3_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Monument disassembly and transformation"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Around the year 2005 CE, the Khanāla family disassembled the temple structure and erected a concrete square room on the site. Asserting ancestral land rights, this action resulted in the incorporation of the temple grounds into their private property. Additionally, the family placed the temple's statues within the confines of the newly constructed concrete room."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/d6327d2c-6457-4406-89aa-4ea448ce22e3> ;
    rdfs:comment "Around the year 2005 CE, the Khanāla family disassembled the temple structure and erected a concrete square room on the site. Asserting ancestral land rights, this action resulted in the incorporation of the temple grounds into their private property. Additionally, the family placed the temple's statues within the confines of the newly constructed concrete room."@en ;
