<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/d7c4e686-d20c-4141-9a25-dfc5d3ccab45_2> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Consecration ;
    rdfs:label "Reconstruction of the Bāhāḥ"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Once people had forgotten that there was a Bahāḥ and used it as a female latrine. Harṣa Bahādur Śākya from Oku Bāhāḥ rebuilt it and developed it as a Theravāda Vihāra for nuns. On that occasion he had consecrated adharmadhātujinālya caiyaat the Bāhāḥ courtyard."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/d7c4e686-d20c-4141-9a25-dfc5d3ccab45> ;
