<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/d7e3c28c-e1ab-430b-9b2d-9b69475905a9_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:TransferOfCustody ;
    rdfs:label "Initial construction"@en ;
    dcterms:description "There is no inscription recording the initial phase of construction. The inscription transferred to the Phalcā dates back to 1889 CE (1009 NS) records the restoration of the phalcā carried out by the son of Amitanārā (Amita Nārāyaṇa) and Mayajumunī. The inscription also reveals that Kvāṭhanāyaka Āsāmadu Bhāro initiated its construction."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/d7e3c28c-e1ab-430b-9b2d-9b69475905a9> ;
    rdfs:comment "There is no inscription recording the initial phase of construction. The inscription transferred to the Phalcā dates back to 1889 CE (1009 NS) records the restoration of the phalcā carried out by the son of Amitanārā (Amita Nārāyaṇa) and Mayajumunī. The inscription also reveals that Kvāṭhanāyaka Āsāmadu Bhāro initiated its construction."@en ;
