<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/d8d8d8e4-76ea-4db0-a222-6527d4e0eda3_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Initial construction"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Numerous medieval inscriptions refer to the completion of temple construction through a ritual known as\"Suvarṇa Kalaśa Dhvajārohaṇa\"(raising of a golden finial) or\"Pāṣāṇa Kalaśa Dhvajārohaṇa\"(raising of a stone finial). The inscription found at the Pāṣāṇa Gaṇeśa (Stone Gaṇeśa) suggests that the installation of thekalaśa(finial) was regarded as marking the completion of temple construction. This date, therefore, may be taken as the initial construction date of the temple."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/d8d8d8e4-76ea-4db0-a222-6527d4e0eda3> ;
    rdfs:comment "Numerous medieval inscriptions refer to the completion of temple construction through a ritual known as\"Suvarṇa Kalaśa Dhvajārohaṇa\"(raising of a golden finial) or\"Pāṣāṇa Kalaśa Dhvajārohaṇa\"(raising of a stone finial). The inscription found at the Pāṣāṇa Gaṇeśa (Stone Gaṇeśa) suggests that the installation of thekalaśa(finial) was regarded as marking the completion of temple construction. This date, therefore, may be taken as the initial construction date of the temple."@en ;
