    rdfs:label "Unknown event"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Although the date is legible, the inscription is heavily worn, making it difficult to determine its exact content. However, since the inscription is dedicated to the music master Nāṭyeśvara, it is particularly intriguing that a carving of akhiṃ(a traditional drum) appears at the top of the inscription."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/d8d8d8e4-76ea-4db0-a222-6527d4e0eda3> ;
