        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Installation of edict"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The stele in the second chamber of the fountain contains a 9-line eroded Tibetan inscription. The inscription appears to be an edict, possibly written between the ninth and twelfth centuries. Archaeologist David C. Andolfatto discovered the stele in 2014 CE. It is currently being translated."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/da0e6aad-2946-46c4-b425-585a104917fe> ;
