<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/dc4fbbf9-6714-46c6-95ca-bb0dc5174b85_1> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:TransferOfCustody ;
    rdfs:label "Addition of statue"@en ;
    dcterms:description "This inscription from 1695 CE (NS 816) is legible but unrelated to the temple. It refers to a Kumāra temple in the area where Kṛṣṇamatī, granddaughter of King Śrīnivāsa Malla, installed an Umāmaheśvara statue and endowed land for a trust. While this Kumāra temple later disappeared, its inscription appears to have been relocated here. Kunu Śarmā’sKīrtipatākāmentions the presence of a temple dedicated to Kārtikeya, another name of Kumāra, west of the Nugaḥ Ṭola. This inscription is from that missing temple."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/dc4fbbf9-6714-46c6-95ca-bb0dc5174b85> ;
    rdfs:comment "This inscription from 1695 CE (NS 816) is legible but unrelated to the temple. It refers to a Kumāra temple in the area where Kṛṣṇamatī, granddaughter of King Śrīnivāsa Malla, installed an Umāmaheśvara statue and endowed land for a trust. While this Kumāra temple later disappeared, its inscription appears to have been relocated here. Kunu Śarmā’sKīrtipatākāmentions the presence of a temple dedicated to Kārtikeya, another name of Kumāra, west of the Nugaḥ Ṭola. This inscription is from that missing temple."@en ;
