<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/ddcff119-38d2-4a7d-aac4-bcff077de144_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Renovation of the jaḥdhuṃ"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Trivikrama Śarmmā reconstructed the Cā̃guJaḥdhuṃ, and the inscription installed during the reconstruction warns that anyone who damages it will be guilty of the five great sins. It also states that failing to fill theJaḥdhuṃwith water on the twelfth lunar day, full moon, and Wednesday will result in sin."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/ddcff119-38d2-4a7d-aac4-bcff077de144> ;
