<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/de1f3dd8-735a-4dcc-99e0-511c861ae0fb_1> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Construction of cemented wall and other structures"@en ;
    dcterms:description "In 1994–95 CE (VS 2051), a small cemented structure, boundary wall, and externalcautārā(resting platform) were built surrounding the well. At that time, public access to the well was restricted; instead, arrangements were made for the water to collect in an external tank for common use. The overflow from this tank was directed through a pipe to another tank located about 400 meters downhill near thecautārā. This renovation was carried out under local leadership with donations collected from devotees."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/de1f3dd8-735a-4dcc-99e0-511c861ae0fb> ;
    rdfs:comment "In 1994–95 CE (VS 2051), a small cemented structure, boundary wall, and externalcautārā(resting platform) were built surrounding the well. At that time, public access to the well was restricted; instead, arrangements were made for the water to collect in an external tank for common use. The overflow from this tank was directed through a pipe to another tank located about 400 meters downhill near thecautārā. This renovation was carried out under local leadership with donations collected from devotees."@en ;
