<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/de2e27d5-8645-4e26-adea-a39f9f3ad89d_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:TransferOfCustody ;
    rdfs:label "Initial construction"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The inscription, preserved on the first floor of thedharmaśālā, documents its initial construction by Brahma Samasera Jaṅga Bahādura Rāṇa in memory of his wife Durgā Kumārī. Additionally, the inscription indicates that no land was allocated to thedharmaśālā, and nogūṭhī(trust) was established for its maintenance. The founder earnestly requests the king, subjects, and nobles to assume responsibility for its renovations whenever necessary."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/de2e27d5-8645-4e26-adea-a39f9f3ad89d> ;
    rdfs:comment "The inscription, preserved on the first floor of thedharmaśālā, documents its initial construction by Brahma Samasera Jaṅga Bahādura Rāṇa in memory of his wife Durgā Kumārī. Additionally, the inscription indicates that no land was allocated to thedharmaśālā, and nogūṭhī(trust) was established for its maintenance. The founder earnestly requests the king, subjects, and nobles to assume responsibility for its renovations whenever necessary."@en ;
