<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/df80a404-139e-44c2-b9e0-d514bad59022_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:TransferOfCustody ;
    rdfs:label "Construction of the jaḥdhuṃ"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Bhavānidāsa of Bakū Nani, Caṃki Ṭol, Lalitpur, together with his wife Mānakumārī and sons Īśvarīdāsa and Kṛṣṇadāsa, built the Jaḥdhuṃ in dedication to Bālakumārī Devī and in memory of his ancestors. To maintain the water supply, he endowed 1.5ropanīof land at Ṣonāthau as aguṭhī, with a clause allowing reclamation in case of neglect. During the annualvarṣavardhana pūjā, offerings ofSamaybaji—beaten rice (ciurā),syāḥbaji,boḍe, meat, and ginger—were made under the supervision of the localpañcas(elders) of Caṃki Ṭol."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/df80a404-139e-44c2-b9e0-d514bad59022> ;
    rdfs:comment "Bhavānidāsa of Bakū Nani, Caṃki Ṭol, Lalitpur, together with his wife Mānakumārī and sons Īśvarīdāsa and Kṛṣṇadāsa, built the Jaḥdhuṃ in dedication to Bālakumārī Devī and in memory of his ancestors. To maintain the water supply, he endowed 1.5ropanīof land at Ṣonāthau as aguṭhī, with a clause allowing reclamation in case of neglect. During the annualvarṣavardhana pūjā, offerings ofSamaybaji—beaten rice (ciurā),syāḥbaji,boḍe, meat, and ginger—were made under the supervision of the localpañcas(elders) of Caṃki Ṭol."@en ;
