<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/e08432a0-2ddc-4244-855e-9ecfacd4ca88_1> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:TransferOfCustody ;
    rdfs:label "Endowment of lands for phalcā"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Three brothers—Dālita, Labikala Sāhu Bhāro, and Bilananda Sāhu Bhāro—donated land for thephalcāwest of the temple in honor of their parents, Tadhi Sāhu and Bakhalakṣmī. They also established a non-expendable trust to support thephalcā. The income from the land and fund was used to organize the worship of Gaṇeśa on the final day of Caitra during theBiskāḥ Jātrāfestival, followed by the distribution of various food offerings on the next day, the 1st solar day of Vaiśākha."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/e08432a0-2ddc-4244-855e-9ecfacd4ca88> ;
    rdfs:comment "Three brothers—Dālita, Labikala Sāhu Bhāro, and Bilananda Sāhu Bhāro—donated land for thephalcāwest of the temple in honor of their parents, Tadhi Sāhu and Bakhalakṣmī. They also established a non-expendable trust to support thephalcā. The income from the land and fund was used to organize the worship of Gaṇeśa on the final day of Caitra during theBiskāḥ Jātrāfestival, followed by the distribution of various food offerings on the next day, the 1st solar day of Vaiśākha."@en ;
