<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/e24051bb-caf5-4479-b3e7-e8252a550661_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Initial Construction of the Temple, Hiti, and Phalcā, and Establishment of a Guṭhī"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The inscription records that a certain donor from Kirtipur constructed this temple along with the nearbyhitiand one of twophalcās,and established aguṭhī.Unfortunately, the part of the inscription where the date and the name of the donor were recorded, is severly damaged.  Its legible part mentionsKvāṭha NāyakaCaṇḍī Rāja Bhāro (Ś. ŚreṣṭhaVS 2057 182-183) as one of theguṭhīmembers.'Kvāṭha Nāyaka'refers to a post which was given to the head officer of Kirtipur by Malla King of Patan in the Late Malla Period. On this basis, it can be assumed that the temple was built in the Late Malla Era."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/e24051bb-caf5-4479-b3e7-e8252a550661> ;
    rdfs:comment "The inscription records that a certain donor from Kirtipur constructed this temple along with the nearbyhitiand one of twophalcās,and established aguṭhī.Unfortunately, the part of the inscription where the date and the name of the donor were recorded, is severly damaged.  Its legible part mentionsKvāṭha NāyakaCaṇḍī Rāja Bhāro (Ś. ŚreṣṭhaVS 2057 182-183) as one of theguṭhīmembers.'Kvāṭha Nāyaka'refers to a post which was given to the head officer of Kirtipur by Malla King of Patan in the Late Malla Period. On this basis, it can be assumed that the temple was built in the Late Malla Era."@en ;
