<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/e277eff9-5f7a-405c-908b-e3d13cda743e_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:TransferOfCustody ;
    rdfs:label "Construction of a phalcā"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Matsyendrasimha of Dattalācheṃ (Dhālācheṃ) Ṭola, Lalitpur, constructed aphalcain the name of Lakṣmīramaṇa Upādhyāya and his three wives Dhanthakuṃ, Lakṣmī, and Pālulakṣmī. He also endowed threeropanīsof land as guthi for its upkeep. The income generated from this land was designated to fund annual worship of Dāmodara (Gaṇeśa), Sarasvatī, and Lakṣmī on 3rd of bright fortnight of Kārtika, followed byśrāddharituals. It was mandated that Brahmins, Brāhmaṇīs, Jyotiśīs, and Karmācāryas be invited to these ceremonies. Any remaining funds after the rituals were to be used to provide a feast for the guthi caretakers. The inscription lists these caretakers as Bhajusimha Bhāro of Olā Ṭola, Gajendrasimha Bhāro of Kobahā Ṭola, Vīranarasimha Bhāro of Sātiglā (Saugaḷ) Ṭola, and Cikiti Bhāro of Dattalācheṃ Ṭola. At present, only asataḥ(raised platform) remains within the Dhantila Vārāhī shrine precinct; nophalcasurvives, indicating that the pavilion built by Matsyendrasiṃha has likely disappeared over time."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/e277eff9-5f7a-405c-908b-e3d13cda743e> ;
    rdfs:comment "Matsyendrasimha of Dattalācheṃ (Dhālācheṃ) Ṭola, Lalitpur, constructed aphalcain the name of Lakṣmīramaṇa Upādhyāya and his three wives Dhanthakuṃ, Lakṣmī, and Pālulakṣmī. He also endowed threeropanīsof land as guthi for its upkeep. The income generated from this land was designated to fund annual worship of Dāmodara (Gaṇeśa), Sarasvatī, and Lakṣmī on 3rd of bright fortnight of Kārtika, followed byśrāddharituals. It was mandated that Brahmins, Brāhmaṇīs, Jyotiśīs, and Karmācāryas be invited to these ceremonies. Any remaining funds after the rituals were to be used to provide a feast for the guthi caretakers. The inscription lists these caretakers as Bhajusimha Bhāro of Olā Ṭola, Gajendrasimha Bhāro of Kobahā Ṭola, Vīranarasimha Bhāro of Sātiglā (Saugaḷ) Ṭola, and Cikiti Bhāro of Dattalācheṃ Ṭola. At present, only asataḥ(raised platform) remains within the Dhantila Vārāhī shrine precinct; nophalcasurvives, indicating that the pavilion built by Matsyendrasiṃha has likely disappeared over time."@en ;
