<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/e277eff9-5f7a-405c-908b-e3d13cda743e_2> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Enshrinement ;
    rdfs:label "Installation of a new statue of Vārāhī"@en ;
    dcterms:description "After the original image of Vārāhī housed in the sanctum was stolen, Kṛṣṇanātha Māske and his wife Śakuntalā Māske of Bālīphala Ṭola, Lalitpur, commissioned and installed a new cast-metal image of the goddess. On this occasion, they also tiled the sanctum floor, added copper sheeting (ilāṃ), applied gilding (jalapa) to the toraṇa, and installed an iron fence around the temple for security."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/e277eff9-5f7a-405c-908b-e3d13cda743e> ;
    rdfs:comment "After the original image of Vārāhī housed in the sanctum was stolen, Kṛṣṇanātha Māske and his wife Śakuntalā Māske of Bālīphala Ṭola, Lalitpur, commissioned and installed a new cast-metal image of the goddess. On this occasion, they also tiled the sanctum floor, added copper sheeting (ilāṃ), applied gilding (jalapa) to the toraṇa, and installed an iron fence around the temple for security."@en ;
