<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/e29f9e62-dc1b-40b1-94a3-75a952edafb6_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Renovation"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The reconstruction of the temple was undertaken by the Kathmandu Valley Preservation Trust, funded by the US Ambassadors Fund for Cultural Preservation, in collaboration with the Department of Archaeology. An inscription from another Śiva temple (KAT1550) of similar size situated north of this monument records the reconstruction of that temple in 2018 CE (VS 2074), in response to the damages caused by the 2015 CE earthquakes. Although the inscription does not make reference to this particular temple, it too underwent reconstruction during that period. In the process of restoration, the struts were repurposed, while some of the carved windows were replaced with new ones."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/e29f9e62-dc1b-40b1-94a3-75a952edafb6> ;
    rdfs:comment "The reconstruction of the temple was undertaken by the Kathmandu Valley Preservation Trust, funded by the US Ambassadors Fund for Cultural Preservation, in collaboration with the Department of Archaeology. An inscription from another Śiva temple (KAT1550) of similar size situated north of this monument records the reconstruction of that temple in 2018 CE (VS 2074), in response to the damages caused by the 2015 CE earthquakes. Although the inscription does not make reference to this particular temple, it too underwent reconstruction during that period. In the process of restoration, the struts were repurposed, while some of the carved windows were replaced with new ones."@en ;
