<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/e4e53fcc-4398-42e7-b561-ffdddf042853_1> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Establishment of the bāhāḥ"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The Ikhācva Bāhāḥ was founded through a fire ritual and the establishment of statues of Akṣobhya, Mahākāla, Cakrasamvara, and Vajravārāhī. The primary donor is believed to be Svakaraju Vajrācārya (Pruscha 1975, Ca-3). An inscription at thebāhāḥstates that Vīradeva and his mother Padmāvatī also took part in the fire oblation. They probably were the son and wife of donor Svakaraju. A Vajrācārya priest from Nyākhācuka, Patan, oversaw the establishment rituals."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/e4e53fcc-4398-42e7-b561-ffdddf042853> ;
    rdfs:comment "The Ikhācva Bāhāḥ was founded through a fire ritual and the establishment of statues of Akṣobhya, Mahākāla, Cakrasamvara, and Vajravārāhī. The primary donor is believed to be Svakaraju Vajrācārya (Pruscha 1975, Ca-3). An inscription at thebāhāḥstates that Vīradeva and his mother Padmāvatī also took part in the fire oblation. They probably were the son and wife of donor Svakaraju. A Vajrācārya priest from Nyākhācuka, Patan, oversaw the establishment rituals."@en ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/agent/antigravity_agent> ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/activity/heritagegraph_kg_construction> ;
    hg:eventIndex 1 ;
    hg:extractionMethod "source_table" ;
    hg:isEventOf <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/e4e53fcc-4398-42e7-b561-ffdddf042853> .

<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/e4e53fcc-4398-42e7-b561-ffdddf042853_2> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Establishment of the statue of Lakṣmīnārāyaṇa"@en ;
    dcterms:description "This inscription does not seem to be connected to the Ikhācva Bāhāḥ. Dātimha Lākhaya, a resident of Bhansāra Ṭola in Cāpāgāũ, installed the Lakṣmīnārāyaṇa statue. He also donated land to establish a trust for the deity’s care and worship. The land’s income was to fund a yearly feast on the 5th of the bright fortnight of Phālguna for those tending to the deity. The Lakṣmīnārāyaṇa statue mentioned in the inscription might be the one found inside the Vādey Kṛṣṇa Temple (CHG0010) in Bhansāra Ṭola."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/e4e53fcc-4398-42e7-b561-ffdddf042853> ;
    rdfs:comment "This inscription does not seem to be connected to the Ikhācva Bāhāḥ. Dātimha Lākhaya, a resident of Bhansāra Ṭola in Cāpāgāũ, installed the Lakṣmīnārāyaṇa statue. He also donated land to establish a trust for the deity’s care and worship. The land’s income was to fund a yearly feast on the 5th of the bright fortnight of Phālguna for those tending to the deity. The Lakṣmīnārāyaṇa statue mentioned in the inscription might be the one found inside the Vādey Kṛṣṇa Temple (CHG0010) in Bhansāra Ṭola."@en ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/agent/antigravity_agent> ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/activity/heritagegraph_kg_construction> ;
