<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/e77be04f-be3a-4445-b751-0cb7995daf6a_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Renovation"@en ;
    dcterms:description "A stone inscription from NS 753?, attached to the east of the Kaṅgaḥ Ajimā shrine, records a renovation of something during King Lakṣmīnarasiṃha Malla’s and his son Pratāpa Malla’s joint rule. Because of the deterioration of the text, the year and other details of the event are unknown. Perhaps it was the Dyaḥchẽ that was renovated."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/e77be04f-be3a-4445-b751-0cb7995daf6a> ;
    rdfs:comment "A stone inscription from NS 753?, attached to the east of the Kaṅgaḥ Ajimā shrine, records a renovation of something during King Lakṣmīnarasiṃha Malla’s and his son Pratāpa Malla’s joint rule. Because of the deterioration of the text, the year and other details of the event are unknown. Perhaps it was the Dyaḥchẽ that was renovated."@en ;
