<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/e77be04f-be3a-4445-b751-0cb7995daf6a_2> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:TransferOfCustody ;
    rdfs:label "Construction of a rest house and land endowment"@en ;
    dcterms:description "According to a stone inscription attached to the first floor of the Dyaḥchẽ (outside the sanctum), five people built a rest house (dharmaśālā) in the name of Revati and Hākusiṃ of the Yatkhā Ṭola (the rest house dealt with in the inscription is most likely the Nāsaḥdyaḥ Sataḥ, adjacent to the Dyaḥchẽ). They also formed aguthiby endowing some plots of land and establishing a fund of 35moharas. The proceeds from the land were to be used to perform special worship of Kaṅgaḥ Ajimā and to light flames in her honour on the day of her procession."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/e77be04f-be3a-4445-b751-0cb7995daf6a> ;
    rdfs:comment "According to a stone inscription attached to the first floor of the Dyaḥchẽ (outside the sanctum), five people built a rest house (dharmaśālā) in the name of Revati and Hākusiṃ of the Yatkhā Ṭola (the rest house dealt with in the inscription is most likely the Nāsaḥdyaḥ Sataḥ, adjacent to the Dyaḥchẽ). They also formed aguthiby endowing some plots of land and establishing a fund of 35moharas. The proceeds from the land were to be used to perform special worship of Kaṅgaḥ Ajimā and to light flames in her honour on the day of her procession."@en ;
