<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/ec08dc4c-646f-45bd-b152-4781e312bd08_5> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Addition of a guṭhī"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Bhoṭu Pā̃ḍe established a trust by donating 6ropanīs of land with a specific purpose: to facilitate the periodic renewal of two distinctive banners known assulupuludhvajāandaṣṭamaṅgalapatākāduring the 12-year dance presentation of Ṅatamaru Ajimā. The trust's financial resources, generated from the donated lands, were designated to ensure that these banners were replaced with new ones every 12 years, just prior to the commencement of the dance performances. The inscription further directed the trust members to accompany these banners alongside the dance troupe during their performances at various locations. An additional copperplate bearing identical content, now held in a private collection by an individual taking on the role of Mahālakṣmī within the dance troupe, exists; however, its current whereabouts are unknown. Furthermore, a historical record from 1915 CE (VS 1972) at the Guṭhī Lagata Jā̃ca Aḍḍā, an administrative office previously responsible for religious trusts, details the financial activities of this trust."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/ec08dc4c-646f-45bd-b152-4781e312bd08> ;
    rdfs:comment "Bhoṭu Pā̃ḍe established a trust by donating 6ropanīs of land with a specific purpose: to facilitate the periodic renewal of two distinctive banners known assulupuludhvajāandaṣṭamaṅgalapatākāduring the 12-year dance presentation of Ṅatamaru Ajimā. The trust's financial resources, generated from the donated lands, were designated to ensure that these banners were replaced with new ones every 12 years, just prior to the commencement of the dance performances. The inscription further directed the trust members to accompany these banners alongside the dance troupe during their performances at various locations. An additional copperplate bearing identical content, now held in a private collection by an individual taking on the role of Mahālakṣmī within the dance troupe, exists; however, its current whereabouts are unknown. Furthermore, a historical record from 1915 CE (VS 1972) at the Guṭhī Lagata Jā̃ca Aḍḍā, an administrative office previously responsible for religious trusts, details the financial activities of this trust."@en ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/agent/antigravity_agent> ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/activity/heritagegraph_kg_construction> ;
