<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/ed6d9432-4c5c-4125-b9fe-f60c92138df0_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:TransferOfCustody ;
    rdfs:label "Endowment of lands for feeding ascetics"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Bālanātha Yogī donated land and a garden to establish a trust for conducting special worship and providing food to ascetics. The trust was responsible forpañcopacārapūjā, a special worship that involves offering five items like flowers and incense to Gorakhanātha on the 8th of the bright fortnight of Vaiśākha and to Buṅgadyaḥ on the day after his chariot arrived at Lagankhel. A copperplate inscription recording the donation deed mentions King Pratāpa Malla as its witness."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/ed6d9432-4c5c-4125-b9fe-f60c92138df0> ;
    rdfs:comment "Bālanātha Yogī donated land and a garden to establish a trust for conducting special worship and providing food to ascetics. The trust was responsible forpañcopacārapūjā, a special worship that involves offering five items like flowers and incense to Gorakhanātha on the 8th of the bright fortnight of Vaiśākha and to Buṅgadyaḥ on the day after his chariot arrived at Lagankhel. A copperplate inscription recording the donation deed mentions King Pratāpa Malla as its witness."@en ;
