<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/edc2f9a3-2786-446a-b150-1018d3fe7382_1> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Offering of a bell"@en ;
    dcterms:description "An inscription on the bell at the nearby Lakṣmīnārāyaṇa temple (KAT2640) mentions that it was offered to Indrabhakteśvara Mahādeva in 1864 CE (VS 1921). However, it appears that the bell originally dedicated to Indrabhakteśvara was later relocated to the nearby temple, likely after the early 1970s."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/edc2f9a3-2786-446a-b150-1018d3fe7382> ;
