<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/ef3c4df6-7764-4432-91a4-abd290cf4b45_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Consecration ;
    rdfs:label "Initial construction"@en ;
    dcterms:description "During the reign of King Mānadeva (r. 464-505 CE), Ratnasaṅgha, a prominent tradesman leader (sārthavāha), consecrated theśivaliṅga, naming it Ratneśvara after himself and endowing numerous land parcels in its honor."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/ef3c4df6-7764-4432-91a4-abd290cf4b45> ;
    rdfs:comment "During the reign of King Mānadeva (r. 464-505 CE), Ratnasaṅgha, a prominent tradesman leader (sārthavāha), consecrated theśivaliṅga, naming it Ratneśvara after himself and endowing numerous land parcels in its honor."@en ;
