<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/ef3c4df6-7764-4432-91a4-abd290cf4b45_1> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:TransferOfCustody ;
    rdfs:label "Land grant for Vimaleśvara"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Aniṣkalaliṅga, an unadorned form ofśivaliṅga, was unearthed while digging the foundation for a private building located approximately 50 meters northeast of the Ratneśvara Śivaliṅga and was subsequently placed within the concrete chamber designated for the Ratneśvara Śivaliṅga. This newly foundśivaliṅgafeatured an inscription dating back to 486 CE (ŚS 407), documenting the donation of land parcels by Vimala Saṃgha, asārthavāha, for theśivaliṅgaestablished by an individual named Sutenātri (Ś. Rājavaṃśī VS 20, pp.43-56). As a result, theśivaliṅgawas named Vimaleśvara in honor of the donor Vimala Saṃgha."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/ef3c4df6-7764-4432-91a4-abd290cf4b45> ;
    rdfs:comment "Aniṣkalaliṅga, an unadorned form ofśivaliṅga, was unearthed while digging the foundation for a private building located approximately 50 meters northeast of the Ratneśvara Śivaliṅga and was subsequently placed within the concrete chamber designated for the Ratneśvara Śivaliṅga. This newly foundśivaliṅgafeatured an inscription dating back to 486 CE (ŚS 407), documenting the donation of land parcels by Vimala Saṃgha, asārthavāha, for theśivaliṅgaestablished by an individual named Sutenātri (Ś. Rājavaṃśī VS 20, pp.43-56). As a result, theśivaliṅgawas named Vimaleśvara in honor of the donor Vimala Saṃgha."@en ;
