        hg:Consecration ;
    rdfs:label "Consecration"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The inscription states the name of Bālakṛṣṇeśvara and the date as the full moon day in the month of Vaiśākha, NS 832. The meaning of the inscription is not clear. This date might refer to an unknown event that happened 6 months after the temple was established.Gutschow(2011, 566) interprets this as the date of its consecration."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/f0ef1474-eb56-11e9-b125-0242ac130002> ;
