<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/f1b969ea-f1ed-44dd-8304-154e7eb89195_6> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Unclear event"@en ;
    dcterms:description "This inscription dates back to the reign of King Yakṣa Malla (r. 1428–1482 CE), long before the construction of the Harṣamukteśvara temple. The inscription bears King Yakṣa Malla's name and praises his glory. The inscription was probably engraved on the pedestal when the statue of Lakṣmīnārāyaṇa (BKT0460-017) was installed. However, since part of the inscription has eroded and the lower portion is buried, the donor's name and the exact date could not be determined."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/f1b969ea-f1ed-44dd-8304-154e7eb89195> ;
    rdfs:comment "This inscription dates back to the reign of King Yakṣa Malla (r. 1428–1482 CE), long before the construction of the Harṣamukteśvara temple. The inscription bears King Yakṣa Malla's name and praises his glory. The inscription was probably engraved on the pedestal when the statue of Lakṣmīnārāyaṇa (BKT0460-017) was installed. However, since part of the inscription has eroded and the lower portion is buried, the donor's name and the exact date could not be determined."@en ;
