<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/f5a48d0e-2f70-4721-abb2-614f7311dec9_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:RitualEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Theft in the temple"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The Bhoṭes, who are of Tibetan origin, forcibly opened the door of the Vajrayoginī Temple and stole the jewelry belonging to the deity. Upon discovering the theft, Priest Bābudeva reported the incident to King Amṛta Malla, who took action and successfully apprehended the thieves. As a part of purification process, a ritual was performed since the thieves had touched the statue of the deity."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/f5a48d0e-2f70-4721-abb2-614f7311dec9> ;
    rdfs:comment "The Bhoṭes, who are of Tibetan origin, forcibly opened the door of the Vajrayoginī Temple and stole the jewelry belonging to the deity. Upon discovering the theft, Priest Bābudeva reported the incident to King Amṛta Malla, who took action and successfully apprehended the thieves. As a part of purification process, a ritual was performed since the thieves had touched the statue of the deity."@en ;
