<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/f5a48d0e-2f70-4721-abb2-614f7311dec9_1> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:TransferOfCustody ;
    rdfs:label "Construction of the Vajrayoginī Mandira"@en ;
    dcterms:description "King Pratāpa Malla initiated the construction of the temple and allocated lands for aguthito oversee the daily rituals at the site. Although the inscription documenting this event does not explicitly specify the architectural style of the temple, it does reference an annual tradition of applying lime to the temple on the full moon day of Caitra. Given that lime coatings are unnecessary for tiered temples, this suggests that the temple erected by Pratāpa Malla followed theśikharastyle. The inscription is divided into two separate steles, with the first one  positioned north of the Jogeśvara Mandira, and the second one affixed to the west-facing wall of the Jogeśvara Mandira."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/f5a48d0e-2f70-4721-abb2-614f7311dec9> ;
    rdfs:comment "King Pratāpa Malla initiated the construction of the temple and allocated lands for aguthito oversee the daily rituals at the site. Although the inscription documenting this event does not explicitly specify the architectural style of the temple, it does reference an annual tradition of applying lime to the temple on the full moon day of Caitra. Given that lime coatings are unnecessary for tiered temples, this suggests that the temple erected by Pratāpa Malla followed theśikharastyle. The inscription is divided into two separate steles, with the first one  positioned north of the Jogeśvara Mandira, and the second one affixed to the west-facing wall of the Jogeśvara Mandira."@en ;
