<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/f5a48d0e-2f70-4721-abb2-614f7311dec9_2> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Offering pinnacle to the later temple"@en ;
    dcterms:description "A later reconstruction of the Temple, dated to 1670 CE (NS 790), included the installation of a finial. However, it is unlikely that a finial was added just 15 years after the initial construction of the Temple in 1655 CE. It is possible that the Temple was rebuilt prior to the addition of the finial, but there are no historical sources available to confirm this hypothesis."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/f5a48d0e-2f70-4721-abb2-614f7311dec9> ;
    rdfs:comment "A later reconstruction of the Temple, dated to 1670 CE (NS 790), included the installation of a finial. However, it is unlikely that a finial was added just 15 years after the initial construction of the Temple in 1655 CE. It is possible that the Temple was rebuilt prior to the addition of the finial, but there are no historical sources available to confirm this hypothesis."@en ;
