<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/f5a48d0e-2f70-4721-abb2-614f7311dec9_21> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Offering of a stone pillar with a lion statue"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Tejanārāyaṇa Tulādhara, a resident of Madu (also known as Maru) Ṭola of Kathmandu, along with his wife Viṣṇumati and other family members, made a generous offering to the Vajrayoginī Temple. They donated a stone pillar adorned with a gilt copper lion figure, which was erected in front of the temple."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/f5a48d0e-2f70-4721-abb2-614f7311dec9> ;
    rdfs:comment "Tejanārāyaṇa Tulādhara, a resident of Madu (also known as Maru) Ṭola of Kathmandu, along with his wife Viṣṇumati and other family members, made a generous offering to the Vajrayoginī Temple. They donated a stone pillar adorned with a gilt copper lion figure, which was erected in front of the temple."@en ;
