<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/f6f28540-6aa7-4a61-abd1-03d8250aa25f_1> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Reconstructions of the Sataḥ"@en ;
    dcterms:description "After the Sataḥ collapsed in the 1934 earthquakes, it was never rebuilt in its former state.N. YogīVS 2012, p. 62 writes that the Sataḥ was rebuilt at the behest of the locals in presence of the police although it was the responsibility of the Guṭhī Saṃsthāna to reconstruct it. The reconstruction converted the Sataḥ into a plain building of one floor that provided space for the operation of a local library. Later in 1959 CE, the Chẽbhaḍela Office of Bhaktapur dismantled the Building and replaced it with a two-story concrete structure."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/f6f28540-6aa7-4a61-abd1-03d8250aa25f> ;
    rdfs:comment "After the Sataḥ collapsed in the 1934 earthquakes, it was never rebuilt in its former state.N. YogīVS 2012, p. 62 writes that the Sataḥ was rebuilt at the behest of the locals in presence of the police although it was the responsibility of the Guṭhī Saṃsthāna to reconstruct it. The reconstruction converted the Sataḥ into a plain building of one floor that provided space for the operation of a local library. Later in 1959 CE, the Chẽbhaḍela Office of Bhaktapur dismantled the Building and replaced it with a two-story concrete structure."@en ;
