<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/fb345afd-944e-49a0-a46a-441395076f6c_0> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Construction of a phalcā"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Prajāpati Jeta, Amita, and Dhana, among others, collectively built aphalcarest house for their lineage deity Viśvakarmā to the east of the temple. Thephalcāmention in this inscription is the god-house (dyaḥchẽ) east of the temple. Thedyaḥchẽwas previously aphalcāand was dismantled in 1988 CE (VS 2045) to be converted into adyaḥchẽ, which has now been rented out."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/fb345afd-944e-49a0-a46a-441395076f6c> ;
    rdfs:comment "Prajāpati Jeta, Amita, and Dhana, among others, collectively built aphalcarest house for their lineage deity Viśvakarmā to the east of the temple. Thephalcāmention in this inscription is the god-house (dyaḥchẽ) east of the temple. Thedyaḥchẽwas previously aphalcāand was dismantled in 1988 CE (VS 2045) to be converted into adyaḥchẽ, which has now been rented out."@en ;
