<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/fb49ddb6-2c68-4965-b235-046da5e9f4fa_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Initial construction"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Rāmakṛṣṇa Bhāro and a group of individuals constructed the temple by establishing Goddess Bhairavī as their patron deity. Alongside the temple's construction, they dedicated tworopanīsof land at Namkhvāḥcā, located south of the temple. This land was intended for conducting the temple's anniversary rituals on the full moon day of Mārgaśīrṣa. The inscription also includes a provision directing concerned individuals to allocate a sum of 1mohararupaiyā̃and 10dāmasfrom the earnings for future renovations of the temple."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/fb49ddb6-2c68-4965-b235-046da5e9f4fa> ;
    rdfs:comment "Rāmakṛṣṇa Bhāro and a group of individuals constructed the temple by establishing Goddess Bhairavī as their patron deity. Alongside the temple's construction, they dedicated tworopanīsof land at Namkhvāḥcā, located south of the temple. This land was intended for conducting the temple's anniversary rituals on the full moon day of Mārgaśīrṣa. The inscription also includes a provision directing concerned individuals to allocate a sum of 1mohararupaiyā̃and 10dāmasfrom the earnings for future renovations of the temple."@en ;
