<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/fdb69fc2-0782-4930-8ef8-df57c79c1006_1> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:HistoricalEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Establishment of Dharmadhātujinālaya Caitya?"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The base plinth of the Dharmadhātujinālaya Caitya (object number KAT1440-005) located in front of thebāhāḥbears an inscription accompanied by carved statues of seven individuals. These individuals are identified as Dasanārāṃ, Budhalnana (possibly Budharatna?), Rakṣmitārā, Budhamāyā, Bisunuprabhā, Māyādevi, and Choti. However, the inscription itself does not provide any further information regarding their role or relationship to thecaitya. It remains unclear whether these individuals were the donors of thecaityaor if thecaityawas established in their memory."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/fdb69fc2-0782-4930-8ef8-df57c79c1006> ;
    rdfs:comment "The base plinth of the Dharmadhātujinālaya Caitya (object number KAT1440-005) located in front of thebāhāḥbears an inscription accompanied by carved statues of seven individuals. These individuals are identified as Dasanārāṃ, Budhalnana (possibly Budharatna?), Rakṣmitārā, Budhamāyā, Bisunuprabhā, Māyādevi, and Choti. However, the inscription itself does not provide any further information regarding their role or relationship to thecaitya. It remains unclear whether these individuals were the donors of thecaityaor if thecaityawas established in their memory."@en ;
