<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/fe6ac976-a5a9-433d-96fa-23480b8ce6ba_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Establishment of Gönpa Gang"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Gönpa Gang (dgon pa sgang), its full original name being Göngang Künzang Chöling (dgon sgang kun bzang chos gling) was built by Künzang Longyang (kun bzang klong yangs; 1644–1696) in memory of his brother between 1684 and 1695. (see Harrison, Luczanits, Ramble 2018: 55).On the founder and his teacher, Orgyen Pelzang (o rgyan dpal bzang; 1617–1677) see Ehrhard 2013a: 207–10, and Harrison, Luczanits, Ramble 2018: 101–116. Details about the construction are revealed in the founder’s autobiography summarised by Ramble."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/fe6ac976-a5a9-433d-96fa-23480b8ce6ba> ;
    rdfs:comment "Gönpa Gang (dgon pa sgang), its full original name being Göngang Künzang Chöling (dgon sgang kun bzang chos gling) was built by Künzang Longyang (kun bzang klong yangs; 1644–1696) in memory of his brother between 1684 and 1695. (see Harrison, Luczanits, Ramble 2018: 55).On the founder and his teacher, Orgyen Pelzang (o rgyan dpal bzang; 1617–1677) see Ehrhard 2013a: 207–10, and Harrison, Luczanits, Ramble 2018: 101–116. Details about the construction are revealed in the founder’s autobiography summarised by Ramble."@en ;
