<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/ff7398f9-1bb2-4e4e-ba9b-c985565f74a7_0> a crm:E12_Production,
        crm:E5_Event,
        hg:Production ;
    rdfs:label "Addition of Stone Lions and Śārdūlas"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The inscription which records the name of the founder of this temple also mentions the installation of the lions and Śārdūla statues flanking the main entrance, and thetoraṇacrowning the wooden windows. According to this inscription, an individual named Balirāma was the chief to execute this installation task, and he was assisted byKvāṭhanāyakaKāśīrāma Bābu, Dharaṇīdhara,KvāṭhanāyakaViśvarāma Bhāro[1], and Hākudeva.Footnotes^He constructed the Umāmaheśvara temple in Kirtipur (seeKIR0006)."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/ff7398f9-1bb2-4e4e-ba9b-c985565f74a7> ;
    rdfs:comment "The inscription which records the name of the founder of this temple also mentions the installation of the lions and Śārdūla statues flanking the main entrance, and thetoraṇacrowning the wooden windows. According to this inscription, an individual named Balirāma was the chief to execute this installation task, and he was assisted byKvāṭhanāyakaKāśīrāma Bābu, Dharaṇīdhara,KvāṭhanāyakaViśvarāma Bhāro[1], and Hākudeva.Footnotes^He constructed the Umāmaheśvara temple in Kirtipur (seeKIR0006)."@en ;
