<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/ff7398f9-1bb2-4e4e-ba9b-c985565f74a7_1> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:TransferOfCustody ;
    rdfs:label "Construction of a Phalcā, Installation of a Viṣṇu Statue, and Land Grant"@en ;
    dcterms:description "This inscription is not related to this temple. It records the initial construction of aphlalcāin the south-eastern corner of the temple by a person called Mādhava Siṃha Kājī and his wife Padminī (text: Padumini). It also mentions that the founders of thephalcāinstalled a Viṣṇu statue in it and granted some plots of land to finance the annual rituals during the Indrajātrā Festival. Thephalcāwas incorporated into a private house in around 1987 CE, and the inscription was then shifted inside this temple."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/ff7398f9-1bb2-4e4e-ba9b-c985565f74a7> ;
    rdfs:comment "This inscription is not related to this temple. It records the initial construction of aphlalcāin the south-eastern corner of the temple by a person called Mādhava Siṃha Kājī and his wife Padminī (text: Padumini). It also mentions that the founders of thephalcāinstalled a Viṣṇu statue in it and granted some plots of land to finance the annual rituals during the Indrajātrā Festival. Thephalcāwas incorporated into a private house in around 1987 CE, and the inscription was then shifted inside this temple."@en ;
