<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/ff7398f9-1bb2-4e4e-ba9b-c985565f74a7_2> a crm:E5_Event,
        hg:DestructionEvent ;
    rdfs:label "Renovation of a Phalcā"@en ;
    dcterms:description "This inscription which is kept inside the sanctum of this temple is also not related to it. According to the local elders, the inscription used to be kept inside thephalcāwhich was built in front of this temple. Following the collapse of thephalcā,[1]the inscription was shifted to its present-day place. It records the renovation of thephalcā,installation of an Umāmaheśvara statue inside it, and land grant to finance its annual rituals byKvāṭhanāyakaDṛṣṭirāja.Footnotes^They could recall the exact date when it collapsed."@en ;
    crm:P12_occurred_in_the_presence_of <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/ff7398f9-1bb2-4e4e-ba9b-c985565f74a7> ;
    rdfs:comment "This inscription which is kept inside the sanctum of this temple is also not related to it. According to the local elders, the inscription used to be kept inside thephalcāwhich was built in front of this temple. Following the collapse of thephalcā,[1]the inscription was shifted to its present-day place. It records the renovation of thephalcā,installation of an Umāmaheśvara statue inside it, and land grant to finance its annual rituals byKvāṭhanāyakaDṛṣṭirāja.Footnotes^They could recall the exact date when it collapsed."@en ;
