<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/55133c56-e68d-11e9-b125-0242ac130002> a crm:E22_Human-Made_Object,
        hg:ArchitecturalStructure,
        hg:Pati ;
    rdfs:label "Calakhu Phalcā  (1775 CE)"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "55133c56-e68d-11e9-b125-0242ac130002" ;
    dcterms:references "Sources and references Inscription identification number LAL4224_I_001 Sources Stone stele inscription embedded in a niche in the phalcā's wall. H: 30 cm, W: 24 cm Details Stone inscription of Calakhu phalcā related to Nārāyaṇa (transliteration and translation by Nutan Sharma, 2018) oṃ namaḥ nārāyaṇaṃ namaskṛtyaṃ naraṃ cau(cai)va narottamāṃ(mam) devīṃ saraś(s)vatīṃ (vyāsaṃ) ta- to jaya mut(d)īraya(e)[t] ||  || śreyostu || saṃmvat 895 māghakṛṣṇa || ṣaṣṭhān tithau bṛhaspativāsare thva kunhu kutubāhālayā laghuvaṃśa rāutta  si _ _ ... ... sa_ siddhilakṣmimaī thva nimha stri pu[ru]khasena svapurta divaṃgata _ _ datta bābusa māmana calaṣu lāṃche͂sa phale dayakaṃ śrī nārāyaṇa mūrtti _ _ _ _ pratiṣṭhā yāsyaṃ śrī 3 candamāsasa duntā pākubuṃ rova 3 java 3 _tasiṃdhuṣacābuṃ rova 3 puna dhalasikva karṣa 7 thvate buṃyā _ _ syanana _ phalesa mata choyakaṃ dāna biyamāla buṃgayātāna enātava || ni... ... _ _bhāropanisena yāyamāla saeva vaiśāṣa lachiṃ śrī 3 buṃga yāta ... ... ... ... || śrī _ _ 2 vaṃ _ _ tya japa pāṭha rācake || śrī 3 bo _ śvara ... ... ... ... kārttika lachiṃ mata biyake māla ... ... ... ... varṣaprati ... ... ... ... yāyamāla  cosye tako yātasā utrottara juya || cosya (tako) mayātasā paṃcamāhāpāpa lāka || śubhamastu || Translation of the inscription: (The beginning part of the inscription is the praises of Lord Narayan) In [NS] 895 (1775 CE), on the 6th day of dark half of Lunar month of Māgha, Thrusday. On this day, the couple from Kutu Bāhā, Si... ... Raghuvaṃśa Rāutta and his wife Siddhilakṣīmayī. The mother of the dead son has constructed this phalcā of Calkhu, Lāṃche͂ establishing in it an icon of Śrīnārāyaṇa in the name of the dead son ... Datta Bābu. Three ropani and 3 yava land of Pākubuṃ, 3 ropani s of land of Tasiṃ Dhuṣacābuṃ and 7 karṣa of land of Dholosikvaṃ are offered.  Those lands shall be used to repair the phalcā when destroyed. Burning lamps shall be offered there during the festival of red Matsyendranātha.... The Bhāro (noble) brothers shall do this during the whole month of Vaiśakha during the festival of red Matsyendranātha .... [Also,] japa (recitation of mantra ) and pāṭha (recitation of sacred texts) shall also be performed.... A lamp shall be offered in the whole month of Kārtika.... Every year.... If done according to what has been written, he shall get prosperous and if not done he shall get five great sins .... May all be well."@en ;
    dcterms:title "Calakhu Phalcā  (1775 CE)"@en ;
