<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/304bed70-ec0d-11e9-b125-0242ac130002> a crm:E22_Human-Made_Object,
        hg:ArchitecturalStructure,
        hg:Pati ;
    rdfs:label "Triratnavihāra Phalcā (1871 CE)"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "304bed70-ec0d-11e9-b125-0242ac130002" ;
    dcterms:references "Sources and references Details Summary of the inscription On the bright fortnight of Śrāvaṇa in NS 991 (1871 CE), a monastery ( vihāra ) called Triratna was constructed together with a rest house ( phalcā ) in front of the caitya located at Saptapurī Mahāvihāra, and a statue of triple gems ( triratna ) was established there on the same day. Triratna Vihāra was constructed by a family (consisting of older brother Bhānuvīra, younger brother Mānavīra and Siddhimāna, and sons and daughters) after having performed worships at all the monasteries of Lalitapura. Further, they donated certain plots of land in different places in order to please Triratna Buddha. It is instructed that the yearly income from the land should be spent on the activities that take place in the monastery."@en ;
    dcterms:title "Triratnavihāra Phalcā (1871 CE)"@en ;
    crm:P12i_was_present_at <https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/event/304bed70-ec0d-11e9-b125-0242ac130002_0> ;
