<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/dc5306f4-f571-11e9-8649-0242ac130002> a crm:E22_Human-Made_Object,
        hg:ArchitecturalStructure,
        hg:Pati ;
    rdfs:label "Dāphā Bhajana Phalcā  (c. 1650)"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "dc5306f4-f571-11e9-8649-0242ac130002" ;
    dcterms:references "Sources and references Sources The inscription at the shrine of Gaṇeśa of Dupāt was also published in Vajracharya (1999,100). Details Śrī Gaṇeśāya namaḥ | Buddhāya- namaḥ Dharmmāya namaḥ Sañghāya na- ma || Svamvat 771 Bhādra padre śukla pratipadāntithau pūrvvaphālguyā nakṣetre Śivayoge, Vṛhaspativāsa- re: thwa kunhu Dopāta Kothvanani, Vi- jayasiṃha Bhāvo Chekajhita, murgudi- cheyā : thaṃkādi Pālasiṃha Bhado(vo) pra- maṣina, Gunirā Dharmma gvaṣṭhi sa- mūhana doyāta rāchi tvaṃ ciña --- --- --- --- --- --- --- --- --- --- yāka Homage to Lord Ganeś. Homage to Lord Buddha, Dharma and Sañgha. On Thursday, the first day of the bright lunar fortnight of Bhādra in NS 771 (1651 AD), a team of Guṃlā Dharma Guthi paved the Dupāt lāchi (road) with brick. (provisionary translation by Rajendra Shakya, 2016)"@en ;
    dcterms:title "Dāphā Bhajana Phalcā  (c. 1650)"@en ;
