<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/b7910d9c-e915-11e9-b125-0242ac130002> a crm:E22_Human-Made_Object,
        hg:ArchitecturalStructure,
        hg:Pati ;
    rdfs:label "Maṇikula Phalcā (1860s CE)"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "b7910d9c-e915-11e9-b125-0242ac130002" ;
    dcterms:references "Sources and references Sources Inscription from NS 983 Details Text: (only the concerning portion from the stone inscription - provided by Nutan Sharma) oṁ namaḥ śrīraktalokeśvarāya || namaskārāyāṃ || śrīganeśvā[rā]yanamaḥ || .... .... ..... 9. _ _ _ || svasti || śrīnepālamaṇḍale lalitāpurīmahānagagyktarvartti cyāsala tola saptapurīmahāvihāravirājita śrī 3 śakyamuni buddha śā- 10. sana brahmacaryabhikṣu śrī maṇiratna vaidya bhāryyā indralakṣmī thvate strī puruṣayā dharmmacitta utpatti yaṅā 11. sthānadhipati śrī 3 ganeśayā devālaya jīrṇoddhāra yāṅa ganeśa mūrtti suvarṇayā dayakāva punaḥ maṃgalabā- 12. ra śevā ṣalaka sammata yāṅa suvarṇa lepita gajuri dayakāva saṃvata 982 jyeṣṭha vadi 4 sa pratiṣṭhā yāṅā- 13. va divaṃgata juyāva vanapiṃ putra putrī pautra pautrī sukhāvatī vāsa lāyamāla dhakaṃ bhāvanā yāṅa prati- 14. varṣa indrajātrā kunhu deva pūjā yāṅa dāna biya dharmmaśārāsa bhajana yāka panitaṃ naivedya 15. taya thva dharmmaśālā jirṇoddhāra yāya thvateka karmma yāyata dānapati brahmacaryya- 16. bhiṣu śrī m aṇiratnajuna saṃvat 983 bhādra śudi 13 thva kunhu thache- 17. ṣelakṣetranāma bu lova 5 duntā julo bhāṣā thvate buyā āśyana thvate 18. karma yāṅāva paraśeṣa dakva dāna patiyā saṃtānana bhuktalapā du jula 19. thvate puṇyana dānapatiyā ihalokasa dharmma artha kāmanādi āyu 20. jaśa prasaṃ sukha ārogya dhana saṃtāna lādhda juyāva pratra sukhā- 21. vativāsa prāpti juya māla || maṇiratna indralakṣmī || śubhamastu sarvaṣāṃ || 22. _ dā malanaliṃ rājadatta munithakuṃ || hirālakṣmī lānimunī cijamatī ratnakumārī Provisional Translation: Salutation to venerable Rakta (red) Lokeśvara. Namaskār. Salutation to venerable Ganeśa. 9-22.  Bhikṣu Maṇiratna Vaidya and his wife Indralakṣmī, husband and wife who live in Nepal Maṇḍala in Lalitpur Mahānagara at Cyāsala Tole in Saptapuri Mahāvihāra, after originating dharmacitta (religious feeling) they have renovated this shrine of thrice venerable Ganeśa, Lord of the area, [and also] after making a golden icon of Ganeśa [and] also organizing Mangalbār Seva khalak (Tuesday Service Group of Gaṇeśa) [and] making a gold plated pinnacle, they have established [all of them in the temple] on the 4th day of the dark half of the Lunar month of Jeṣṭha in [NS] 982 (1862 CE).  And, wishing their dead son, daughter, grandson [and] granddaughters may get an abode in Sukhāvati heaven. [They] have arranged naivedya (food) to worship the deity and bhajan (recitation of the religious songs) every year on Indrajātrā in the dharmaśāla which was donated by them. In order to renovate the dharmaśālā , the donor Bhikṣu Maṇiratna has offered 5 ropanis of land named Thacheṣelaṣetra on 13th day of bright half of the lunar month of Bhadra in [NS] 983 (1863 CE). After performing such activities, the descendants of the donor may consume rest of the income (of the land). From this virtue, the donors may get dharma, fulfillment of their desires, prosperity, long life, fame, pleasure, health, money and children in this life and after this life (after their death) they may get to abode in Sukhavati, heaven. Maniratna, Indralakṣmī. May all be well. _ dā Malanasiṃ Rāj Datta, Munithakuṃ, Hiralakṣmī, Lānimunī, Cijamatī, Ratnakumārī (other family members)."@en ;
    dcterms:title "Maṇikula Phalcā (1860s CE)"@en ;
