<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/bc3c1b44-e60d-11e9-8bc4-0242ac130002> a crm:E22_Human-Made_Object,
        hg:ArchitecturalStructure,
        hg:Pati ;
    rdfs:label "Cvalcā Phalcā (1665 CE)"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "bc3c1b44-e60d-11e9-8bc4-0242ac130002" ;
    dcterms:references "Sources and references Inscription identification number LAL4007_I_001 Sources Inscription from NS 785, transcription and translation by Dr. Nutan Sharma, 2021) Details transcription from Newari (Pracalit Newari script) Oṃ śreyostu || samvat 785 | sa caitra vaddhi 12 piṃthache || jake bhā- va thaṃkāḍi yāṅa || abharāja bhāvo hākudeva bhāvo, luterāma bhāvo, lugusiṃ- ha bhāvo, jasarāma bhāvo, jayarāma bhāvo, jugarāma bhāvo, jateyā bhū- samohana, śvaku toratā, mādhava- rāma bhāvo chem hoya yāṅā, sa e- vo pithache lāche sa eva so caka śrīmat śrīśrī buṃga bhaṭṭārakāsake pūrṇamī sevā dayaka thva phale svaṃka- vala dayaka juro, thva pale sunāna ju- lasana senakarasā pañcamāhāpā- taka lāka, bhinakarasā utotra Juro ||  śubha || Translation: Oṃ. may all be well. In the dark half of the month of Caitra, in NS 785 (1665 CE), Jake Bhāvo was declared as senior-most member on the 12th day. The group of Abharāja Bhāvo, Hākudeva Bhāvo, Luterāma Bhāvo, Lugusiṃha Bhāvo, Jasarāma Bhāvo, Jayarāma Bhāvo, and Jugarāma Bhāvo made Pūrṇimā (full moon day) Sevā (serving) Group for Buṃgadyaḥ and built the phalcā in the same Pīthache (area) after leaving the same 3 bays ( kavaḥ for the phalcā) while the house of Mādhava Rāma Bhāvo was expanded. It is built facing east in Pithach ẽ L ā chi area. The norm (rule) of worshipping Buṅgadyah ̣ on the day of every full moon is established (Purn ̣ imā sevā). If anyone tries to destroy the phalcā , he/she will have to bear Pa ñ ca Mah ā P ā pa (five worst sins) where as a good-doer of it will be rewarded with happiness and prosperity. May all be well."@en ;
    dcterms:title "Cvalcā Phalcā (1665 CE)"@en ;
