<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/e6c73144-fadc-11e9-8649-0242ac130002> a crm:E22_Human-Made_Object,
        hg:ArchitecturalStructure,
        hg:Pati ;
    rdfs:label "Lũchẽ Nani Phalcā (1668 CE)"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "e6c73144-fadc-11e9-8649-0242ac130002" ;
    dcterms:references "Sources and references Sources Inscription of NS 788 (1668 CE) On Tuesday, [1] 6th day of the bright fortnight of Jyeṣṭha NS 833, Statue of Amoghapāśa Lokeśvara has been erected in the Phalcā. On Wednesday, 8th day of the bright fortnight of Bhādra NS 832, Ranhasiṃha Bhāvo, Parusiṃha Bhāvo, Lvayarāma Bhāvo, his son Ratnaki Rāma Bhāvo, Lakṣmīrāma Bhāvo, Dhanaṃsiṃha Bhāvo, Viśvarāma Bhāvo all from Jyābāhā Bahī ṭola made a Phalcā and established a guṭhī donating 1 karṣa (1/4 ropanī ) land for its management. With the income of the land every year on the 14th day of the bright fortnight of Bhādra, 1 pāthī beaten rice with 2 prastha meat, 1 kuḍa soaked pea and 1 prastha soybean should be distributed sitting in the Phalcā. [1] The date is unclear Details Dedicated to Rokyaśvara and Śaktī, Harirāma Bhāvo and his wife Dhavaṃti of the Lũchẽ Nani sponsored the construction of the phalcā to the east of Jyāthabāhāra Vihāra, completed on Saturday, the third day of the bright lunar fortnight of Vaiśākha in NS 788 (1668 CE). नेसं ७८८ वैशाख शुक्ल तृतिया, सञ्चरबार खुनु हरिराम भावो व वय्‌क:या तिरि धवंन्तिं ज्याथबाहार विहारया पूर्वय् थुगु फल्चा दय्‌का: शक्ति सहितया लोकेश्वर छम्ह नं पलिस्था या:गु जुल ।"@en ;
    dcterms:title "Lũchẽ Nani Phalcā (1668 CE)"@en ;
