<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/3f87ad30-e5d0-11e9-8bc4-0242ac130002> a crm:E22_Human-Made_Object,
        hg:ArchitecturalStructure,
        hg:Pati ;
    rdfs:label "Nārāṃhiṭī Phalcā (1750 CE)"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "3f87ad30-e5d0-11e9-8bc4-0242ac130002" ;
    dcterms:references "Sources and references Sources Inscription in southern wing Details Text and translation (by Nutan Sharma): [svasti sign] ...................................... māse śukra pakṣe...................................... kṛ- ttikā nakṣtre................................. (vaidhiriti) yo- ge.......... muhutake.............. rāśiga- te savirta || .......... raśigate candra ma- si................................................. naya ............................................pati- pa..............................................phale dvayakā (praticchā) yāṅā dina juro thva phaleyā............................. tra ya- ntā bu ro nachi ............................ sva 3 ju- ro || śubhasastu sarvadā || śubha Translation: May all be well. The phalcā has been built and established in the bright half of Lunar month of ... ... in the constellation called Kṛttikā, combination called Vaidhiriti (?) when the Sun was in ... when the Moon was in .... Two ropanis of land is offered for this phalcā. May all be well. ... constellation called Kṛttikā, combination called Vaidhiriti (?) when the Moon was in .... Two ropanis of land called Yantābu is offered for this phalcā ... ... and (also) 3. May all be well."@en ;
    dcterms:title "Nārāṃhiṭī Phalcā (1750 CE)"@en ;
