<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/673afbfc-e6f2-11e9-8bc4-0242ac130002> a crm:E22_Human-Made_Object,
        hg:ArchitecturalStructure,
        hg:Pati,
        hg:Sattal ;
    rdfs:label "Bhindyaḥ Phalcā (1751 CE)"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "673afbfc-e6f2-11e9-8bc4-0242ac130002" ;
    dcterms:references "Sources and references Inscription identification number LAL4139_I_001 Sources Stone inscription attached to the western wall of the phalcā. Details Transliteration of the stone inscription of Bhindyaḥlāchi Capāḥ Phalcā (transcribed by Nutan Sharma , 2018) [Svasti sign] śrī bhīmasenāya namaḥ || mārggāṇāṃ vighnahantāraṃ dāṇuvāraṃ siromaṇi || Kauravāḥ māra saṃhārā- rtamvande draupadipriyaṃ || svasti || samvatsara 871 phālguṇa māse śukla pakṣe || tṛtīyāyāṃntithau utatra bhādra pra revatī nakṣetre || śubha varaśika yoge tetilagaraṇe | yathā mūharttake || ādi- tavāsare || kumbha rāśigate savitari|| mīnarāśigate candramasi || tasmindine śrī matchri śrībhīmase- na pritina nhapā dasya cogva phale jīrṇa juyāva coṅasa bauddhagītakṛta dhamma dyakā guru thāpanā dhuṅā _ _ kula bhāro, lakṣmīsiṃha bhāvo, kajhita khapiṃche nāyhiti phusa gṛha prajāpati gyānasiṃha prajāpati bhā- gīrathasiṃ bhāvo sisiṃha prajāpati sūryyasiṃha prajāpati mukundasiṃha prajāpati dhantasiṃha prajā- pati bidhusiṃha prajāpati anantasiṃha prajāpati dhanaśaṃkara prajāpati puna dharmasiṃha prajāpa- ti masiṃ prajāptī dhamarā prajāptī aṣchi prajaptī kajitayā bhāryyā sūryyalakṣmīmayi bhitri thavte smuhana thva pata- kvalāchisa thva śata dayakaṃ pratiṣṭhā [yā]ṅā drinna juro || puna bhākhā sa eva gyānasiṃha pramukhana jimanhasamha samuhana mohora ṭaṃkā ṣuyacyā 68 dantā thva dānayā kalatrana śrībuṃgayātayā raṃgana yāta ṅhāva kunhu thva satarasa cāṃgva depva pujāyāsya phaṃ 1 siyāvaji phaṃ 2 ajithvaṃ dhaṃ 12 rābu 1 chāta thvateyā cettayāta dānabisyaṃ pra 2 ceknayā mata choke māra bhūya indrajātrā lhugla yāta kunu deva pūjā dana biya mata chvayeke nejyātasaṃ utiṃ yāya māra juro | thvateyā cittāyāka sa- eva gyānasiṃha ādina jimanhasa mha samuhasa avichinna yāsyaṃ cintā yāya  [mā]ra || puna bhākhā thva śatana phale suṃ jogi dopa phogiṃ taya madu gomhanaṃ tavasā paṃñca mahāpātaka rā- ka juro || || śrī 3 bhīmasenaya kudṛṣti rāka juro || śubhamastu || : || māra deva citāka juro (On top of the inscription is a small statue of Lord Buddha) Provisional Translation: Salutations to the venerable Bhīmasena, remover of obstacles, the jewel of head (ornament). Salutations to him who killed the Kauravas and who is Draupadī's beloved one. May all be well. In the year of (NS) 871 (1751 CE), on the third day of bright fortnight of Phālguna, on the constellation of Uttara Bhādra and Revati, subha-yoga , Teliya Karaṇa, Sunday when the sun is in Aquarius and the moon in Pisces. On this day, the decayed rest house which was built in devotion to Bhīmasen was renovated as a sataḥ by the group of Kula Bhāro, Lakṣmīsiṃha Bhāro, Gyānasiṃha Prajāpati who is the senior member lives near Khapinche, Nayhiti, Prajāpati Bhāgīrathasiṃ Bhāvo, Sisiṃha Prajāpati, Sūryyasiṃha Prajāpati, Mukundasiṃha Prajāpati, Dhantasiṃha Prajāpati, Bidhusiṃha Prajāpati, Anantasiṃha Prajāpati, Dhanaśaṃkara Prajāpati, Dharmasiṃha Prajāpati, Masiṃ Prajāpati, Dhamarā Prajāpati, Aṣchi Prajāpati, Sūryyalakṣmīmayi who is the wife of senior member after establishing the Caryā Guṭhī and a guru (in it). Again, the same group of 17 persons led by Gyānasiṃha Prajāpati offers 68 mohor coins to worship the deities of the phalcā by making a dāna of burning wick lamp with four mānās of oil during the festivals of Indrajātrā and Rāto (red) Matsyendranātha Lagana-jātrā after offering 1 pāthī (?), puffed rice 2 pāthī , 12 daṃ of rice beer and one type of meat. For both, the same amount (of offering) shall be made. The responsible persons are the same group of 17 persons led by Gyānasiṃha Prajāpati. Again, it is not allowed to give shelter to a jogī (Kapālī), dopa (do͂) and phogiṃ (begger) in the phale . If allowed by anybody, he shall get five kinds of great sin (killing a woman, brahman, cow etc.) and shall bear the anger of the three times venerable Bhīmasen. May all be well."@en ;
    dcterms:title "Bhindyaḥ Phalcā (1751 CE)"@en ;
