<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/befb8373-194a-4bc4-9fa5-7a736ab73196> a crm:E22_Human-Made_Object,
        hg:ArchitecturalStructure,
        hg:DhungeDhara ;
    rdfs:label "Lāykū Lũ Hiti (1688 CE)"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "befb8373-194a-4bc4-9fa5-7a736ab73196" ;
    dcterms:references "Sources and references Inscription identification number BKT0720_I_001 Sources The inscription related to the construction of the Hiti consists of three sections. The first section is engraved on a gilded plate situated below the five gavākṣas (arched niches) above the Hiti. The second section is carved on the northern side of the spout, while the third section is on the southern side of the spout. Inscription from NS 808 on the gilded plate below the five niches: H 1.5 cm, W 91 cm. Inscription on the northern part of the spout: H 2.2 cm, W 37 cm. Inscription on the southern part of the spout: H 2.2 cm, W 37 cm. Vaidya & Shrestha 2002, p. 200; P. Śreṣṭha VS 2080, pp. 745-746."@en ;
    dcterms:title "Lāykū Lũ Hiti (1688 CE)"@en ;
