    rdfs:label "Triliṅgeśvara Mahādeva Mandira (16th cent. CE)"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "b66fa304-e68d-11e9-b125-0242ac130002" ;
    dcterms:references "Sources and references Inscription identification number LAL0250_I_001 Sources This stone inscription by King Vasanta Deva (r. 506-532) stands against the plinth on the northwest corner of the temple. It was first published in the \"Abhilekha Saṃgraha, part- 5 by Itihāsa Saṃśodhana Maṇḍala. It was also published by Vajracharya (VS 2030,112). According to Dhanavajra Vajracharya, the upper part of the inscription was found damaged and the lower half was buried. size of stone stele: H: 56 cm, W: 60 cm size of inscrition fragment on the left: H: 12 cm, W: 10 cm"@en ;
    dcterms:title "Triliṅgeśvara Mahādeva Mandira (16th cent. CE)"@en ;
