<https://data.cairnepal.org/heritage/resource/monument/a9dcf214-13cc-4b71-8b0c-488ff996713b> a crm:E22_Human-Made_Object,
        hg:ArchitecturalStructure,
        hg:BuddhistMonument ;
    rdfs:label "Cīdhaṃ Bāhāḥ (built in 1539 CE)"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "a9dcf214-13cc-4b71-8b0c-488ff996713b" ;
    dcterms:references "Sources and references Sources Stone inscription from NS 800 attached to the western side of the entrance to the sanctum The entrance to the sanctum has two inscriptions flanking it, with the western one being the first portion and the eastern one having the remaining portion. The inscription on the western side records the construction of the bāhāḥ . It is worth noting that one of the members of the bāhāḥ prohibited photographing the first portion of the inscription. See, S. Śākyabhikṣu NS 1131, pp.35-36; S. Bhaṭṭarāī VS 2068, p.25"@en ;
